Cuaderno_2013_1_E	74	answer	0	Start light exercise (walking) one week after the intervention.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	74	answer	1	Shower or bathe after 1 or 2 days.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	74	answer	2	Return to sexual activity when desired.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	74	answer	3	If you had fat intolerance before the operation, gradually add fat to your usual diet in small increments.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	74	answer	4	Resume the normal diet.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	75	question	-	A patient with dyspepsia will undergo a screening test for Helicobacter pylori. Before carrying out the test, the patient should know that:
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	75	answer	0	Treatment with proton pump inhibitors should be discontinued at least one week before the test.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	75	answer	1	Treatment with proton pump inhibitors should be discontinued at least two weeks before the test.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	75	answer	2	The use of antacids also modifies the results of the test.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	75	answer	3	The use of antibiotics does not modify the diagnostic tests for H. pylori.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	75	answer	4	Antibiotic treatments negativize the diagnostic tests for H. pylori, so these drugs should be avoided for one week before any diagnostic test.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	76	question	-	In general, water intake should be increased in patients undergoing chemotherapy with the aim of:
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	76	answer	0	Prevent kidney damage.
Cuaderno_2013_1_E	76	answer	1	Fluidify bronchial secretions.
