Cuaderno_2013_1_M	67	answer	3	Replacement of the aortic valve by a homograft.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	67	answer	4	Implantation of a percutaneous valve.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	68	question	-	When it comes to pericardial tamponade, which of the following statements is NOT correct?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	68	answer	0	Chest radiography is very useful for diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	68	answer	1	The jugular venous registry allows to objectify a very deep collapse.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	68	answer	2	The presence of a paradoxical arterial pulse is common.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	68	answer	3	Right atrial collapse is very sensitive for diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	68	answer	4	Right ventricular collapse is very specific for diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	69	question	-	The following patients are sent to the hypertension clinic. Indicate which one you would NOT suspect secondary hypertension.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	69	answer	0	25 year old woman with an abdominal puff.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	69	answer	1	Hypertension with hypokalemia in a 50-year-old man who does not take drugs.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	69	answer	2	A 55-year-old woman with a body mass index of 28 and dyslipidemia.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	69	answer	3	A 78-year-old woman who has not been controlled with 3 drugs for 3 months.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	69	answer	4	Man of 60 years with daytime sleepiness, morning headache and snoring.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	70	question	-	In the treatment of heart failure:
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	70	answer	0	Angiotensin receptor blockers (ARA II) have shown superiority over angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors and should be the first therapeutic option.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	70	answer	1	Aldosterone antagonists have not shown prognostic improvement, being contraindicated in patients with advanced systolic dysfunction and functional grade IV.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	70	answer	2	Beta-blockers have been shown to decrease mortality in patients with decreased ejection fraction.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	70	answer	3	Cardiac resynchronization pacemaker therapy is indicated in patients with systolic dysfunction whenever the QRS is narrow (less than 120 msg).
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	70	answer	4	The implantation of automatic defibrillators is contraindicated in patients with ventricular dysfunction, especially if it is caused by ischemia.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	71	question	-	In a patient with symptoms of heart failure who have a disproportionately high ascites in relation to peripheral edema, the most likely etiology would be:
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	71	answer	0	A severe aortic stenosis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	71	answer	1	A dilated cardiomyopathy with significant left ventricular dysfunction.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	71	answer	2	A primary pulmonary hypertension.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	71	answer	3	An obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	71	answer	4	A constrictive pericarditis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	72	question	-	Point out the FALSE afimation with respect to the cardiac "third noise":
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	72	answer	0	It is a low frequency sound.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	72	answer	1	It can occur in processes that increase the velocity or ventricular filling volume.
