Cuaderno_2013_1_M	81	answer	3	Evaluate the response to a gluten-free diet.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	81	answer	4	Colonoscopy
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	82	question	-	A 37-year-old woman with an extensive ulcerative colitis has a severe outbreak where treatment with prednisone is started at a dose of 1 mg / kg. After a week of treatment, the patient does not show improvement. What is the next therapeutic measure to perform?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	82	answer	0	Subtotal colectomy of urgency and in a second time proctectomy and ileoanal reservoir.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	82	answer	1	Associate an immunosuppressant such as azathioprine.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	82	answer	2	Associate mesalazine in doses of 4 grams per day oral and rectal triamcinolone 1 application every 12 hours
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	82	answer	3	Endovenous cyclosporine 2 mg / Kg.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	82	answer	4	Treatment with etanercept (an anti-TNFa antibody) should be assessed.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	83	question	-	In a liver transplant patient who is receiving immunosuppression with tacrolimus, which of the following antibiotics markedly increases the levels of the immunosuppressant and should therefore be avoided?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	83	answer	0	Amoxicillin clavulanic.
