Cuaderno_2013_1_M	86	answer	4	Pelvic MRI.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	87	question	-	A patient goes to a hospital emergency department presenting frank hematemesis. In the initial assessment the patient is pale and sweaty, has a heart rate of 110 beats per minute and a systolic blood pressure of 98 mmHg. Which of the following actions would NOT be performed in the initial care of this patient?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	87	answer	0	Ensure adequate oxygenation of the patient.
