Cuaderno_2013_1_M	120	answer	4	Chest x-ray.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	121	question	-	Except in patients whose chronic renal failure is due to diabetic nephropathy or tubulointerstitial nephropathy, the arterial blood gas pattern that you would expect to find in a patient with chronic renal failure would be:
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	121	answer	0	pH 7.30, HCO3 18 mEq / L, Cl 116 mg / dL, because metabolic acidosis with normal anion gap is characteristic.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	121	answer	1	pH 7.46, HCO3 18 mEq / L, Cl 116 mg / dL, because hyperchloremic metabolic alkalosis is characteristic.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	121	answer	2	pH 7.456, HCO3 18 mEq / L, Cl 100 mg / dL, because metabolic acidosis with increased anion gap is characteristic.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	121	answer	3	pH 7.46, HCO3 30 mEq / L, Cl 90 mg / dL, because metabolic alkalosis with normal anion gap is characteristic.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	121	answer	4	pH 7.45, HCO3 23 mEq / L, Cl 100 mg / dL, because metabolic alkalosis with normal anion gap is characteristic.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	122	question	-	Regarding the definition of chronic kidney disease, one is INCORRECT:
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	122	answer	0	It requires persistent presence of structural or functional alterations of the kidney for at least 2 months.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	122	answer	1	It includes alterations in urine as proteinuria, independently of the glomerular filtration rate (GFR).
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	122	answer	2	It includes a lower GFR of 60 ml / min / 1.73m2 of body surface regardless of the presence or absence of other markers of kidney damage.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	122	answer	3	It is classified into 5 stages according to the TFG.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	122	answer	4	The preparation for renal replacement therapy should be done in stage 4.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	123	question	-	A 38-year-old man consulted for dyspnea and hemoptysis. Blood tests have creatinine 7 mg / dl, urea 250 mg / dl and anti-MBG (anti-glomerular basement membrane antibodies) positive high titer. A renal biopsy was performed, showing crescents in 75% of the glomeruli, and in the immunofluorescence a linear Ig deposition pattern appeared. Which of the following is the correct answer?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	123	answer	0	It is an Ig A Nephropathy with acute renal failure.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	123	answer	1	The performance of plasmapheresis would be indicated.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	123	answer	2	It is a membranous glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	123	answer	3	Mycophenolate mofetil is the initial treatment of choice.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	123	answer	4	Glomerular involvement is caused by the presence of circulating immune complexes.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	124	question	-	In a renal transplant patient, which of the following characteristics is the characteristic of acute renal rejection?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	124	answer	0	Interstitial infiltrate of B lymphocytes.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	124	answer	1	Preferably infiltrated with T lymphocytes in the renal interstitium and in the renal tubules.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	124	answer	2	Fibrosis and tubular atrophy.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	124	answer	3	Proliferative glomerulonephritis without affecting the interstitium.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	124	answer	4	Presence of circulating antidonant antibodies and renal infarcts.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	125	question	-	Regarding benign prostatic hypertrophy, it is NOT true that:
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	125	answer	0	Abdominal ultrasound is a non-invasive method to assess prostate size and post-voiding residual.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	125	answer	1	It can cause increases in PSA levels.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	125	answer	2	Rectal examination is a method to estimate prostate size.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	125	answer	3	Treatment with 5-alpha reductase inhibitors decreases symptoms.
