Cuaderno_2013_1_M	127	question	-	Before a 49-year-old man, asymptomatic, with a family history of a father who died of prostate cancer, a PSA (Specific Prostate Antigen) of 5.9 ng / ml was identified in a routine company control, with a PSA ratio free / Total PSA of 11% and that in a digital rectal examination there is an increase in consistency in the right prostatic lobe, what is the following clinical indication?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	127	answer	0	Ask the patient to perform a transrectal ultrasound and prostate biopsy.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	127	answer	1	Perform a abdominopelvic CT scan.
