Cuaderno_2013_1_M	150	answer	1	Assess absolute risk of fracture using the FRAX questionnaire without BMD and treat only if it is high.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	150	answer	2	Start treatment with bisphosphonates and vitamin D (800 IU / day).
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	150	answer	3	Administer calcium supplement (1g) and vitamin D (800 IU / day).
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	150	answer	4	Assess if you have osteopenia on the radiographs and treat if it is present.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	151	question	-	The diagnosis of sarcoidosis is based on:
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	151	answer	0	Clinical-radiological compatible picture and presence of non-caseating granulomas in one or more organs, with negative cultures of mycobacteria and fungi.
