Cuaderno_2013_1_M	182	answer	3	Td, tetravalent, pneumococcal meningitis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	182	answer	4	Viral triple, seasonal flu, pneumococcal.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	183	question	-	In order to check the efficacy of a treatment to stop smoking, a control group (placebo) is compared with a treated group. For groups to be comparable it is important that they do not differ much in the age of the participants. We are informed that the average age in the control group is 52 years and that in the treated group it is also 52 years. From this information we can say that:
