Cuaderno_2013_1_M	183	answer	1	If the study is well designed, it can not give us the same average age in both groups.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	183	answer	2	To compare the distribution of the age variable in both groups, it would be convenient to know a measure of dispersion as the standard deviation in addition to the mean.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	183	answer	3	For the final conclusion it does not matter the distribution of age in both groups, only if the treatment is effective or not.
