Cuaderno_2013_1_M	203	answer	3	Epstein Barr virus.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	203	answer	4	Cytomegalovirus.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	204	question	-	A 25-year-old woman with no history of interest or toxic habits who went to the emergency room due to severe pain in her right ear, total inability to open her mouth, sudden onset and no previous history of trauma. It refers to the use of a discharge plate due to a nighttime dental clenching habit. What is your diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	204	answer	0	Dislocation of the mandibular condyle in front of the joint eminence.
