Cuaderno_2013_1_M	221	answer	3	Infectious arthritis due to mycobacteria.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	221	answer	4	Rheumatoid arthritis.
Cuaderno_2013_1_M	222	question	-	A 29-year-old woman, obese, with no history of interest, who consulted for a bilateral, intense, pulsatile headache lasting one month, accompanied by horizontal diplopia and episodes of monocular amaurosis of seconds duration. The exploration is normal, except for the presence of bilateral papilledema. Which of these tests do you think will allow you to fully confirm your diagnosis ?:
