Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	43	question	-	Gas chromatography combined with mass spectrometry (GC-MS) is the most commonly used chromatographic coupled technique. The main difficulty of the coupling is in:
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	43	answer	0	The analysis of molecular ions in the same place where they are generated.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	43	answer	1	The production of highly fragmented ions with accelerated electron generation.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	43	answer	2	The increase in the output flow rate of the chromatograph, which can not exceed nL / min.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	43	answer	3	The obtaining of the bidimensional spectrum that allows the separation in function of the relationship q / r.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	43	answer	4	The introduction into the high vacuum of the mass analyzer, of a compound that is at an atomospheric pressure.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	44	question	-	For the analysis of traces of inorganic constituents, in samples of organic nature, a preliminary treatment of the sample is needed, which normally consists of:
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	44	answer	0	Dissolve the sample in cold water.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	44	answer	1	Dissolve the sample in hot water.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	44	answer	2	Dissolve the sample between 30 and 70 ºC.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	44	answer	3	Heat the sample between 400 and 700 ºC.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	44	answer	4	Heat the sample in 0.1 M hydrochloric acid.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	45	question	-	Linear sweep voltammetry is characterized by:
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	45	answer	0	To be a technique based on a stationary diffusion regime.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	45	answer	1	To be a voltammetric technique based on a pure diffusion regime.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	45	answer	2	Use a rotating electrode as working electrode.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	45	answer	3	Use a hanging drop electrode as the working electrode.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	45	answer	4	Have an electrode preconcentration stage.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	46	question	-	In suppression ion chromatography:
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	46	answer	0	A single column is used and the conductivity of the mobile phase is kept very low.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	46	answer	1	The eluent must be able to be removed selectively after separation and prior to the conductometric measurement.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	46	answer	2	The eluent incorporates a regenerating solution of strong acid flowing in the same direction as the mobile phase.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	46	answer	3	Weak exchangers are used from polystyrene polymers.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	46	answer	4	A mobile phase with ionic conductivity gradient is used.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	47	question	-	Voltammetry of anodic redissolution:
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	47	answer	0	It is always carried out with mercury film electrodes.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	47	answer	1	It uses an oxidation process with chemical agents.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	47	answer	2	It is based on the formation of mercury salts in the electrode.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	47	answer	3	It does not need background electrolyte.
Cuaderno_2013_1_Q	47	answer	4	It has an electrodeposition stage.
