Cuaderno_2014_1_E	122	answer	1	Advice and information.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	122	answer	2	Education for individual health.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	122	answer	3	Education for group health.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	122	answer	4	Education for massive health.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	123	question	-	A program of Health Education (EpS) is organized for women in the climacteric stage. One of the sessions aims to know how they are living this stage and how it is affecting them personally and family. The most appropriate EpS technique is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	123	answer	0	Grating.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	123	answer	1	Brainstorming.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	123	answer	2	Phillips 6/6.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	123	answer	3	Fotopalabra
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	123	answer	4	All are adequate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	124	question	-	The Program of Preventive Activities and Health Promotion (PAPPS) DOES NOT include as a minimum package in the Infant Subprogram:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	124	answer	0	Screening for congenital hypothyroidism.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	124	answer	1	Promotion of breastfeeding.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	124	answer	2	Prevention of pregnancy and sexually transmitted diseases in adolescents.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	124	answer	3	Prevention of suicide.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	124	answer	4	Prevention of active and passive smoking.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	125	question	-	In the control of chronic diseases that require continuous treatment, one of the main challenges for the primary care nurse is to favor adherence to pharmacological treatment and to make recommendations related to lifestyles. Of the following recommendations, which would NOT be indicated to encourage such adhesion ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	125	answer	0	Provide clear advice on the benefits and possible adverse effects of the treatment and on the posology and its duration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	125	answer	1	Take into account the habits and preferences of the patient.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	125	answer	2	Use standardized diets and exercise charts that reduce monitoring.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	125	answer	3	Establish a therapeutic relationship based on the motivational interview.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	125	answer	4	Offer multiple or combined sessions of behavioral interventions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	126	question	-	A 45-year-old man of Moroccan origin, who arrived in Spain three years ago, goes to the nurse's office, with a clean superficial wound, and tells us that six months after arrival he was given a dose of the diphtheriate bath vaccine. Of the following interventions, which is indicated ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	126	answer	0	Start diphtheria tetanus vaccination.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	126	answer	1	Administration of the 2nd dose of tetanus diphtheria.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	126	answer	2	Administration of antitetanus gammaglobulin.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	126	answer	3	Administration of antitetanic gamma globulin and 2nd dose of diphtheria tetanus.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	126	answer	4	No intervention would be indicated since he has a dose of diphtheria tetanus.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	127	question	-	P.C. is a 27-year-old woman who was given the first dose of the HBV vaccine 3 weeks ago. He has just been given the results of the serological markers of rubella: Ac anti rubella negative. Taking into account the vaccination situation, what intervention is adequate ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	127	answer	0	Vaccinate the triple viral and the 2nd dose of HBV, at the time of consultation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	127	answer	1	Vaccinate the triple virus at the time of consultation and wait a week for the administration of the 2nd dose of the HBV vaccine.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	127	answer	2	Vaccinate the 2nd dose of the HBV vaccine at the time of the consultation and wait a week for the administration of the triple virus.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	127	answer	3	Vaccinate from the 2nd dose of the HBV vaccine at the time of consultation, and do not vaccinate from the triple virus since it is immunized.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	127	answer	4	Do not vaccinate for the anti-rubella ACs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	128	question	-	A 38-year-old man comes to the nursing consultation and says he has maintained risky sexual practices with a source + HBV. The result of the serology performed is HBsAc> 10mUl / ml. Taking into account the data provided, what intervention is indicated ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	128	answer	0	Immediate administration of the lgHB, initiate HBV vaccination and EpS of safe sex practices.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	128	answer	1	Only immediate administration of the lgHB and EpS of safe sex practices.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	128	answer	2	Put HBV and EpS recall doses of safe sex practices.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	128	answer	3	Start vaccination and EpS of safe sex practices.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	128	answer	4	EpS of safe sex practices.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	129	question	-	Within the direct care functions developed by the Primary Care Teams is NOT:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	129	answer	0	Promotion of healthy lifestyles.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	129	answer	1	Secondary prevention of more prevalent problems in the community.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	129	answer	2	Preparation and implementation of health education projects in school environments.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	129	answer	3	Undergraduate and postgraduate training of health personnel.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	129	answer	4	Rehabilitation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	130	question	-	The recommended secondary prevention measure for the prevention of cervical cancer is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	130	answer	0	Vaccine against HPV.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	130	answer	1	Promote the use of condoms.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	130	answer	2	Substitute treatment of estrogen and progesterone in postmenopausal women.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	130	answer	3	Performing cervical cytology for women between 25 and 65 years
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	130	answer	4	All are recommendations for secondary prevention.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	131	question	-	An essential aspect that should be included in the assessment of a smoker is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	131	answer	0	Degree of dependency.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	131	answer	1	Stage of the change process.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	131	answer	2	Degree of motivation
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	131	answer	3	Supports and difficulties.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	131	answer	4	All are correct.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	132	question	-	According to the Strategy of the National Drug Plan (2009-2016), among the population groups that benefit from programs and activities aimed at social assistance and integration, there are NO people who:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	132	answer	0	They consume drugs and they go to the general health network for problems related to their consumption or other health problems.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	132	answer	1	They frequent environments and participate in situations where there is a special facility for consumption.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	132	answer	2	They are affected by dual pathology, they present complicated comorbid conditions that become chronic and worsen the evolution and prognosis of the addictive problem.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	132	answer	3	They are interned in prisons or following alternative programs to the enforcement of prison sentences.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	132	answer	4	They are minors and drug users, inmates in protection or reform centers.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	133	question	-	What type of primary prevention intervention is indicated during the pre-pathogenic period of cardiovascular diseases ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	133	answer	0	Carry out the assessment of cardiovascular risk using the SCORE scale from adolescence.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	133	answer	1	Control of total cholesterol levels periodically based on age.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	133	answer	2	Blood pressure control periodically based on age.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	133	answer	3	Promotion of healthy lifestyles: tobacco consumption, diet and exercise mainly.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	133	answer	4	All measurements are indicated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	134	question	-	What measure defines the frequency of lung cancer among people who smoke 20 cigarettes a day compared to those who do not smoke ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	134	answer	0	Accumulated incidence.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	134	answer	1	Incidence density.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	134	answer	2	Relative risk.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	134	answer	3	Attributable risk.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	134	answer	4	Etiological risk fraction.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	135	question	-	Of the following variables, which is considered a risk marker in the onset of cardiovascular disease:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	135	answer	0	Elevated figures of LDL-cholesterol and total cholesterol.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	135	answer	1	Man over 55 years old.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	135	answer	2	Smoker of 20 cigarettes daily.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	135	answer	3	Sedentary.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	135	answer	4	All are correct.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	136	question	-	Dengue is an infectious disease endemic in certain communities. When 38% of the population of a community has said disease, we talk about:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	136	answer	0	Holoendemia
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	136	answer	1	Hyperendemia
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	136	answer	2	Mesoendemia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	136	answer	3	Hypoendemia
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	136	answer	4	Pandemic.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	137	question	-	Taking into account the WHO classification of methods and means of education for health, campaigns to prevent traffic accidents carried out on television are considered a method:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	137	answer	0	Indirect and visual
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	137	answer	1	Direct and visual
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	137	answer	2	Indirect and audiovisual.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	137	answer	3	Mixed.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	137	answer	4	Mixed, sound, visual and audiovisual.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	138	question	-	According to the article 15 of the Law of Prevention of Labor Risks, it is NOT considered a principle in the preventive activity:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	138	answer	0	Avoid the risks and fight them from their origin.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	138	answer	1	Adapt the job to the person.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	138	answer	2	Adopt measures that put individual protection before collective protection.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	138	answer	3	Substitute the dangerous for what it means little or no danger.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	138	answer	4	Training of workers
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	139	question	-	The least effective prevention measure in the appearance of an outbreak of salmonellosis is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	139	answer	0	Active immunization to the population at risk.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	139	answer	1	Rigorous and frequent hand washing, as well as utensils and surfaces that will be used for cooking.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	139	answer	2	Keep food in the refrigerator.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	139	answer	3	Cook food with sufficient temperature (at least 70ºC).
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	139	answer	4	Quick refrigeration of cooked foods.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	140	question	-	In the health diagnosis of a community, if the objective is to know how the environment influences the community, the indicator that must be included in the analysis is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	140	answer	0	Unemployment rate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	140	answer	1	Geographic characteristics.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	140	answer	2	General structure of the population.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	140	answer	3	Fertility rate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	140	answer	4	Population correctly vaccinated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	141	question	-	Point out the INCORRECT response in relation to the Portfolio of Primary Care Services:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	141	answer	0	It is the selection of services prioritized and organized in a specific way, which responds exclusively to health policy priorities.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	141	answer	1	The basic unit of the Portfolio of Services is a set of activities or action criteria that guide the attention to a problem or process of clinical or preventive health with specification of the population to which it is directed.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	141	answer	2	The general structure may have variants depending on the service in question or the different Autonomous Communities.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	141	answer	3	Its purpose is to promote the attention of the most frequent and relevant processes in PA in accordance with agreed scientific and technical criteria.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	141	answer	4	It reduces the avoidable clinical variability and facilitates equity in the provision of services.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	142	question	-	Among the sources used to make the diagnosis of health of a community, it is essential to know:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	142	answer	0	Census of the population.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	142	answer	1	Notifiable diseases registration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	142	answer	2	Potable water supply.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	142	answer	3	Waiting lists.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	142	answer	4	All are correct.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	143	question	-	The quotient between the number of live births registered in a year and the female population of reproductive age (15-49 years) refers to the concept of:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	143	answer	0	Crude birth rate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	143	answer	1	General fertility rate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	143	answer	2	Synthetic fertility index.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	143	answer	3	Gross reproduction rate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	143	answer	4	Net reproduction rate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	144	question	-	If in an epidemiological study, the participating population has voluntariness as an inclusion criterion, the validity of the results are subject to a bias of:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	144	answer	0	Information.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	144	answer	1	Confusion.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	144	answer	2	Selection.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	144	answer	3	Interpretation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	144	answer	4	Publication.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	145	question	-	A 55-year-old man came to the nursing consultation for follow-up of newly diagnosed hypertension. In the assessment he says that he smokes 15 cigars a day. Taking advantage of the opportunity of the consultation, the nurse provides information on the importance of quitting smoking and offers support if you decide to quit. This type of EpS intervention is considered:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	145	answer	0	Advice / Information.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	145	answer	1	Individual attention
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	145	answer	2	Health promotion.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	145	answer	3	EpS sued.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	145	answer	4	All are correct.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	146	question	-	According to article 56 of the General Health Law of 1986, "the structure responsible for the unitary management of health centers, benefits and programs to be developed in their territorial demarcation" is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	146	answer	0	Comprehensive specialized care center.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	146	answer	1	Clinic.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	146	answer	2	Basic Health Area.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	146	answer	3	Primary Care Team.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	146	answer	4	Health area.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	147	question	-	Among the epidemiological criteria of causality defined by Bradford Hill (1965) is NOT:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	147	answer	0	Strength of association.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	147	answer	1	Temporal sequence.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	147	answer	2	Biological gradient
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	147	answer	3	Cessation or reversibility effect.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	147	answer	4	Presence of alternative explanations.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	148	question	-	The results of the evaluation of a prevention program carried out in a specific context, environment and population refer to the concept of:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	148	answer	0	Effectiveness.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	148	answer	1	Efficiency.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	148	answer	2	Effectiveness.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	148	answer	3	Feasibility.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	148	answer	4	Sustainability
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	149	question	-	The demographic dynamics of a community is determined by:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	149	answer	0	Natality
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	149	answer	1	Mortality.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	149	answer	2	Immigration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	149	answer	3	Emigration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	149	answer	4	All are correct.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	150	question	-	It is NOT considered a tertiary prevention intervention in a situation of mistreatment of women:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	150	answer	0	Perform a periodic and systematic assessment of the indicators of abuse risk.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	150	answer	1	Perform a comprehensive physical assessment (injuries produced), psychological (emotional state) and social (social support networks).
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	150	answer	2	If there is an immediate life risk, an urgent transfer to the hospital or to the guardhouse will be necessary.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	150	answer	3	Contact and inform the pediatrician if the woman has children, both because of the potential risk (when witnessing the abuse) and the possibility of being victims of it.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	150	answer	4	Inform of the legal steps.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	151	question	-	Which of the following manifestations is an emergency for the pregnant woman ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	151	answer	0	Appearance of varicose veins
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	151	answer	1	Leucorrhea
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	151	answer	2	Polaquiuria.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	151	answer	3	Intense headache
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	151	answer	4	Sickness.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	152	question	-	C. S. who is 40 weeks pregnant and gets rubella, consult with the nurse your doubts about whether you can breastfeed the newborn. What will be the response of the nurse ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	152	answer	0	It is totally contraindicated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	152	answer	1	The disease is compatible and also vaccination with breastfeeding.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	152	answer	2	You must wait until the baby is 15 days old.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	152	answer	3	It depends on the viral load.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	152	answer	4	Breastfeeding will begin 3 days after putting the gammaglobulin to the baby.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	153	question	-	Between 24 and 36 hours after the peak of release of the hormone LH occurs, it is triggered:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	153	answer	0	The menstruation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	153	answer	1	Maturation of the Graaf follicle.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	153	answer	2	The ovulation
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	153	answer	3	Oogenesis
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	153	answer	4	The formation of the primordial follicle.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	154	question	-	In the Pap test, cytological samples should be collected from:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	154	answer	0	The vulva, the cervix and the inside of the uterine cavity.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	154	answer	1	The vaginal walls and the uterine fundus.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	154	answer	2	The inside of the cervix, the external cervical os and the posterior vaginal sac.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	154	answer	3	The vaginal introitus and the ectocervix.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	154	answer	4	The endocervix and the lateral vaginal sacs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	155	question	-	Due to its high mercury content, the Spanish Agency for Food Safety and Nutrition recommends pregnant women not to consume:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	155	answer	0	Mature soft cheeses, type Brie or Camembert.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	155	answer	1	Pate or foie gras.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	155	answer	2	Large fatty fish.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	155	answer	3	Raw sausages
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	155	answer	4	Green leaf vegetables.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	156	question	-	The effect of anti-D gammaglobulin given to Rh negative women who have developed an Rh positive fetus is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	156	answer	0	Eliminate fetal red blood cells from maternal blood.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	156	answer	1	Destroy the antigens formed by the mother's immune system.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	156	answer	2	Avoid the formation of anti-Rh negative antibodies.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	156	answer	3	Induce the formation of maternal antibodies against fetal antigen.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	156	answer	4	Provide the woman with permanent active immunity.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	157	question	-	In a woman with hyperemesis gravidarum, the appearance of:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	157	answer	0	Convulsive crisis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	157	answer	1	Hyperglycemia
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	157	answer	2	Dehydration
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	157	answer	3	Abruptio placentae
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	157	answer	4	Polyuria
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	158	question	-	For the care of the nipple cracks during lactation it is recommended:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	158	answer	0	Washed with water and neutral pH soap after each feeding.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	158	answer	1	Spread a few drops of milk and let air dry after the tetada.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	158	answer	2	The use of healing ointments.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	158	answer	3	70º alcohol applied through sterile gauze between shots.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	158	answer	4	Apply cold between shots.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	159	question	-	In relation to toxoplasmosis and pregnancy, indicate which of the following options is true:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	159	answer	0	Placental transmission to the fetus can occur.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	159	answer	1	The rate of antibodies should be detected at the beginning of pregnancy and, in their absence, vaccination with killed virus vaccine should be carried out.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	159	answer	2	The infection is less severe but more frequent the younger the pregnant woman is.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	159	answer	3	In our environment, the main cause of infection is the coexistence and management of domestic birds.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	159	answer	4	The infection occurs intrapartum, favored by the rupture of the amniotic sac.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	160	question	-	A child with gluten intolerance asks the nurse what trinkets she can take when she goes out to play with her friends:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	160	answer	0	Snacks
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	160	answer	1	Chocolates
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	160	answer	2	Popcorn.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	160	answer	3	Pastries
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	160	answer	4	Candies.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	161	question	-	Regarding the exploration of psychomotor development, the area of ​​language and sociability in a four-year-old child, which of the following findings can be considered a sign of alarm in the maturation process ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	161	answer	0	Abrupt stop of the acquisition of skills or loss of some already acquired.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	161	answer	1	Hyperactivity He does not know how to entertain himself, he needs constant vigilance.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	161	answer	2	Excessive sociability; he goes with anyone indiscriminately.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	161	answer	3	Repeat questions instead of answering them.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	161	answer	4	All these situations are warning signs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	162	question	-	The presence of foreign bodies such as small buttons, sunflower seeds, etc., in the respiratory tract in young children is a relatively frequent accident. Point out the signs that appear when these objects are lodged in the lower respiratory tract:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	162	answer	0	Episodes of cough, hoarseness and dyspnea.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	162	answer	1	Chronic cough, hypoventilation on auscultation, signs of infection.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	162	answer	2	Asphyxia, dyspnea, cyanosis, respiratory failure.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	162	answer	3	Fever, cough and dysphonia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	162	answer	4	Tachypnea, increased respiratory effort.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	163	question	-	Of the following scales of pain assessment in childhood, which is recommended for school children aged 7 to 8 ?:
