Cuaderno_2014_1_E	170	question	-	In the health report of Mrs. P. T. of 83 years of age, it is reported that she has a depressive picture. Regarding depression in the elderly has been described that:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	170	answer	0	It is uncommon for them to have somatic symptoms.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	170	answer	1	It is not characteristic that cognitive disorders appear.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	170	answer	2	The Yesavage scale is an instrument to establish a safe diagnosis of depression.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	170	answer	3	There is unanimity in stating that it has specific manifestations in the elderly.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	170	answer	4	There may be pictures of pseudodementia, with symptoms of dementia but caused by depressive states.
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	171	question	-	Mr. T. T., 92 years old, admitted to the hospitalization unit recently, has started with different symptoms that suggest that he has an acute confusional syndrome. Within the measures of prevention and care for this problem is indicated:
Cuaderno_2014_1_E	171	answer	0	Advise the family not to stop constantly stimulating the patient.
