Cuaderno_2014_1_M	41	answer	4	Cholestasis due to drugs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	42	question	-	A 66-year-old man, previously diagnosed with liver cirrhosis of alcoholic etiology, is brought to the Emergency Department due to an increase in the abdominal perimeter and temporo-spatial disorientation. On physical examination, there is evidence of ascites and "flapping tremor" or asterixis. Which of the following explorations should be done as a matter of urgency?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	42	answer	0	A cranial computed tomography to rule out a cerebrovascular accident.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	42	answer	1	An abdominal ultrasound to confirm the presence of ascites.
