Cuaderno_2014_1_M	49	answer	1	Treat the patient as if it were an infarction with ST-segment elevation, proposing a reperfusion therapy as early as possible.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	49	answer	2	To implant a transcutaneous pacemaker before the possibility of developing a more advanced block.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	49	answer	3	Perform an urgent CT to rule out the presence of an acute pulmonary embolism.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	49	answer	4	As it could be an acute pericarditis, we will administer NSAIDs.
