Cuaderno_2014_1_M	70	question	-	A 7-year-old boy presents a subacute picture of cerebellar ataxia and intracranial hypertension. Magnetic resonance imaging demonstrates an expansive lesion in the cerebellar vérmix that captures contrast and obstructs the fourth ventricle. The most likely diagnosis is:
