Cuaderno_2014_1_M	70	answer	4	Lymphoma
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	71	question	-	Patient of 70 years with the only antecedent of being ex-alcoholic for 3 years and diagnosed with atrophic gastritis. Consultation for a 4-month evolution that began with distal and symmetrical paresthesias in the lower limbs and progressively added gait difficulty, this being impossible without help, and confusional episodes of paroxysmal presentation. On neurological examination, the cranial nerves are normal, have a slight bradypsychia, failures in deep sensation in four limbs, pseudo-dystonic attitude in the upper limbs, finger-nose dysmetria and bilateral knee heel with closed eyes, extenuated osteotendinous reflexes, bilateral Babinski and distal paresis in upper limbs. Point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	71	answer	0	Perform a blood count and determination of B12 when funicular myelosis is suspected.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	71	answer	1	Perform an MRI looking for atrophy of vermis and cerebellar foliae before the high suspicion of alcoholic cerebellar degeneration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	71	answer	2	Initially, 100 mg of intravenous thiamine should be administered because of suspicion of Wernicke-Korsakoff encephalopathy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	71	answer	3	The first thing to do would be a determination of natremia to rule out a central pontine myelinolysis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	71	answer	4	Perform an electromyographic study when there is a high suspicion of primary lateral sclerosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	72	question	-	A 52-year-old male presents with acute form a confusional syndrome, paresis of both external ocular rectus muscles and gait ataxia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	72	answer	0	Hyperglycemic encephalopathy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	72	answer	1	Korsakoff encephalopathy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	72	answer	2	Cerebellar infarction.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	72	answer	3	Administer thiamin immediately.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	72	answer	4	Lead poisoning.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	73	question	-	A 24-year-old student who, after three weeks of a cold in the upper respiratory tract, visited the doctor for a sensation of numbness in his hands and loss of limb strength in recent days. The picture was preceded by low back pain. In the exploration, it stands out, decrease of asymmetric muscular force in upper and lower extremities, loss of osteotendinous reflexes. In this patient the most likely diagnosis is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	73	answer	0	Myasthenia gravis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	73	answer	1	First outbreak of multiple sclerosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	73	answer	2	Acute inflammatory demyelinating polyradiculopathy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	73	answer	3	Dermatomyositis
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	73	answer	4	Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	74	question	-	A 68-year-old man with a history of diabetes of 20 years of evolution, hypertension and prostatism in treatment, consulted for repeated episodes of syncope. The episodes have occurred while standing, after meals and have been preceded by an oppressive pain in the nape, neck and shoulder girdle. Which of these complementary tests is essential?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	74	answer	0	Brain and cervical MRI.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	74	answer	1	Angio-MR of the supra-aortic trunks.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	74	answer	2	Nuclear medicine study of cerebral dopamine transporter (SPECT with ioflupane).
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	74	answer	3	Measurement of blood pressure in decubitus and standing.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	74	answer	4	24-hour Holter record of the electrocardiogram.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	75	question	-	Which of the following symptoms is NOT present in the Wallemberg syndrome, usually produced by ischemia of the dorsal-lateral region of the bulb?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	75	answer	0	Diffuse
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	75	answer	1	Dysphagia
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	75	answer	2	Piramidalism
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	75	answer	3	Ataxia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	75	answer	4	Horner syndrome.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	76	question	-	In relation to Hereditary Spherocytosis it is true that:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	76	answer	0	It is a congenital hemolytic anemia of inheritance linked to the X chromosome that causes severe anemia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	76	answer	1	It is characterized by a decrease in osmotic fragility.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	76	answer	2	It manifests as episodes of acute medication anemia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	76	answer	3	Splenectomy is the treatment of choice when it is symptomatic.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	76	answer	4	It is rarely associated with cholelithiasis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	77	question	-	A 45-year-old patient who went to the emergency room for general malaise, headache and progressive tiredness in recent weeks. On physical examination, a slight icteric dye of the skin and mucous membranes was detected and a 2-cm splenomegaly was felt under the costal margin. The analytical presents hemoglobin 8.6 g / dL, VCM 100 fL. The number of reticulocytes is high and anisopoikilocytosis is observed in the blood smear. In the biochemistry highlights LDH 1300 IU / L, bilirubin 2.2 mg / dL and undetectable haptoglobin. Which test is the most appropriate to guide the diagnosis of the patient?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	77	answer	0	Fecal occult blood test.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	77	answer	1	Test of Coombs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	77	answer	2	Determination of iron, cobalamin and folic acid.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	77	answer	3	Abdominal ultrasound.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	77	answer	4	Bone marrow aspirate.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	78	question	-	35-year-old woman on hormonal treatment for infertility. He went to the emergency department due to constitutional syndrome and paresthesias in the left side of the body. In blood tests, Hb 7.5 g / dL, reticulocytes 10% (0.52%), platelets 5,000 / uL, normal leukocytes, LDH 1,200 IU / L, direct negative Coombs test, undetectable haptoglobin are detected. Morphology of peripheral blood with abundant schistocytes. Normal coagulation tests. What is the diagnostic suspicion and the most appropriate treatment?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	78	answer	0	Autoimmune hemolytic anemia. Start steroids.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	78	answer	1	Von Willebrand disease. Administration of desmopressin.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	78	answer	2	Thrombocytopenic purpura. Start steroids and platelet transfusion.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	78	answer	3	Evans syndrome. Start steroids.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	78	answer	4	Thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura. Treatment with plasmapheresis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	79	question	-	A 70-year-old man should undergo cataract extraction surgery. He has a mitral mechanical prosthesis for 10 years and is being treated with acenocoumarol. The electrocardiogram shows a sinus rhythm. Which of the following recommendations do you find most appropriate?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	79	answer	0	Perform eye surgery without stopping acenocoumarol.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	79	answer	1	Suspend acenocoumarol 5 days before surgery and restart it the day after it.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	79	answer	2	Suspend acenocoumarol 5 days before surgery, start low molecular weight heparin 3 days before surgery and suspend it 24 hours before surgery.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	79	answer	3	Suspend acenocoumarol 1 day before the intervention and use fresh frozen plasma during it.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	79	answer	4	Suspend acenocoumarol 1 day before the intervention and give vitamin K just before it.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	80	question	-	A 29-year-old woman with a history of abundant rules and long-standing iron-deficiency anemia who have required treatment with ferrotherapy since she was 17 years old. Consult because after a tooth extraction you have hemorrhage that has required local hemostatic treatment. He relates that a maternal aunt presents frequent epistaxis. In analytical presents: 8000 leukocytes / uL, Hb 10.7 g / dL, VCM 76 fL, 380,000 platelets / uL; the biochemistry is normal. Prothrombin activity 90%; INR 0.9; Activated Partial Thromboplastin Time (APTT) 48 sec (39 sec) with an APTT ratio of 1.3 and fibrinogen derivative 340 mg / dL. What is the most likely diagnostic suspicion and how would it confirm it?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	80	answer	0	Hemophilia A and mixtures test.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	80	answer	1	Lupus anticoagulant and ANAS study.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	80	answer	2	Sideroblastic anemia and spinal aspiration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	80	answer	3	Congenital thrombocytopathy and study of platelet aggregation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	80	answer	4	Von Willebrand disease and determination of factor vW.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	81	question	-	Which of the following statements is FALSE with respect to multiple myeloma?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	81	answer	0	The cytogenetics and serum levels of albumin and beta2-microglobulin are important data for the prognosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	81	answer	1	Bortezomib, thalidomide, lenalidomide and polychemotherapy are very useful therapeutic tools.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	81	answer	2	Autogenic transplantation of hematopoietic progenitors provides a long progression-free survival.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	81	answer	3	Allogeneic transplantation should be considered an experimental procedure (of unproven efficacy).
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	81	answer	4	Radiation therapy has no role in the treatment of the disease or its complications.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	82	question	-	Patient of 74 years of age, asymptomatic, who in a routine analysis presents platelets 40,000 platelets / μL, the remainder being the normal blood cell count and the complete normal biochemistry. Point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	82	answer	0	The most likely diagnosis is an Idiopathic Thrombocytopenic Purpura and steroid treatment should be started as soon as possible.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	82	answer	1	It is a serious thrombocytopenia with a high risk of spontaneous bleeding.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	82	answer	2	A peripheral blood smear should be performed to rule out pseudotrombocytopenia or spurious thrombocytopenia before further measurements are made.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	82	answer	3	The most probable diagnosis is that of a myelodysplastic syndrome, so the initial test to be performed would be a bone marrow study.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	82	answer	4	An initial study should be performed with viral serologies, autoimmunity study and abdominal ultrasound. If all these tests were normal, the study should be completed with a peripheral blood smear.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	83	question	-	Pruritus is a typical manifestation of all the following diseases, except:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	83	answer	0	Hodgkin lymphoma.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	83	answer	1	Polycythemia vera.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	83	answer	2	Mycosis fungoides
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	83	answer	3	Systemic mastocytosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	83	answer	4	Acute myeloblastic leukemia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	84	question	-	A 34-year-old woman is admitted to the hospital for pulmonary embolism confirmed by angio-CT. He has no history of recent surgery, trauma or travel. He refers to Raynaud's phenomenon for 2 years, and the previous year he had an abortion at 12 weeks of gestation. He has no family history of venous thromboembolic disease. The activated partial thromboplastin time is 56 sg (normal 25-35 sg) and the platelet count is 120000 / uL. Which of the following diagnostic tests would help you most in the diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	84	answer	0	Antithrombin III.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	84	answer	1	Lupus anticoagulant.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	84	answer	2	Factor V of Leiden.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	84	answer	3	Protein C.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	84	answer	4	Protein S.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	85	question	-	Patient with diabetes mellitus, weight loss, anemia and necrolytic migraine erythema. The most likely diagnosis is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	85	answer	0	Somatostatinoma.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	85	answer	1	Insulinoma
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	85	answer	2	Vipoma
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	85	answer	3	Gastrinoma
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	85	answer	4	Glucagonoma
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	86	question	-	A 78-year-old woman has recently been diagnosed with diabetes mellitus type 2. She has a history of deep vein thrombosis 5 years ago, high blood pressure, depression and generalized anxiety. Take hydrochlorothiazide, lisinopril, citalopram and aspirin. Live alone in sheltered apartments. Eat little, typically coffee and toast for breakfast, fruit and half a sandwich to eat and salad for dinner. Walk 1.5 km daily. It measures 152 cm and weighs 39 Kg. The blood pressure is 130/80 mmHg and the heart rate is 82 bpm. Laboratory tests included basal glycemia of 147 mg / dL (1 month ago it was 152 mg / dL), creatinine 1.0 mg / dL (estimated glomerular filtration rate 28 ml / min), urea 32 mg / dL and glycosylated hemoglobin 9 ,5%. Which of the following is the best initial treatment for diabetes?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	86	answer	0	Insulin glargine subcutaneous 8 U per day.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	86	answer	1	Oral metformin at a dose of 850 mg every 12 hours.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	86	answer	2	Oral Glibenclamide 10 mg daily.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	86	answer	3	It does not need pharmacological treatment, only diet.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	86	answer	4	Pioglitazone 15 mg daily.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	87	question	-	Metformin is recommended as initial treatment in most consensus of treatment of type 2 diabetes, for efficacy, safety and price; However, its use has some limitations and it is obligatory to suspend it in some clinical situations. In which of the following situations would you NOT consider stopping this treatment?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	87	answer	0	Introduction of long-acting insulin analogue due to poor metabolic control.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	87	answer	1	Alcohol intake greater than 50 g / day as usual.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	87	answer	2	CT scan with intravenous contrast.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	87	answer	3	Diarrheic picture with elevated plasma Cr at 2.5 mg / dL.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	87	answer	4	Acute ischemia of the lower extremities with significant tissue hypoxia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	88	question	-	In relation to the risk factors of cardiovascular diseases, which of the following statements is NOT correct?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	88	answer	0	Regarding LDL cholesterol, the therapeutic objective depends on the global cardiovascular risk.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	88	answer	1	Type 2 diabetic patients should be considered at high cardiovascular risk and the objective in terms of LDL cholesterol should be <100 mg / dL.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	88	answer	2	There is not enough evidence that low levels of HDL cholesterol suppose a cardiovascular risk factor.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	88	answer	3	The important thing about the risk associated with hypertension is that it improves when blood pressure is reduced regardless of the type of drug used.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	88	answer	4	The existence of coronary disease in the family is a risk factor for the patient.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	89	question	-	A 24-year-old man with hypogonadism of hypothalamic origin secondary to operated craniopharyngioma, undergoing intramuscular treatment with testosterone undecanoate every 12 weeks, which is referred to us from another center for follow-up. The patient interrogates us in the initial visit about the follow-up of his basic pathology, possible adverse events of the hormonal treatment and probabilities of having offspring in the future. Which of the following statements is NOT correct?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	89	answer	0	Serum testosterone levels should be measured just before each subsequent injection.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	89	answer	1	The goal of treatment is to maintain serum testosterone concentrations in the normal range of normality.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	89	answer	2	It is indicated to check the hematocrit on an annual basis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	89	answer	3	Treatment with intramuscular testosterone for a prolonged period will increase the chances of conception with your partner.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	89	answer	4	The treatment with testosterone does not require the monitoring of luteinizing hormone concentrations.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	90	question	-	A 25-year-old man with no personal or family history of interest, who enters Neurosurgery due to a cranial fracture due to a motorcycle accident. Three days later it begins abruptly with polyuria, polydipsia and intense thirst both during the day and at night. In the study conducted, a urinary volume of 7 liters with urinary osmolarity of 190 mOsm / L (90-1200) and plasma osmolarity of 292 mOsm / L (275-295) was observed. The plasma Na is 143 mmol / L. A water restriction test is performed and after checking that there is no increase in urinary osmolarity, a dose of 2 micrograms of desmopressin subcutaneously is administered. The posterior urinary osmolality is 410 mOsm / kg. What is the most likely diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	90	answer	0	Primary polydipsia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	90	answer	1	Central diabetes insipidus.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	90	answer	2	Acute adrenal insufficiency.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	90	answer	3	SIADH.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	90	answer	4	Nephrogenic insipid diabetes.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	91	question	-	Of the following statements, one is NOT a trigger for abdominopsychoneurological crises in acute porphyria. Indicate which:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	91	answer	0	The luteal phase of the menstrual cycle.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	91	answer	1	The enzymatic hepatic inducer drugs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	91	answer	2	The infections
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	91	answer	3	A restrictive diet in proteins.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	91	answer	4	The protease inhibitors used in HIV infection.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	92	question	-	The gluten-free diet is the cornerstone in the treatment of celiac disease. In this regard, there are numerous products manufactured with an uncertain composition in terms of gluten, often being misleading labeling. Of the following food groups, which one can we consider completely safe in the diet of a celiac patient?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	92	answer	0	Canned meat: Hamburgers, meatballs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	92	answer	1	Milk and derivatives: yogurt, cheese, cream, curd.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	92	answer	2	Sauces, condiments and food additives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	92	answer	3	Integral pasta: noodles, macaroni, noodles.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	92	answer	4	Delicatessen products, sausages, pâtés.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	93	question	-	Regarding the loss of bone mass in patients treated with glucocorticoids, what statement do you consider correct?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	93	answer	0	If the dose of prednisone received by the patient is less than 15 mg per day, for a time less than 6 months, it is not a real problem and no preventive measure should be taken.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	93	answer	1	Thiazides have been shown to reduce the risk of fractures, both in the hip and in the spine, in patients treated with glucocorticoids. Therefore, its use should be recommended in these patients as a preventive measure.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	93	answer	2	It is recommended to perform a bone densitometry after the first year of treatment with glucocorticoids, since before there is no loss of bone mass.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	93	answer	3	All patients treated with glucocorticoids should receive an adequate supply of calcium and vitamin D, which can come from the diet or from pharmacological supplements.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	93	answer	4	The loss of bone mass is observed, especially in the hip, so the densitometry of the spine has no use in its assessment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	94	question	-	A 33-year-old woman with a loss of 6 kg in the last 4 months, asthenia and anorexia. Amenorrhea for 2 months. The hormonal results indicate a basal cortisol serum concentration of 108 nmol / l (baseline normal value 115-550) and 123 nmol / l after stimulation with ACTH. The baseline plasma concentration of ACTH is 48 pmol / l (normal value: 2-12). What is the most likely diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	94	answer	0	Primary adrenal insufficiency.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	94	answer	1	Secondary adrenal insufficiency.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	94	answer	2	Tertiary adrenal insufficiency due to hypothalamic lesion.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	94	answer	3	ACTH-producing pituitary tumor (corticotropinoma).
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	94	answer	4	More tests should be done since the diagnosis is inconclusive.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	95	question	-	Which of the following clinical pictures is compatible with the diagnosis of subacute thyroiditis?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	95	answer	0	A 38-year-old woman with a 2-week history of thyroid pain, elevated T4 and T3, low TSH, and increased technetium uptake on the scan.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	95	answer	1	A 42-year-old man with a history of pain in the thyroid gland 4 months ago, fatigue, general malaise, low concentrations of free T4 and high TSH levels.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	95	answer	2	A 31-year-old woman with enlarged thyroid gland, painless on palpation, low TSH, high free T4 and T3, and increased technetium uptake on scintigraphy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	95	answer	3	A 30-year-old woman under treatment with oral contraceptives, with discomfort in the neck and palpable thyroid nodule that behaves as a solid on ultrasound. Increase in total T4 with normal TSH.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	95	answer	4	A 46-year-old man who consulted due to fatigue during the last 3 months. In the analytical, low concentrations of free T4 and T3 and TSH were observed.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	96	question	-	Which statement regarding the substitution treatment with L-thyroxine in a patient with hypothyroidism is correct?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	96	answer	0	Thyroid function will be determined 48 hours after its initiation to assess efficacy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	96	answer	1	In elderly patients and in order to improve symptomatology quickly, treatment with L-T4 is started at a dose of 150-200 micrograms per day.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	96	answer	2	In pregnancy, thyroid hormone requirements usually increase by about 50 micrograms per day, over the previous dose.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	96	answer	3	The medication should be taken in the middle of meals.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	96	answer	4	It is advisable to administer a gastric protector simultaneously to avoid gastritis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	97	question	-	Which of the following statements is INCORRECT in relation to the alterations of the acid-base balance?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	97	answer	0	The arterial pH is regulated by the Henderson-Hasselbach equation and is 7.35-7.45.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	97	answer	1	Hypercapnia (increase in PaCO2) is a consequence of the increase in CO2 production.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	97	answer	2	Metabolic acidosis occurs due to increased endogenous acid production, acid accumulation and / or loss of bicarbonates.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	97	answer	3	In patients with lactic acidosis it is common to find an anion gap or difference greater than 12 mmol / L.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	97	answer	4	The use of alkalizing solutions should be reserved for cases of severe acidemia with ph <7.20.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	98	question	-	A 47-year-old man consulted for edema in lower limbs of 3 weeks of evolution. In blood analysis, creatinine 1.3 mg / dL, total cholesterol 270 mg / dL and albumin 2.4 g / dL. In the urine sediment, it presents 15-20 red cells per field and in urine of 24 hours proteinuria is detected 3.7 g / day. What is the most likely diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	98	answer	0	Minimal change disease.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	98	answer	1	Focal and segmental glomerulosclerosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	98	answer	2	Membranous nephropathy
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	98	answer	3	Membranoproliferative glomerulonephritis type I.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	98	answer	4	Mesangial proliferative glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	99	question	-	A 68-year-old woman diagnosed with pulmonary tuberculosis. Treatment with Isoniacid, Rifampicin and Ethambutol was started. At 12 days after the start of treatment, he consulted for fever of 38ºC, skin rash, lymphadenopathy, arthralgia, lumbar pain, oliguria and eosinophilia with acute deterioration of renal function. The urine test revealed hematuria, leukocyturia with eosinophiluria in Wright's stain and non-nephrotic proteinuria (1.2 grams daily). With these clinical data the most likely diagnosis is:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	99	answer	0	Acute tubular necrosis due to drug nephrotoxicity.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	99	answer	1	Acute tubular necrosis of ischemic etiology.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	99	answer	2	Ateroembolic disease.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	99	answer	3	Thrombotic occlusion of the main renal artery.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	99	answer	4	Acute tubulointerstitial nephritis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	100	question	-	In which of the following types of glomerulonephritis is there a greater indication of IECAS or ARA-II as antiproteinuric therapy?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	100	answer	0	Segmental and focal glomerulosclerosis secondary to hyperfiltration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	100	answer	1	Acute postinfectious glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	100	answer	2	Extracapillary glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	100	answer	3	Glomerulonephritis due to minimal changes.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	100	answer	4	Membranoproliferative glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	101	question	-	Which of the following clinical situations carries a greater risk of progression of chronic kidney disease and would require more strict control by the nephrologist?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	101	answer	0	Diabetic patient with a glomerular filtration rate of 46 mL / min and a urine albumin / creatinine ratio of 25 mg / g.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	101	answer	1	Diabetic patient with a glomerular filtration rate of 89 mL / min and urine albumin / creatinine ratio of 475 mg / g.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	101	answer	2	Hypertensive patient with glomerular filtration rate of 65 mL / min and urine albumin / creatinine ratio of 150 mg / g.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	101	answer	3	A 70-year-old hypertensive patient with 1 simple cyst in each kidney, a glomerular filtration rate of 35 mL / min and an albumin / creatinine ratio in urine of 10 mg / g.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	101	answer	4	An 87-year-old hypertensive patient with a glomerular filtration rate of 30 mL / min and a urine albumin / creatinine ratio of 5 mg / g.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	102	question	-	Chronic interstitial nephropathies affect the tubular structures and the renal interstitium. If we analyze the functional defects that these pathologies can produce, we will NOT wait to find:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	102	answer	0	Isostenuria.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	102	answer	1	Hypochloremic metabolic alkalosis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	102	answer	2	Tubular atrophy and interstitial fibrosis in the renal histological study.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	102	answer	3	Normal or little expressive urinary sediment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	102	answer	4	Proteinuria of less than 2 grams per day.
