Cuaderno_2014_1_M	177	question	-	He is presented with a cohort study involving 1000 female smokers and 2000 non-smoking women of the same age. If, after 5 years, 30 smokers and 20 nonsmoking women have experienced a stroke, what would be the relative risk and the attributable risk?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	177	answer	0	Relative risk = 3, attributable risk = 10 out of every 1000.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	177	answer	1	Relative risk = 3, attributable risk = 20 out of every 1000.
