Cuaderno_2014_1_M	184	question	-	In a pharmacoeconomic study, drug A produces a life expectancy of 5 years with a total cost of 5,000 euros, while drug B produces a life expectancy of 6 years with a total cost of 15,000 euros (average values ​​per patient) . The decision criterion is based on choosing the most effective intervention with a cost-effectiveness threshold of 30,000 euros per year of additional life earned per patient, what drug is cost-effective compared to the other and why?
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	184	answer	0	Drug B, because the incremental cost-effectiveness with respect to A is below the cost-effectiveness threshold.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	184	answer	1	Drug A, because it costs much less than B and there is only one year of difference in life expectancy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	184	answer	2	Drug A, because the incremental cost-effectiveness of B with respect to A is above the cost-effectiveness threshold.
