Cuaderno_2014_1_M	189	question	-	In a clinical trial that evaluates the efficacy of a hypolipidemic agent in the primary prevention of coronary heart disease, if the researchers have planned analysis of intermediate results and in view of them suspending the study before its completion they must know that:
Cuaderno_2014_1_M	189	answer	0	The study can only be interrupted when in some intermediate analysis there is a difference between the results of the interventions, p <0.05.
