Cuaderno_2014_1_P	28	answer	2	We obtain incomplete and biased information by the characteristics of the sample.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	28	answer	3	The basic criterion of inclusion in the sample is the accessibility of the participants.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	28	answer	4	The size of the sample should be as close as possible to that of the population.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	29	question	-	What is called "baseline" in single-case research designs or N = 1 designs ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	29	answer	0	The difference between the pretest and posttest measurements of the participant.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	29	answer	1	The normative reference of the population with which to compare the results of the intervention.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	29	answer	2	The changes detected in the dependent variable as a consequence of the application of the treatment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	29	answer	3	The series of observations of the dependent variable made before applying the treatment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	29	answer	4	The absence of variability in the observations of the dependent variable.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	30	question	-	Intrasubject experimental research designs:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	30	answer	0	They use independent variables not manipulated directly by the researcher but through the selection of the participants.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	30	answer	1	They are based on the verification of independent groups assigned to the experimental conditions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	30	answer	2	They combine two independent variables based on the characteristics of the participants.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	30	answer	3	They have lower internal validity than the intersubject designs when they do not use random assignment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	30	answer	4	They use specific control techniques to control the effects associated with the order of application of the experimental conditions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	31	question	-	What is the characteristic of the quasi-experimental research strategy that differentiates it from the experimental strategy ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	31	answer	0	Single or very small cases are studied.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	31	answer	1	The study is carried out in simulated contexts.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	31	answer	2	There is no random assignment of participants to the different study conditions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	31	answer	3	Several dependent variables are used.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	31	answer	4	It is done with samples of participants obtained by probabilistic sampling.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	32	question	-	Experimental factorial designs or also called complex experimental designs:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	32	answer	0	They study the effect of an independent variable on several dependent variables.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	32	answer	1	They study the main effects of several independent variables and their possible joint effect or interaction.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	32	answer	2	They are inadequate if it is suspected that some of the study variables may have interaction effects.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	32	answer	3	They can dispense with experimental control techniques because of their complexity.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	32	answer	4	They are based on the application of all experimental conditions to the same group of participants.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	33	question	-	What specific procedure of the experimental strategy makes it the most appropriate to test hypotheses of causality? :
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	33	answer	0	The representative sampling of the participants.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	33	answer	1	The manipulation of the independent variable with control of possible strange variables.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	33	answer	2	The realization of the study in real contexts with natural groups.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	33	answer	3	The identification of possible predictor variables through the retrospective analysis of the study phenomenon.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	33	answer	4	The application of statistical techniques for the analysis of data.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	34	question	-	The structure of the personality can be organized according to:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	34	answer	0	The three-dimensional model of R.B. Cattell.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	34	answer	1	The five-factor proposal of Zuckerman.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	34	answer	2	The five basic factors of Cantor and Kihstrom.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	34	answer	3	The sixteen factors of H.J. Eysenck.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	34	answer	4	The Monorrasgo theory of Costa and McCrae.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	35	question	-	Cognitive investigations of intelligence, and as regards the relationship between Reaction Time (RT) and Intellectual Quotient (IQ):
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	35	answer	0	They have found positive associations of great magnitude.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	35	answer	1	They describe negative relationships with differences in magnitude, according to the studies.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	35	answer	2	They have found an absence of association between both constructs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	35	answer	3	They have not received attention from the scientific community.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	35	answer	4	They start from the study of cultural differences in intelligence.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	36	question	-	According to the classification of features that R.B. Cattell:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	36	answer	0	The specific features are observed in the daily behavior of individuals, in all cultures.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	36	answer	1	Ergos and feelings shape the dynamic or motivational structure.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	36	answer	2	Capabilities and competences are temperamental traits.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	36	answer	3	Attitudes are performance traits.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	36	answer	4	The basic features are directly observable and qualitatively objective.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	37	question	-	The fluid intelligence:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	37	answer	0	It is involved in tasks that are new.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	37	answer	1	It is shown in tasks with verbal content.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	37	answer	2	It reflects formal learning.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	37	answer	3	It is not part of the general intelligence.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	37	answer	4	Delimits skills based on previous experience.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	38	question	-	Interpersonal intelligence, spatial intelligence and logical-mathematical intelligence, are types of intelligence belonging:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	38	answer	0	To Cattell's model of intelligence.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	38	answer	1	To the Triarchic Theory of Sternberg.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	38	answer	2	To the proposal offered by Eysenck.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	38	answer	3	To the model of the Multiple Intelligences of Gardner.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	38	answer	4	The structure of the intellect is superfluous to Guilford's proposal.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	39	question	-	In personality psychology, when talking about consistency and stability of the personality, one can be referring to the observation that:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	39	answer	0	The features that the person shows are coherent with their ontogenetic history.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	39	answer	1	The behaviors and situations that are equated through the time points are similar.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	39	answer	2	Personality is the response to situational demands.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	39	answer	3	The items that evaluate a trait maintain high correlations with each other.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	39	answer	4	Stable and consistent behaviors are indicators of mental health.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	40	question	-	The heritability of a personality trait:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	40	answer	0	It is a statistical concept to estimate the influence of phenotypes on genotypes, regardless of the environment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	40	answer	1	It is generalizable to all humans, regardless of the culture and the historical moment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	40	answer	2	It calls into question the ability of the environment to modify the genetic endowment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	40	answer	3	It is studied, among other perspectives, from molecular genetics.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	40	answer	4	It refers to the direct influence of paternal and maternal genes on the behavior of an individual.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	41	question	-	Beliefs and values, according to the psychology of personality:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	41	answer	0	Once established, they do not experience changes during the rest of the individual's life.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	41	answer	1	They direct the person towards transcendence, according to Maslow's motivational proposal.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	41	answer	2	They predispose the person to prefer some modes of behavior over others.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	41	answer	3	They impel people towards the defense of human rights.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	41	answer	4	They encourage group development in the face of individual development.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	42	question	-	According to the Theory of Multiple Intelligences, intrapersonal intelligence:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	42	answer	0	It has been preponderant in our current system of academic evaluation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	42	answer	1	It is the ability to understand and interact with others.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	42	answer	2	It focuses on the potential to form a mental model of a spatial world.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	42	answer	3	It is the ability to form an adjusted model of oneself and to use it effectively in life.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	42	answer	4	It is exhibited when it comes to making products that need to use the body.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	43	question	-	The content validity of an evaluation instrument refers to:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	43	answer	0	The evidence obtained by factor analysis.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	43	answer	1	The concurrence of measures.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	43	answer	2	The adequacy in the establishment of inferences.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	43	answer	3	The relevance and representativeness of its items.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	43	answer	4	The significant relationships with other measures.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	44	question	-	What does the intersessional sampling used in observation techniques refer to:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	44	answer	0	To the registration of relevant information between sessions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	44	answer	1	To the periodicity, number and criteria of start-end of the sessions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	44	answer	2	To the successive rounds of observation of the subjects to observe.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	44	answer	3	To the temporary selection and its interval or partial modality.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	44	answer	4	To the record of focal events that occur between sessions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	45	question	-	In which group of techniques is included the Thematic Apperception Test (Murray TAT) ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	45	answer	0	Interpretive projects
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	45	answer	1	Subjective constructive.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	45	answer	2	Construction projects
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	45	answer	3	Rational graphics.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	45	answer	4	Subjective narratives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	46	question	-	What can indicate, among other things, the high scores on the F Scale of the Minnesota Multiphasic Personality Inventory (MMPI) ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	46	answer	0	Social desirability and good image intent.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	46	answer	1	A high number of incomplete answers.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	46	answer	2	The degree of sincerity.
