Cuaderno_2014_1_P	49	question	-	When the cutoff point of a diagnostic instrument is very high, the risk of:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	49	answer	0	False positives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	49	answer	1	False negatives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	49	answer	2	True positives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	49	answer	3	Sensitivity of the test.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	49	answer	4	Inconsistencies of validity.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	50	question	-	The sensitivity of a diagnostic test is related to:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	50	answer	0	Its ability to discriminate true positives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	50	answer	1	Its ability to discriminate true negatives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	50	answer	2	Its ability to discriminate against false positives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	50	answer	3	Its ability to discriminate against false negatives.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	50	answer	4	The high cut point.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	51	question	-	Adaptive tests are characterized by:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	51	answer	0	The unidirectional relationship between the evaluated and the test.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	51	answer	1	The interactive process of selection of items dependent on the response of the evaluated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	51	answer	2	The homogeneous and identical application of the items to all those evaluated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	51	answer	3	The identical length in the number of items to be applied.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	51	answer	4	The selection of items by independent criteria to the response of the evaluated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	52	question	-	The Raven Progressive Matrices test provides an estimate of:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	52	answer	0	Level of development.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	52	answer	1	Level of maturation.
