Cuaderno_2014_1_P	52	answer	3	Verbal intelligence level
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	52	answer	4	Manipulative intelligence level.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	53	question	-	What are, among others, the main biases associated with the observer in the framework of observation techniques ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	53	answer	0	The duration of the experiment.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	53	answer	1	The excess of information.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	53	answer	2	The technical accuracy
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	53	answer	3	The illusion of learning.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	53	answer	4	The expectation and mechanical errors of registration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	54	question	-	Indicate which of the following options make possible the criterial evaluation tests (or with reference to criteria):
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	54	answer	0	Assess the performance with respect to a normative group.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	54	answer	1	Determine relative performance among other people.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	54	answer	2	Obtaining a normative score.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	54	answer	3	Evaluate the performance with respect to a content area or domain.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	54	answer	4	Assess a skill considering the performance of your reference group.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	55	question	-	In 1994, Spitzer and collaborators developed a questionnaire and a joint interview for the evaluation of the main most frequent disorders in primary care health services. This instrument is called:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	55	answer	0	DIS-CIDI
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	55	answer	1	SCID II.
