Cuaderno_2014_1_P	68	answer	4	The motor.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	69	question	-	The individual evaluation of the intelligence presents, in front of its collective evaluation, the following advantage:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	69	answer	0	The application of individual tests implies a shorter duration.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	69	answer	1	The individual evaluation requires less training of the psychologist who administers them (the groups require more expertise).
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	69	answer	2	It offers a total score without detailing in the different skill profiles.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	69	answer	3	It is considered more useful for a clinical purpose than the collective evaluation.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	69	answer	4	Individual evaluation does not require time control.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	70	question	-	When distinguishing alcoholic patients with Korsakoff Syndrome from patients with alcoholic dementia, we can take into account that:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	70	answer	0	In patients with Korsakoff syndrome, the IQ measurement remains relatively intact, while this measure is impaired in the case of alcoholic dementia.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	70	answer	1	Patients with dementia do not have memory problems, while those with Korsakoff syndrome do.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	70	answer	2	In cases of dementia, amnesia appears as the first and most relevant symptom.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	70	answer	3	In the case of Korsakoff Syndrome there is no anterograde amnesia (ability to acquire new information).
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	70	answer	4	In the case of dementia, the skills learned remain intact, whereas in Korsakoff Syndrome they are very deteriorated.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	71	question	-	If a patient claims to hear voices in Paris when he is in London, we say that he suffers:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	71	answer	0	A hallucination reflects.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	71	answer	1	A paranoid hallucination.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	71	answer	2	An extracampine hallucination.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	71	answer	3	An autoscopic hallucination.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	71	answer	4	A negative hallucination
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	72	question	-	In psychology they are called "illusions" to:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	72	answer	0	The perceptive deceptions.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	72	answer	1	The pseudoalucinations.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	72	answer	2	The abnormal associations of sensations (synesthesia).
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	72	answer	3	The anomalies of perceptual integration (morpholysis).
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	72	answer	4	The anomalies in the structuring of ambiguous stimuli.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	73	question	-	Within the perceptual distortions we can find:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	73	answer	0	Hallucinations
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	73	answer	1	The metamorphopsias.
