Cuaderno_2014_1_P	156	question	-	What is the fundamental goal of cognitive therapy for auditory hallucinations in schizophrenia ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	156	answer	0	Completely eliminate the appearance of auditory hallucinations.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	156	answer	1	Avoid listening to hallucinations and avoid situations that provoke them.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	156	answer	2	Getting no one to realize that the person is having hallucinations.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	156	answer	3	Reduce beliefs about omnipotence, malevolence, benevolence, and obedience, regarding voices.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	156	answer	4	Modify the beliefs they have about schizophrenia and medication.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	157	question	-	The use of psychoeducation in schizophrenia now adopts a prosthetic criterion instead of issuing disqualification judgments. What goal should psychoeducation be set to follow this principle ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	157	answer	0	It is intended that the person discovers everything that he will never be able to do due to his abilities.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	157	answer	1	The person is instructed to avoid making decisions for himself because his disorder prevents him from doing so.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	157	answer	2	It is intended that the person discover the best way to make their life but accepting and taking into account their abilities.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	157	answer	3	He tries to concentrate all his efforts is his strengths and ignore his disabilities.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	157	answer	4	The person is instructed about the fact that he can only achieve his goals if he takes the medication and does psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	158	question	-	Patients with schizophrenia usually present the so-called interactive imbalance that is expressed in the conversation with an exaggerated response latency, minimal speech or lack of participation in it. What is the most appropriate method to evaluate the patient and decide if it is convenient to perform a Social skills training ?:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	158	answer	0	Through scales of intelligence.
