Cuaderno_2014_1_P	177	question	-	With respect to effective psychological treatments for depression, it can be stated that:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	177	answer	0	They are more expensive treatments (in terms of efficiency) than psychotropic drugs.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	177	answer	1	They have been proposed by the NICE guide (National Institute for Health and Clinical Excellence) as the second treatment of choice for those cases in which the drugs have not been shown to be effective.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	177	answer	2	In general, those psychological treatments that use active methodologies, limited in time and structured, tend to be more effective.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	177	answer	3	They generate a similar number of dropouts than pharmacological therapy.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	177	answer	4	They generate a higher level of stigma than pharmacological therapies.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	178	question	-	Point out the correct answer regarding therapy for Rehm's depression:
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	178	answer	0	It focuses on three processes: self-tracking, self-esteem and self-reinforcement.
Cuaderno_2014_1_P	178	answer	1	It has no empirical evidence to be considered well-established treatment.
