Cuaderno_2015_1_E	151	answer	3	Pre-eclampsia added to a chronic hypertension.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	152	question	-	In the fourth stage of labor one of the signs of placental detachment is the observation of the spontaneous descent of the cord clamp that protrudes through the vulva. How is this sign called ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	152	answer	0	Sign of Küstner.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	152	answer	1	Sign of Fabre.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	152	answer	2	Strassman sign.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	152	answer	3	Sign of Ahlfeld.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	153	question	-	In relation to rubella and pregnancy, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	153	answer	0	The risk of congenital anomalies is very high when the infection occurs in the first weeks of gestation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	153	answer	1	The most frequent fetal injuries that occur are the so-called "Gregg's triad".
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	153	answer	2	The diagnosis of maternal immunity is made by serological determination of IgG antibodies.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	153	answer	3	Due to its great teratogenic potential, non-immunized women will be given the vaccine during pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	154	question	-	What type of pathogen is the cause of chlamydia ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	154	answer	0	Ectoparasite
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	154	answer	1	Fungus.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	154	answer	2	Bacterium.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	154	answer	3	Protozoon.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	155	question	-	The O'Sullivan test consists of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	155	answer	0	Administer 50 g of oral glucose and determine the basal glycaemia and one hour post-intake.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	155	answer	1	Administer 100 g of oral glucose and determine basal glycemia and one hour post-intake and two hours post-intake.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	155	answer	2	Administer 100 g of oral glucose and determine basal glycaemia, and three post-intake determinations separated by one hour in each.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	155	answer	3	Administer 50 g of oral glucose and determine basal glycaemia and two hours post-intake.
