Cuaderno_2015_1_E	156	answer	0	Intramurals
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	156	answer	1	Subserosal.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	156	answer	2	Submurals
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	156	answer	3	Submucosal
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	157	question	-	The nervous anorexies are usually accompanied by an amenorrhea due to malnutrition that can be primary or secondary and that has an origin:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	157	answer	0	Ovarian
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	157	answer	1	Uterine.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	157	answer	2	Pituitary
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	157	answer	3	Hypothalamic
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	158	question	-	What is the most effective measure for the prevention of neonatal hemorrhagic disease ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	158	answer	0	Perform the Coombs test with umbilical cord blood at birth.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	158	answer	1	Vaccination of the mother with antibodies before delivery.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	158	answer	2	Administration of 1 mg of vitamin K intramuscularly to the newborn.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	158	answer	3	Administration of 1 mg of vitamin K orally and repeat the dose after 1 week.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	159	question	-	What is the treatment of choice when faced with an infestation caused by pediculus humanus capitis or head louse ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	159	answer	0	Cream or lotion of permethrin 1% and new application in 7-10 days.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	159	answer	1	Cream or lotion of líndano to 1% and new application in 5 days.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	159	answer	2	Acetic acid lotion at 2% daily for 7 days.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	159	answer	3	Mebendazole 100 mg cream in a single application.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	160	question	-	Which is NOT a sign of respiratory distress in the newborn ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	160	answer	0	Nasal flaring.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	160	answer	1	Cyanosis.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	160	answer	2	Expiratory moan
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	160	answer	3	Thoraco-abdominal dissociation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	161	question	-	On the growth and development of a healthy child in the first 18 months of life. Which of the following findings would you consider as an alarm sign ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	161	answer	0	Loss of 10% of the weight at birth during the first week of life.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	161	answer	1	Persistence of the Moro reflex at 2 months.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	161	answer	2	Absence of contralateral transfer of objects at 12 months.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	161	answer	3	Monthly weight gain less than 300 g between 15 and 18 months.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	162	question	-	Pilar is a 17-year-old mother of a newborn of 30 weeks of gestational age, who affirms that she would have liked to have a daughter and not a child that reminds her of the couple that has abandoned her. Until a month ago I worked as a cashier in a supermarket. Indicate the nursing diagnosis that presents:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	162	answer	0	Parental deterioration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	162	answer	1	Risk of alteration of the maternal / filial dyad.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	162	answer	2	Tiredness of the role of caregiver.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	162	answer	3	Ineffective maternity process risk.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	163	question	-	According to Piaget's Theory of Cognitive Development, a 5-year-old child is in:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	163	answer	0	Period of formal operations.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	163	answer	1	Sensory-motor period.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	163	answer	2	Period of specific operations.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	163	answer	3	Pre-operational period
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	164	question	-	Javier is a 16-year-old adolescent, diagnosed with a non-curable disease. What will be the expected behavior in front of others when they are aware of their own death ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	164	answer	0	Behave as an adult would.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	164	answer	1	Getting angry with your family
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	164	answer	2	Surround yourself with your friends.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	164	answer	3	Allow to be supported and helped by your family.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	165	question	-	Laura is a 7-year-old girl who has been diagnosed with Type I Diabetes Mellitus for the last 2 years. Three days ago she started skating classes and after them she reported tiredness, nervousness, tremors and headache. When commenting to the nurse of the sports center where he performs this activity, the therapeutic recommendation on his part would be:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	165	answer	0	To control blood glucose before, during and after exercise.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	165	answer	1	Let him skating since it would not be good for his disease control.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	165	answer	2	Have simple carbohydrates before exercise.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	165	answer	3	That it is normal to feel this way after so much sport.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	166	question	-	In relation to diaper rash, indicate the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	166	answer	0	It preferably affects folds and concave areas.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	166	answer	1	The prophylactic use of creams with mild corticosteroids is convenient.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	166	answer	2	The number of diaper changes has NO repercussion on the development of diaper rash.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	166	answer	3	The most frequent associated superinfection is caused by gram-negative bacteria.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	167	question	-	He approaches to assess a newborn of 28 weeks of gestational age and observes that he has tachycardia, grayish skin, crying difficult to calm, fingers and extended legs. These symptoms are characteristic of the nursing diagnosis:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	167	answer	0	Apnea.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	167	answer	1	Chronic pain.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	167	answer	2	Disorganized infant behavior.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	167	answer	3	Anxiety.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	168	question	-	Point out the FALSE statement:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	168	answer	0	The predominant symptomatology in paracetamol poisonings is hepatotoxicity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	168	answer	1	Gastric lavage is not indicated as a therapeutic measure in the management of acute paracetamol poisoning.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	168	answer	2	The cornerstone in the treatment of paracetamol poisoning is its specific antidote, N-acetylcysteine.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	168	answer	3	Gastrointestinal decontamination by the administration of activated charcoal is indicated if less than 4 hours have elapsed from the intake of paracetamol at a toxic or unknown dose.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	169	question	-	With regard to childhood pain, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	169	answer	0	The sensation of pain is subjective and must be accepted by the nurse.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	169	answer	1	The response to pain is important when a child is being screened to diagnose their illness and their analgesic treatment can be delayed.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	169	answer	2	Parents when they meet their children are able to identify when the child has pain.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	169	answer	3	Children do not tolerate pain better than adults.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	170	question	-	Infant of 4 months of age (6.280 Kg) that goes to the Pediatric Emergency Service with acute diarrhea of ​​24 hours of evolution, with watery stools without blood or mucus and signs of light-moderate dehydration. Receive exclusive breastfeeding His mother reports that he has not vomited, that he takes the shots avidly and that he is irritable. The therapy of choice for the management of this infant would consist of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	170	answer	0	Temporary interruption of breastfeeding and parenteral rehydration with normal saline during the first 4 hours or until the signs of dehydration have disappeared. An intestinal motility inhibitor will be administered.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	170	answer	1	Oral rehydration with low osmolarity solution in frequent low volume doses, ensuring between 50-100 ml / kg for 3-4 hours, replacement of maintained losses and maintaining breastfeeding.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	170	answer	2	Oral rehydration with low osmolarity solution in frequent low volume doses assuring contributions between 15-30 ml / kg for 4 hours to replenish deficit and 10 ml / kg per deposition, and administration of lactose-free formula.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	170	answer	3	Parenteral load with glucosaline solution at 10-15 ml / kg in 30 minutes, oral rehydration with high osmolality solution ensuring contributions between 75-100 ml / kg in the first 4 hours and maintenance of breastfeeding on demand.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	171	question	-	The classic triad of symptoms associated with hemolytic uremic syndrome consists of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	171	answer	0	Iron deficiency anemia, thrombocytopenia and acute kidney damage.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	171	answer	1	Hemolytic anemia, pancytopenia and chronic kidney damage.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	171	answer	2	Hemolytic anemia, thrombocytopenia and acute renal damage.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	171	answer	3	Hemolytic anemia, pancytopenia and acute kidney damage.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	172	question	-	Among the stress factors for hospitalization in school children (children 6-12 years), it is NOT:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	172	answer	0	Lost of control.
