Cuaderno_2015_1_E	178	answer	2	Varicella zoster.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	178	answer	3	Measles.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	179	question	-	Your team receives a warning for the attention in the public thoroughfare of a teenager with altered level of consciousness. His group of friends comments that he has "drunk a lot", denying the consumption of other toxic substances. On examination, the patient is unable to maintain standing without help, responds with "grunts" and slow withdrawal to the painful stimulation by opening his eyes to call him forcefully by name. It presents miotic and symmetrical pupils, with reactivity to slowed light. What would be the initial care for that patient ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	179	answer	0	Patient stabilization (ABC) and rapid test of toxins and capillary blood glucose to establish the therapeutic plan. Transfer to the hospital.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	179	answer	1	Patient stabilization (ABC), safety position, thermal protection, monitoring and peripheral venous catheterization for administration of fluid therapy with 5% glucose solution, after administration of 100 mg of thiamine, correction of hypoglycaemia and acidosis, according to analytical data. Rapid determination of toxins and administration of antidote, when appropriate. Transfer to the hospital.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	179	answer	2	Patient stabilization (ABC), administration of activated charcoal without causing vomiting until fully conscious, and intramuscular naloxone (0.2-0.4 mg). Transfer to the hospital.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	179	answer	3	Patient stabilization (ABC), safety position and central venous catheterization for load administration with 50% hypertonic glucose, 1M bicarbonate bolus (5 mEq / kg) and subsequent rapid fluid therapy with Ringer® solution. Transfer to the hospital.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	180	question	-	In relation to the clinical problems that most preterm infants of very low birth weight can present in the first days of life. Which of the following statements is correct?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	180	answer	0	The main cause of the alterations that occur in the respiratory function of the premature newborn (hyaline membrane disease) is the late prenatal administration of corticosteroids.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	180	answer	1	The depletion of intravascular volume is the most frequent cause of hypotension in very low weight premature infants, being the expansion with colloids (5% albumin diluted to the medium) the therapy of choice.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	180	answer	2	The persistence of the ductus arteriosus (ductus) produces the typical clinical manifestations of right-to-left shunting.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	180	answer	3	The vulnerability of premature infants to hypoxia and hypertension are associated with an increased risk of intraventricular hemorrhage.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	181	question	-	If the mother has varicella infection during pregnancy, when is there a greater risk of the child developing varicella fulminans ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	181	answer	0	When the infection occurs between the first and second trimesters of pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	181	answer	1	When the infection occurs between the second trimester and the 21 days prior to delivery.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	181	answer	2	When the infection occurs between 20 and 6 days before delivery.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	181	answer	3	When the infection occurs between 5 days before delivery and 2 days after delivery.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	182	question	-	In relation to the geriatric assessment process, indicate the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	182	answer	0	The Reisberg scale is used for mental evaluation of affective type.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	182	answer	1	The scale of Lawton and Brody is used for social assessment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	182	answer	2	The Pfeiffer test is a scale for cognitive assessment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	182	answer	3	The Katz index is a scale to assess dementia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	183	question	-	Indicate which of the following is NOT a risk factor for urinary incontinence in older people:
