Cuaderno_2015_1_E	183	answer	1	Hyperglycemia of the hypoglossal nerve.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	183	answer	2	Presence of architectural barriers.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	183	answer	3	Degradation of physic movility.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	184	question	-	Related to the need for food in people who have suffered neurological problems, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	184	answer	0	It is convenient to mix solid foods with liquids to facilitate swallowing.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	184	answer	1	Distracting elements should be avoided during feeding.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	184	answer	2	The person must maintain an upright posture, seated and with slight anterior flexion of the neck.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	184	answer	3	An adequate oral hygiene should be carried out after the ingestion.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	185	question	-	What theory of aging exemplifies a retired 76-year-old cabinetmaker who is interested in staying active and collaborating with the school and the parish of the neighborhood in the maintenance of furniture, doors, pieces of wood for children, etc. ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	185	answer	0	Theory of activity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	185	answer	1	Theory of human needs.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	185	answer	2	Theory of individualism.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	185	answer	3	Theory of continuity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	186	question	-	An elderly man addresses the nurse saying: "I feel overwhelmed with the treatment they have given me; I do not know if I'll be able to follow him. " From the following responses from the nurse, which is the best example of therapeutic communication ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	186	answer	0	"Is right. The treatment is very heavy, but believe me, the treatment is good. "
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	186	answer	1	"Do not worry or give it that much importance. You will see how everything will be fine ".
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	186	answer	2	"Tell me, why do you think you will not be able to follow it? Do you think it will not help? "
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	186	answer	3	"You must trust the doctor who has given you the treatment. He knows what he's doing".
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	187	question	-	As the result of a recent stroke, a person has suffered a sensory-functional hemiplegia. In order to favor the maximum stimulation of the affected side, the nurse must:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	187	answer	0	Place objects on the unaffected side to stimulate functional capacity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	187	answer	1	Address the patient from the unaffected side.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	187	answer	2	Decrease sensory stimulation to avoid the feeling of frustration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	187	answer	3	Place objects on the affected side to stimulate the use of paretic limbs.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	188	question	-	Pedro with a history of chronic constipation presents fecal impaction with fecalomas. Of the following statements about the activities to be carried out for the digital extraction of them. Which one is NOT correct ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	188	answer	0	Do not use laxatives or enemas.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	188	answer	1	Explain to the person what is going to be done and monitor the vital signs.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	188	answer	2	Extract the fecal mass carefully and without breaking it, to favor rectal stimulation and defecation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	188	answer	3	Place the patient in the left lateral decubitus position.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	189	question	-	On malnutrition in the elderly, which of the following statements is NOT correct ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	189	answer	0	An albumin below 2.5 g / dl is considered a sign of severe malnutrition.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	189	answer	1	Anthropometric measures are late signs of malnutrition and do not identify initial malnutrition.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	189	answer	2	Obtaining a score of 16 points in the complete Mini Nutritional Assesmen test (MNA) is indicative of the risk of malnutrition.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	189	answer	3	Albumin is the most used biochemical marker to determine nutritional status.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	190	question	-	In the annual review, a 70-year-old person is worried because he has noticed the presence in his eyes of a grayish yellow ring around the iris. Which of the following responses from the nurse indicates knowledge of the condition that concerns the patient ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	190	answer	0	Tell the patient that this condition could cause complications and that it should be seen by the specialist.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	190	answer	1	Inform the doctor to make sure it is not something serious.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	190	answer	2	Explain to the patient that it is a normal change that occurs in the eye over time.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	190	answer	3	Discuss that it could be a serious medical problem and refer you to the ophthalmologist.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	191	question	-	Point out the INCORRECT response. Nursing information systems involve:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	191	answer	0	Increased satisfaction in the work of the nurse.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	191	answer	1	Reduction of errors by omission.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	191	answer	2	Decrease in the time spent with patients.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	191	answer	3	Increase in job satisfaction.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	192	question	-	Flowcharts or flowcharts are graphical representations of sequences of operations, procedures or routines that are used for process analysis or decision making. These diagrams use a set of symbols that are common to all this type of representations and that has a concrete meaning. In this sense, as a nurse, they have commissioned a flow chart to represent a decision-making process in the provision of care that is carried out in their healthcare unit. During your design you use the diamond symbol (: point out the meaning given to the diamond symbol in the flow diagrams:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	192	answer	0	Decision.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	192	answer	1	Start and stop.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	192	answer	2	Flow.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	192	answer	3	Document.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	193	question	-	Pablo, a 58-year-old man, has a small shop in the area attached to the Health Center where you are attending. Pablo is married to 57-year-old Pilar who is completely dedicated to the care of her two daughters (13 and 14 years old) and Pablo's mother who is 82 years old, and whom Pablo himself defines as "a great dependent". During the interview Pablo is tired, concerned about the physical and emotional state of his wife and says that in the next town, which is as big as his own and has the same proportion of dependent elderly, "they have opened a center day for the elderly and that we need it too ". Point out the correct answer that indicates the type of need that Paul shows:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	193	answer	0	Sense
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	193	answer	1	Compared
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	193	answer	2	Normative.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	193	answer	3	Expressed
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	194	question	-	Regarding Herzberg's theory on the factors that explain the behavior of workers, point out which of the following is a motivational factor:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	194	answer	0	Salary.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	194	answer	1	Category.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	194	answer	2	Progress.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	194	answer	3	Job security.
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	195	question	-	Point out the correct answer. The achievement of the health objectives that entails the development of action protocols and health programs is part of the planning:
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	195	answer	0	Strategic
Cuaderno_2015_1_E	195	answer	1	Tactic.
