Cuaderno_2015_1_M	51	question	-	In patients with hematological diseases, a "hemorrhagic cystitis" picture may occasionally occur. Among the multiple etiologies of this process, some viruses are included. Which of the following is the most frequently involved?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	51	answer	0	Polymyoma virus BK.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	51	answer	1	Herpes simplex virus type 2
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	51	answer	2	Poxvirus.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	51	answer	3	Enterovirus 71
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	52	question	-	One of the following statements related to hepatitis viruses is NOT correct. Indicate it:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	52	answer	0	In contrast to HBV and HCV, blood transmission of HAV is uncommon, because viremia is short and low-grade.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	52	answer	1	HEV is a defective virus that uses the antigen on the surface of HBV as its envelope protein.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	52	answer	2	The polymerase encoded by HBV acts as a reverse transcriptase using viral mRNA as a template for the synthesis of progenie DNA genomes.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	52	answer	3	The detection of HBsAg for more than six months indicates a chronic carrier state.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	53	question	-	A 70-year-old patient was admitted to the ICU after suffering anterior AMI treated by coronary angioplasty and stent placement in the anterior descending artery. 4 days later, he presented a sudden hypotension that required a vigorous volume, the start of vasoactive drugs, orotracheal intubation and connection to mechanical ventilation. Physical examination highlights a murmur not previously present. Given the suspicion of mechanical complication of the infarction, transthoracic echocardiography showing pericardial effusion was performed. Point out the CORRECT Answer:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	53	answer	0	Mortality with medical treatment is 20%.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	53	answer	1	In case of free wall rupture there is an oximetric jump in the right ventricle in the Swan-Ganz catheterization.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	53	answer	2	In case of free wall break there is no palpable thrill.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	53	answer	3	Mechanical complications usually appear on the first day after infarction.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	54	question	-	A 54-year-old patient was admitted due to a thermometrical fever of 38ºC in the previous five days and rest dyspnea (NYHA IV), which appeared 6 hours before going to the hospital. In the emergency room, the scan is compatible with heart failure and the ECG shows complete atrioventricular block with an exhaust ventricular rate of 45 bpm. The signs of heart failure are refractory to medical treatment and transesophageal echocardiography performed shows an aortic valve with an effective regurgitant orifice of 0.5 cm2. Serial cultures are positive for Streptococcus gallolyticus. Indicate the most accurate attitude:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	54	answer	0	Cardiac surgery of aortic valvular replacement by mechanical prosthesis with antibiotic therapy according to antibiogram.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	54	answer	1	Antibiotic therapy according to antibiogram and implantation of intra-aortic balloon counterpulsation and transient pacemaker up to 3 weeks, after which definitive pacemaker will be implanted.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	54	answer	2	Implantation of transient pacemaker, antibiotic therapy according to antibiogram and percutaneous implantation of aortic valve prosthesis.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	54	answer	3	Urgent implantation of definitive pacemaker with antibiotic therapy according to antibiogram for 6 weeks.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	55	question	-	A 72-year-old woman came to the hospital for 2 hours of oppressive chest pain. The blood pressure is 68/32 mm Hg, the heart rate is 124 beats / min, the respiratory rate is 32 breaths / min, the oxygen saturation is 91% with 50% oxygen. Pulmonary auscultation showed bilateral crepitations. An ECG is performed showing a subepicardial lesion on the anterior side, with a mirror image on the inferior face. The chest radiograph shows a bilateral alveolar pattern. What is your therapeutic decision?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	55	answer	0	Start infusion of nitrates i.v.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	55	answer	1	Perform fibrinolysis with tenecteplase (TNK).
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	55	answer	2	Perform urgent coronary angioplasty.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	55	answer	3	Administer furosemide 40 mg i.v.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	56	question	-	Which of the following symptoms associated with high blood pressure has a worse prognosis?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	56	answer	0	Abrupt loss of right leg and arm strength of 10 minutes duration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	56	answer	1	Epistaxis of 30 minutes duration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	56	answer	2	Nocturnal evening headache.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	56	answer	3	Tachycardia and tremor.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	57	question	-	A 73-year-old woman admitted for progressive dyspnea to rest, orthopnea and an increase of 4 kg. Physical examination showed blood pressure of 150/84 mm Hg, heart rate 100 beats / minute, increase in jugular venous pressure, crackles in both bases and malleolar edema. Usual treatment: enalapril 5 mg every 12 hours, furosemide 80 mg daily. What is the most appropriate treatment at this time?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	57	answer	0	Administer furosemide intravenously.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	57	answer	1	Increase the dose of enalapril according to tolerance and administer furosemide intravenously.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	57	answer	2	Start a beta-blocker.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	57	answer	3	Add treatment with amlodipine.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	58	question	-	A 60-year-old man with a history of high blood pressure and dyslipidemia has recently been diagnosed with heart failure. After performing the relevant tests, it is possible to maintain the ejection fraction of the left ventricle (> 50%). In relation to the treatment, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	58	answer	0	The initial treatment should be directed to the underlying pathological process.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	58	answer	1	Treatment with diuretics should be started at high doses.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	58	answer	2	In case of needing treatment with nitrates, it should be started at low doses.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	58	answer	3	Dyspnea can be treated by reducing neurohormonal activation with angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors or angiotensin receptor antagonists.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	59	question	-	A patient consulted for a prominent cervical vascular beat. When listening to him, a high frequency diastolic murmur is heard. What is the cause?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	59	answer	0	Persistent ductus
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	59	answer	1	Papillary muscle dysfunction.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	59	answer	2	Mitral stenosis
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	59	answer	3	Aortic insufficiency
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	60	question	-	While performing the anamnesis to a patient who consults for chest pain in an Emergency Department, this loses consciousness, you stimulate and does not respond, opens the airway and checks that the patient does not breathe and can not find the carotid pulse. After asking for help, what is the next maneuver you should do?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	60	answer	0	Chest compressions
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	60	answer	1	Precordial blow
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	60	answer	2	Rescue ventilations.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	60	answer	3	Gold-tracheal intubation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	61	question	-	A 65-year-old patient presented with progressive dyspnea of ​​5 days of evolution until resting, orthopnea of ​​three pillows and episodes of nocturnal paroxysmal dyspnea. On auscultation, bilateral crepitations, holosystolic murmur irradiated to axilla and gallop rhythm for third and fourth noise. Point out the INCORRECT statement:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	61	answer	0	The third noise coincides with the rapid filling phase of the ventricular diastole of the cardiac cycle.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	61	answer	1	The most probable diagnosis is that of heart failure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	61	answer	2	The holosystolic murmur may correspond to a mitral insufficiency.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	61	answer	3	The fourth noise usually appears when there is a certain degree of valvular stenosis.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	62	question	-	Indicate among the following the most probable complication that presents the patient operated on, 20 years ago, of gastric ulcer by means of antrectomy and gastrojejunostomy (Billroth II) that comes to his office referring to post-radial abdominal pain, abdominal distension, diarrhea and analytical data of malabsorption of fats and vitamin B12:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	62	answer	0	Gastropathy due to bile reflux.
