Cuaderno_2015_1_M	75	answer	2	Jejunal diverticuli.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	75	answer	3	Radiation enteritis.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	76	question	-	Which of the following options is FALSE in relation to the papillary intraductal pancreatic mucinous tumor?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	76	answer	0	They are considered premalignant lesions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	76	answer	1	They can affect both the main pancreatic duct and the secondary branches and are characterized by mucin-producing epithelium.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	76	answer	2	The presence of nodules in the wall of the lesion does not constitute a sign of alarm.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	76	answer	3	When it affects the secondary branches, surgical resection is indicated if it is greater than 3 cm.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	77	question	-	Which of the following is NOT considered a risk factor for gallbladder carcinoma ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	77	answer	0	Biliary lithiasis.
