Cuaderno_2015_1_M	78	answer	1	Hyperthyroidism due to Graves' disease.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	78	answer	2	Ovarian teratoma (ovarian struma).
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	78	answer	3	Subacute thyroiditis
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	79	question	-	Woman diagnosed with type 1 diabetes mellitus for 24 years. He comes to clinic consultation with 3 months of tingling in both feet, with distribution in sock, with paresthetic pain and sensation of warm feet of nocturnal predominance, which interferes remarkably with his sleep. Which of the following drugs would you use first line for the treatment of your pathology?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	79	answer	0	Ibuprofen.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	79	answer	1	Oxycodone
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	79	answer	2	Duloxetine
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	79	answer	3	Paracetamol.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	80	question	-	A 49-year-old man consulted for intense polyuria and polydipsia and involuntary loss of 10 kg of weight and was diagnosed with diabetes mellitus by a plasma glycemia of 322 mg / dL and a glycosylated hemoglobin of 9.8%. Your doctor gives you dietary recommendations, the convenience of physical exercise, and starts treatment with metformin 850 mg / 12 hours and glimepiride 6 mg / day. In the following weeks the glycemic controls are progressively reduced. At 4 months the glycemia is 94 mg / dL and the HbA1c is 5.9%. The patient complains of frequent episodes of dizziness, epigastric pain, blurred vision, sweating and tremor, which improve eating something and that occur especially at the end of the morning and at the end of the afternoon. What modification would you propose in your treatment?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	80	answer	0	Check the distribution of carbohydrates in your diet.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	80	answer	1	Suspend metformin.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	80	answer	2	Suspend the sulfonylurea.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	80	answer	3	Replace metformin with a DPP4 inhibitor.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	81	question	-	In a 70-year-old diabetic man with a history of ischemic heart disease, what is the therapeutic target for LDL cholesterol and glycosylated hemoglobin (Hb A1c)?
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	81	answer	0	LDLc <115 mg / dL and Hb A1c <6.5%.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	81	answer	1	LDLc <100 mg / dL and Hb A1c <7%.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	81	answer	2	LDLc <70 mg / dL and HbA1c <7%.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	81	answer	3	LDLc <115mg / dL and Hb A1c <7%.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	82	question	-	A 22-year-old boy with hyposmia presents a lack of development of secondary sexual characteristics and infertility. Testicular volume of 4 mL bilateral. Analytically, FSH 1.2 U / L (vn 5-15); LH 0.6 U / L (vn 3-15); Testosterone 100 ng / dL (vn 300-1200), normal prolactin. Indicate the treatment that you will be proposed to achieve fertility:
