Cuaderno_2015_1_M	82	answer	2	Intramuscular administration of FSH and LH once a week.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	82	answer	3	Treatment with bromocriptine.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	83	question	-	We refer from ophthalmology to a 31-year-old man who consulted for vision loss and progressive headache. On physical examination, a temporal hemianopsia was observed and in pituitary magnetic resonance a tumor measuring 35 x 30 x 20 mm compressed the chiasm and cavernous sinus. The results of the functional study are cortisol 14 microg / dL, TSH 1.4 microU / mL, T4L 1.2 ng / dL, prolactin 480 microg / L (vn <15), testosterone 160 ng / dL (vn 300-1200) , FSH 1,2 U / L (vn 5-15) and LH 2 U / L (vn 3-15). What is the initial therapeutic approach ?:
