Cuaderno_2015_1_M	132	question	-	A patient of 25 years, during a tennis match, has severe pain in the neck and in the left eye. The next morning he wakes up with a feeling of instability of the gait and has palpebral ptosis of the left eye and anisocoria, with the left pupil being smaller than the right one. The patient maintains good visual acuity. Where would you most likely locate the injury?
