Cuaderno_2015_1_M	211	answer	3	It is the characteristic picture of Purstcher's traumatic retinal angiopathy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_M	212	question	-	84-year-old woman who came for loss of vision in the left eye of 4 days of evolution accompanied by metamorphopsias. The macula shows abundant hard exudates, two small deep hemorrhages and a localized detachment of the neurosensory retina. In the contralateral eye presents abundant soft drusen. Given this scenario, which of the following diagnoses do you think is most likely?
