Cuaderno_2015_1_M	220	question	-	Mariano is a 53-year-old man who comes to his office saying that he has felt a lot of discomfort for a few years now. He relates discomfort with a behavior that he finds absurd but which he is unable to avoid. This behavior that always takes place when you get home from work is to operate the toilet knob on the top floor of the house before doing anything else, even before greeting your family. Sometimes it has tried to resist to do it but it has only managed to be anguished and to delay the conduct a few minutes. This behavior that Mariano performs in an incoercible and automatic way is what is called:
