Cuaderno_2015_1_P	48	answer	3	The persistent difficulty in phonological production.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	49	question	-	What is the correct statement about the prevalence of depression in childhood and adolescence ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	49	answer	0	Between 6 and 12 years, the prevalence is much higher in girls.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	49	answer	1	In adolescence, depression is much more frequent in girls than in boys.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	49	answer	2	In adolescence, depression has a very similar prevalence in girls and boys.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	49	answer	3	The prevalence of depression is similar in adolescents and younger children.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	50	question	-	What is the correct answer about organic factors in mental retardation ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	50	answer	0	They are especially important at the most severe levels of delay.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	50	answer	1	Those who act after birth are not considered as such.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	50	answer	2	Its influence is demonstrated by the normal distribution of the Intellectual Quotient in the population.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	50	answer	3	When they are hereditary, they always involve multiple genes.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	51	question	-	Which of the following symptoms is NOT considered a manifestation of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder in childhood ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	51	answer	0	Verification compulsions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	51	answer	1	The excessive slowness associated with the need for symmetry.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	51	answer	2	Obsessive intrusive thoughts without compulsions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	51	answer	3	Evolutionary rituals that do not cause interference.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	52	question	-	Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of stereotyped behavior ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	52	answer	0	Be repetitive and rhythmic.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	52	answer	1	To be invariable in topography (physical manifestation).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	52	answer	2	Be rare and excessive in frequency, rate or amplitude.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	52	answer	3	Be inconsistent and in any case harmless to the subject.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	53	question	-	Which of the following symptoms is considered nuclear for the diagnosis of superficial developmental dyslexia ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	53	answer	0	The deterioration in the reading of pseudowords in comparison with that of words.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	53	answer	1	The concomitant appearance of aphasia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	53	answer	2	Regular words, even if they are unknown, are more likely to be read correctly than irregular words.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	53	answer	3	The appearance of visual and derivative paralexies.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	54	question	-	From the behavioral model What learning mechanism has been proposed as the main mechanism for selective mutism ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	54	answer	0	The positive reinforcement.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	54	answer	1	The negative reinforcement.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	54	answer	2	The positive punishment
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	54	answer	3	Modeling.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	55	question	-	In what cases of school refusal should the diagnosis of specific phobia be made ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	55	answer	0	When the fear, anxiety or avoidance is persistent and lasts 6 months or more.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	55	answer	1	When the refusal to go to school is persistent and generates clinically significant discomfort or deterioration in social, academic or family.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	55	answer	2	Provided it is not due to a separation anxiety disorder.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	55	answer	3	In those in which the phobic stimulus is a concrete aspect of the school context.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	56	question	-	What two major categories of syndromes distinguish the empirical classification of child psychopathology promoted by Achenbach ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	56	answer	0	Affective disorders and behavior disorders.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	56	answer	1	Socialized disorders and non-socialized disorders.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	56	answer	2	Internalized and externalized disorders.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	56	answer	3	Withdrawal and social problems.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	57	question	-	What effect does parent depression have on the psychopathology of children during their childhood ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	57	answer	0	It increases the risk of suffering from affective disorders but not that of suffering from anxiety disorders.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	57	answer	1	Prevents the development of a secure attachment relationship with the parent.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	57	answer	2	Specifically increases the likelihood of suffering a conduct disorder due to the alteration of parenting.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	57	answer	3	Its negative consequences are manifested in multiple areas of the child's functioning.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	58	question	-	According to the DSM (IV-TR and 5) Which of the following is required to diagnose Tourette Disorder ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	58	answer	0	A beginning of the symptoms before the 12 years.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	58	answer	1	That motor tics and vocal tics have been present at some time of the disease concurrently.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	58	answer	2	That the tics persist for more than a year since the appearance of the first tic.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	58	answer	3	That at least 3 vocal tics have been present.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	59	question	-	A 16-month-old boy said "potato" (potato) to refer to any round fruit or vegetable. How is this application of a word to more objects that include its conventional meaning ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	59	answer	0	Semantic restriction
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	59	answer	1	Semantic alliteration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	59	answer	2	Semantic infraexclusivity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	59	answer	3	Semantic overextension.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	60	question	-	A teenager, when asked why you can not steal, answers "because they can see you, report you to the police and you could go to jail". According to Kohlberg, what level of moral development is that teenager demonstrating ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	60	answer	0	Conventional.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	60	answer	1	Preconventional
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	60	answer	2	Oriented to the law.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	60	answer	3	Oriented to individual principles.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	61	question	-	Regarding the sense of sight in born babies What statement is true ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	61	answer	0	Babies are born practically blind.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	61	answer	1	Babies coordinate both eyes (bionocular vision) from birth.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	61	answer	2	Of the five senses, sight is the least mature at the time of birth.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	61	answer	3	Babies have special problems focusing on objects that are between 6 and 75 cm.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	62	question	-	Many teenagers think that they are special, that they have an exceptional life or that what happens to them is unique and has not been experienced by anyone before. How is this egocentric bias particularly frequent in adolescence called ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	62	answer	0	Bias of the uniqueness.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	62	answer	1	Imaginary audience
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	62	answer	2	Personal story
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	62	answer	3	Self-aggrandizement bias
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	63	question	-	A six-month-old baby has learned to pick up the rattle and shake it to make it sound. The result appeals to him and he repeatedly shakes it again. This behavior is a typical example of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	63	answer	0	Secondary circular reaction.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	63	answer	1	Assimilation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	63	answer	2	Tertiary circular reaction.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	63	answer	3	Accommodation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	64	question	-	Unlike crystallized intelligence, which of the following characteristics does fluid intelligence present?
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	64	answer	0	Their scores depend a lot on the design of the study, being more optimistic in studies with transversal designs.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	64	answer	1	It involves knowledge sensitive to the cultural context.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	64	answer	2	Presents scores that tend to increase in adulthood and old age.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	64	answer	3	It reaches its maximum level in early adulthood and then its scores tend to decrease.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	65	question	-	One of the characteristic elements of the cognitive treatment of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder is:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	65	answer	0	That the patient assumes or admits as normal the interpretations and dysfunctional evaluations that he maintains about his obsessions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	65	answer	1	That the therapist becomes the principal, and, if possible, the only source of reassurance for the patient.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	65	answer	2	Encourage the patient to interpret their obsessions as "noise" and to "let them go" without actively processing them or seeking special meaning.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	65	answer	3	Center the focus of the treatment on the contents of the obsessions to refute them.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	66	question	-	In the behavioral treatment of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder, the technique of exposure with prevention of response has the purpose that the patient:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	66	answer	0	Become accustomed to the anxiety caused by obsessions without using strategies to neutralize or diminish it.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	66	answer	1	Learn to effectively suppress your obsessions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	66	answer	2	Learn to delay the performance of the ritual until your anxiety decreases to at least 50% of the initial baseline.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	66	answer	3	Learn to question the contents of your obsessions using cognitive-type techniques (eg, the descending arrow, etc.).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	67	question	-	In the cognitive-behavioral treatment of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder, behavioral experiments:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	67	answer	0	They replace the live exposure when this technique can not be applied.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	67	answer	1	They must graduate in complexity, just as it is done with exposure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	67	answer	2	They should only be used in the relapse prevention phase because they allow more accurate predictions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	67	answer	3	They are useful so that the patient can verify in his daily life that his catastrophic predictions do not correspond with reality.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	68	question	-	The most recommended therapeutic style for the cognitive treatment of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder includes, among others, the following characteristics:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	68	answer	0	The correct application of exposure techniques with response prevention.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	68	answer	1	A collaborative empiricism and the use of guided discovery.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	68	answer	2	Use the relatives to convince the patient that their obsessions do not make sense and that their rituals waste their time.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	68	answer	3	A management style that is at the same time reassuring, that promotes in the patient the search for the causes of their problems in negative early life experiences.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	69	question	-	In which of the following phases of the technique of desensitization and reprocessing by eye movements (EMDR) of Shapiro, for the treatment of post-traumatic stress, the therapist performs series of bilateral visual or tactile stimulation ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	69	answer	0	Evaluation Phase.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	69	answer	1	Desensitization phase.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	69	answer	2	Phase of Corporal Exploration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	69	answer	3	Closing Phase.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	70	question	-	Which of the following techniques is included in the Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction (MBSR) program proposed by KabatZinn ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	70	answer	0	The differential activation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	70	answer	1	The corporal self-exploration.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	70	answer	2	The way to do.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	70	answer	3	The cognitive death.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	71	question	-	Which of the following is a goal of cognitive approaches in the treatment of Social Anxiety Disorder (Social Phobia):
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	71	answer	0	Increase expectations of loss of control over one's behavior at first.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	71	answer	1	Reduce exposures to feared situations until anticipatory anxiety is minimal.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	71	answer	2	Focus the subject's attention on the increase of its autonomous activation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	71	answer	3	Stop the tendency to set perfectionist goals.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	72	question	-	One of the therapeutic objectives of the current treatment models of Social Anxiety Disorder / Social Phobia (Clark, 2001) is to correct the excessive attention centered on oneself and the distorted image of the execution that many patients present. What technique do Clark and Beck propose for this purpose ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	72	answer	0	The technique of restructuring images.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	72	answer	1	Video-feedback
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	72	answer	2	Autobiographical memory of past social threats.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	72	answer	3	Mindfunlness meditation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	73	question	-	Which of the following is considered a predictor of poor response to exposure treatment in Posttraumatic Stress Disorder ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	73	answer	0	Feelings of anger or guilt.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	73	answer	1	Intense fear
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	73	answer	2	Sexual abuse
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	73	answer	3	Severe insomnia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	74	question	-	Which of the following components is part of the brief intervention program of Foa et al. (1995) for the treatment of victims of sexual assault ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	74	answer	0	Acceptance and commitment therapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	74	answer	1	Training in stress inoculation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	74	answer	2	Cognitive restructuring on irrational beliefs about the dangerousness of the world and the lack of control over the facts.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	74	answer	3	Problem resolution.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	75	question	-	In the treatment of what disorder propose Foa and Rothbaum (1998) the metaphor of "psychological digestion" to explain to the patient the objective of his intervention ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	75	answer	0	Obsessive Compulsive Disorder
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	75	answer	1	Generalized anxiety disorder.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	75	answer	2	Posttraumatic Stress Disorder
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	75	answer	3	Panic disorder.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	76	question	-	How can we improve the effectiveness of exposure in the treatment of specific phobias ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	76	answer	0	Extending the time elapsed between sessions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	76	answer	1	Prolonging the duration of the exhibition sessions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	76	answer	2	Associating exposure therapy with benzodiazepines.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	76	answer	3	Using the imagined exposure instead of the live exposure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	77	question	-	To a woman diagnosed with Generalized Anxiety Disorder we ask her not to send continuous whassaps to her daughter when she goes away from home over the weekend, and do not go to pick her up with her car when leaving the club every Saturday. We would be applying the technique known as:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	77	answer	0	Induction of rumination.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	77	answer	1	Prevention of behaviors of concern.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	77	answer	2	Concealed avoidance
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	77	answer	3	Defocusing of attachment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	78	question	-	The drugs of choice for Separation Anxiety Disorder are:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	78	answer	0	The antidepressants
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	78	answer	1	The antihistamines.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	78	answer	2	The beta-blockers.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	78	answer	3	The antipsychotics.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	79	question	-	For the psychological treatment of children with Attention Deficit and Hypersensitivity Disorder (ADHD), the technique of restoring the effects of adapted behavior is included, which is known as:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	79	answer	0	Response cost
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	79	answer	1	Problem resolution.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	79	answer	2	Self-regulation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	79	answer	3	Overcorrection
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	80	question	-	In which childhood-juvenile disorder is it more appropriate to use the therapeutic habit inversion procedure ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	80	answer	0	Hyperactivity
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	80	answer	1	Bruxism
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	80	answer	2	Obsessive compulsive disorder
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	80	answer	3	Defiant negativist disorder
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	81	question	-	Differential reinforcement procedures for the treatment of minors with aggressive behaviors:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	81	answer	0	They suppose a form of control of the antecedents of the conduct.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	81	answer	1	They include the reinforcement of omission.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	81	answer	2	They involve isolating the child in a corner of the room.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	81	answer	3	They consist in reducing the aversive stimulation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	82	question	-	In the cognitive behavioral treatment of adolescents with bulimia nervosa (Fairburn, 1993), during the phase of dietary change:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	82	answer	0	A weekly frequency is established for weighing.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	82	answer	1	Some prohibited foods are introduced.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	82	answer	2	A random meal pattern is prescribed.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	82	answer	3	It is discouraged for patients to record the foods they eat.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	83	question	-	On the use of neurofeedback for the treatment of ADHD in children, we can affirm that:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	83	answer	0	It uses the mechanisms of classical conditioning.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	83	answer	1	It is a training of brain electrical activity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	83	answer	2	Very complex and fun games tend to be more effective.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	83	answer	3	It is recommended in cases with low motivation towards treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	84	question	-	In the basic self-instruction training for children and adolescents, the phase in which a model performs a task while speaking aloud is called:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	84	answer	0	External guidance aloud.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	84	answer	1	Masked self-instructions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	84	answer	2	Cognitive modeling
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	84	answer	3	Covert self-instructions.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	85	question	-	Which of the following therapies uses the most and best evaluated procedures in the treatment of autistic spectrum disorders ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	85	answer	0	Occupational therapy
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	85	answer	1	Auditory integration therapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	85	answer	2	Therapies based on the applied analysis of behavior.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	85	answer	3	Hypnotherapy
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	86	question	-	What is the treatment for childhood depression with more empirical support ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	86	answer	0	Systemic family therapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	86	answer	1	Behavioral therapy
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	86	answer	2	Play therapy
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	86	answer	3	Relaxation of Koeppen.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	87	question	-	Which of the following is an objective of the treatment program for child victims of sexual abuse of Deblinger and Heflin ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	87	answer	0	Teach the child emotional expression skills.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	87	answer	1	Forget the abuse.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	87	answer	2	Increase the distrust of minors towards adults.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	87	answer	3	Modify the child's sexual consultation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	88	question	-	Which of the following behavioral treatments is appropriate for the approach to Childhood Tics Disorder ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	88	answer	0	Training in relaxation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	88	answer	1	Reversal of habit
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	88	answer	2	Positive mass practice
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	88	answer	3	Management of contingencies.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	89	question	-	Which of the following techniques is considered, according to the available evidence, a well-established treatment in the case of childhood phobias:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	89	answer	0	The participant modeling.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	89	answer	1	The training in assertiveness and HHSS.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	89	answer	2	The emotive images.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	89	answer	3	The therapy based on the game.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	90	question	-	Which of the following therapies was developed for the prevention of depressive relapses in patients recovered from one or more severe episodes of depression ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	90	answer	0	The therapy of acceptance and commitment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	90	answer	1	Analytic-functional psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	90	answer	2	Cognitive-behavioral analysis system of psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	90	answer	3	Cognitive therapy of depression based on full consciousness.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	91	question	-	Which of the following techniques is used in the cognitive therapy of depression in order to bring to consciousness the processes of construction of meanings and the underlying dispositions of the patient ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	91	answer	0	Temporary projection.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	91	answer	1	Attention refocalization.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	91	answer	2	Destructing biases
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	91	answer	3	Falling arrow.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	92	question	-	What is basically the first phase (the first four sessions) of cognitive therapy for depression based on full consciousness ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	92	answer	0	To learn to pay attention with full awareness to different aspects.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	92	answer	1	To learn to detect changes in mood.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	92	answer	2	To learn to avoid the occurrence of negative thoughts or feelings.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	92	answer	3	To learn to choose what is the best way to respond to negative thoughts or feelings.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	93	question	-	To improve adherence to treatment in a bipolar patient, we can perform a behavioral contract. Which of the following aspects is NOT recommended to be included in that contract ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	93	answer	0	The definition of treatment objectives.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	93	answer	1	External rewards for adherence to treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	93	answer	2	The factors that could interfere with the treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	93	answer	3	Plans to reduce obstacles to adherence.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	94	question	-	A technique of great relevance in addictions to motivate the patient to perform the treatment is:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	94	answer	0	The cathartic motivation.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	94	answer	1	The stimulate control.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	94	answer	2	The motivational interview
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	94	answer	3	The paradoxical intention.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	95	question	-	The treatment for addictions that seeks therapeutic change by manipulating the natural contingencies that may be influencing the maintenance of addiction, using reinforcers to facilitate the process, is called:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	95	answer	0	Training in self-control
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	95	answer	1	Relapse prevention program.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	95	answer	2	Training in social skills.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	95	answer	3	Community reinforcement program.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	96	question	-	Effective treatments based on the "behavioral execution mechanism" have been developed to:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	96	answer	0	Schizophrenia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	96	answer	1	Hypochondria.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	96	answer	2	Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	96	answer	3	The pathological game.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	97	question	-	Within the study oriented to the specification of the active ingredients of a psychological treatment, the strategy is to alter not the ingredients of the treatment, but the amount of them (eg the intensity of an ingredient) to achieve the maximum Efficacy is known as:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	97	answer	0	Parametric treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	97	answer	1	Build the treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	97	answer	2	Placebo treatment
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	97	answer	3	Dismantle the treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	98	question	-	It is considered that providing a rational explanation that accounts for the problems of the client or patient and the appropriate treatment is:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	98	answer	0	A specific therapeutic ingredient.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	98	answer	1	The most common and central procedure of systemic therapists.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	98	answer	2	A common factor of psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	98	answer	3	It should only be done when the client or patient shows resistance.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	99	question	-	Who formulated the proposal to collect information from the first contact for the request of consultation through the phone card, in order to develop circular hypotheses ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	99	answer	0	The interactive school of the Mental Research Institute (MRI).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	99	answer	1	The strategic school.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	99	answer	2	The Milan team led by M. SelviniPalazzoli.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	99	answer	3	The structural school.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	100	question	-	What is, according to psychoanalysis, the defense mechanism consisting in replacing the true desire of the person who provokes anxiety with another that does not cause it ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	100	answer	0	Projection.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	100	answer	1	Rationalization.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	100	answer	2	Repression.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	100	answer	3	Displacement.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	101	question	-	When a study compares two treatments, the difference between the means obtained by each treatment is usually calculated and divided by the joint standard deviation. How is this computation denominated ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	101	answer	0	Meta-analysis
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	101	answer	1	Size of the effect
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	101	answer	2	Percentage of patients recovered.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	101	answer	3	Reliable exchange rate.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	102	question	-	Kelly designed a complex procedure in which the client writes a description of himself (self-characterization) and then the therapist rewrites it in a way that allows the exploration of other alternative schemes. The subject is then asked to execute the new role in his daily life for two weeks with due preparation and training. At the end of this intense period, the new perspective acquired allows the client, with the therapist's help, to restructure some of his old superordinate schemes. What is this procedure called ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	102	answer	0	Search for alternatives
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	102	answer	1	Re-attribution technique.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	102	answer	2	Analysis of costs and benefits.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	102	answer	3	Fixed role technique.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	103	question	-	What can we say about the studies that aim to determine if a psychological treatment produces measurable effects in large populations of patients in their real clinical setting ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	103	answer	0	They are effectiveness studies.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	103	answer	1	These are studies that aim to achieve maximum internal validity.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	103	answer	2	They are studies of effectiveness.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	103	answer	3	They are characterized by the randomization of patients.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	104	question	-	In Rational Emotive Therapy the concept of "ego anxiety" refers to the discomfort that people experience when:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	104	answer	0	They present beliefs related to incompetence or personal disqualification.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	104	answer	1	They consider that they have to get what they want.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	104	answer	2	They consider that their welfare is threatened.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	104	answer	3	They do not tolerate and they seem terrible the unpleasant situations of the life.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	105	question	-	During problem-solving training in problem-solving therapy, the principle of "postponement of judgment" is indicated in the phase of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	105	answer	0	Orientation towards the problem.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	105	answer	1	Decision making.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	105	answer	2	Implementation of the chosen alternative.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	105	answer	3	Generation of solution alternatives.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	106	question	-	To plan effective exposure sessions in a case of animal-specific phobia, keep in mind that the rate of exposure (also called exposure gradient):
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	106	answer	0	It does not affect the effectiveness of the technique and will depend on the patient's preferences.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	106	answer	1	It affects effectiveness, with gradual exposure being more effective.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	106	answer	2	It affects the effectiveness, the symbolic gradual exposure being more effective.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	106	answer	3	It affects the effectiveness, being more effective the massive exhibition.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	107	question	-	Exposure with response prevention is currently one of the most useful techniques for the treatment of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	107	answer	0	Social anxiety
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	107	answer	1	Obsessive compulsive disorder
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	107	answer	2	The specific phobias.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	107	answer	3	Bulimia nervosa.
