Cuaderno_2015_1_P	109	answer	2	The reversal of habit.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	109	answer	3	The paradoxical intention.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	110	question	-	In Cognitive Therapy the beliefs that have to do with attitudes, rules and assumptions that are formulated in propositional terms of the type "if ... then" are called:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	110	answer	0	Nuclear beliefs.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	110	answer	1	Intermediate beliefs
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	110	answer	2	Control schemes.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	110	answer	3	Automatic thoughts
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	111	question	-	The verbal insults and insults can be an example of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	111	answer	0	Primary stimuli.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	111	answer	1	Deterrent incentives
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	111	answer	2	Unconditioned aversive stimuli.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	111	answer	3	Conditioned aversive stimuli.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	112	question	-	In borderline personality disorder, the treatment that has received the most empirical evidence is:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	112	answer	0	Cognitive therapy based on the schemes.
