Cuaderno_2015_1_P	117	answer	1	They do not interfere with cognitive functioning.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	117	answer	2	They have better tolerance and a lower risk of tardive dyskinesia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	117	answer	3	They do not increase the risk of developing a metabolic syndrome.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	118	question	-	What type of family intervention of schizophrenia has among its main objectives the reduction of expressed emotion and contact with the patient and the increase of social networks of the family:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	118	answer	0	The psychoeducational model of Anderson.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	118	answer	1	The socio-family model of Leff.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	118	answer	2	The cognitive behavioral model of Tarrier.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	118	answer	3	Fallon's family behavioral therapy.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	119	question	-	The application of the integrated psychological therapy of Roder's schizophrenia:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	119	answer	0	Significantly improves cognitive and behavioral variables after treatment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	119	answer	1	It exclusively improves the cognitive variables.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	119	answer	2	It improves cognitive variables significantly while its behavioral effects are inconsistent.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	119	answer	3	Improves cognitive and behavioral variables inconsistently.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	120	question	-	Among the criteria for referral of eating disorders to an emergency department of a general hospital to receive urgent medical treatment, we find:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	120	answer	0	Weight loss> 50% in the last 6 months (> 30% in the last 3 months).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	120	answer	1	Presence of regular bulimic episodes, that is, behaviors of food overeating and / or persistent purgative behaviors (self-induced vomiting, abuse of laxatives and use of diuretics).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	120	answer	2	Lack of awareness of disease.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	120	answer	3	Chronic amenorrhea and asthenia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	121	question	-	Interpersonal therapy is one of the treatments of choice for cases of:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	121	answer	0	Anorexia nervosa.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	121	answer	1	Bulimia nervosa.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	121	answer	2	Obesity with binge eating (especially for weight loss).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	121	answer	3	Rumination
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	122	question	-	A modeling procedure that combines model exposure and performance, verbal and physical instigators, behavior testing, and in vivo desensitization is called:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	122	answer	0	Modeling in vivo.
