Cuaderno_2015_1_P	168	question	-	Which of the following aspects differentiates panic disorder from a specific phobia, according to the DSM (IV-TR and 5) ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	168	answer	0	The presence of panic attacks.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	168	answer	1	The intensity of panic attacks (higher in panic disorder).
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	168	answer	2	The symptoms present during the panic attack.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	168	answer	3	The type of panic attack: unexpected in the panic disorder, and situational in the phobia.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	169	question	-	What kind of expectations does Reiss's cognitive model include for the explanation of phobias ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	169	answer	0	Expectations of anxiety and expectations of concern.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	169	answer	1	Expectations of damage and expectations of danger.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	169	answer	2	Expectations of anxiety and expectations of danger.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	169	answer	3	Expectations of anxiety and expectations of disgust.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	170	question	-	To make a diagnosis of Panic Disorder according to DSM (DSM-IV-TR and DSM-5) Which of the following aspects is essential ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	170	answer	0	That there have been at least three panic attacks.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	170	answer	1	That panic attacks have led to avoidance responses.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	170	answer	2	That panic attacks are accompanied by a high hypervigilance to physical sensations.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	170	answer	3	That biological causes (i.e. substance use or general medical condition) of the symptoms have been ruled out.
