Cuaderno_2015_1_P	173	answer	2	The exaggerated responsibility.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	173	answer	3	Excessive and uncontrolled worry.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	174	question	-	Which of the following elements is most central in the cognitive model of Compulsive Obsessive Disorders ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	174	answer	0	The absence of a relationship between obsessions and maladaptive beliefs or assessments.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	174	answer	1	Hypervigilance to the threatening stimuli of the environment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	174	answer	2	The maladaptive belief of having excessive responsibility.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	174	answer	3	The expectations of harm and anxiety.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	175	question	-	We say that a depressed person suffers "anhedonia" when:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	175	answer	0	Express feelings of sadness
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	175	answer	1	He suffers a decrease in his positive emotions and vital enjoyment.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	175	answer	2	It presents a diminished activity level and lack of motivation to carry out activities.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	175	answer	3	In depression, a risk of suicide is detected.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	176	question	-	Which of these theories explains why it is easier for a child to acquire a conditioned response of fear to a small insect than to a remote control ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	176	answer	0	The two-factor theory of Mowrer.
