Cuaderno_2015_1_P	178	answer	3	In reality Operant Conditioning does not play any role in the theory, since it is based solely on the Classic Conditioning.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	179	question	-	Unlike other phobias, the phobia of blood and wounds is characterized by the presence of dizziness and, on occasion, fainting. What are these responses to ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	179	answer	0	A biphasic response pattern characterized by an increase in heart rate and blood pressure, followed by a vasovagal deceleration of the heart rate and a decrease in blood pressure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	179	answer	1	A pattern of biphasic response characterized by a decrease in heart rate and blood pressure, followed by a sympathetic acceleration of the heart rate and an increase in blood pressure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	179	answer	2	A pattern of unifasic response characterized by an increase in heart rate and blood pressure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	179	answer	3	A pattern of unifasic response characterized by a decrease in heart rate and blood pressure.
Cuaderno_2015_1_P	180	question	-	Which of the following aspects is nuclear for the diagnosis (DSM-IV-TR and DSM 5) of Post Traumatic Stress Disorder ?:
