Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	17	question	-	Can ozone be considered a good oxidant ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	17	answer	0	No. It is a powerful reducer. In fact, it is usually used to obtain hydrogen from water (reducing the water's protons).
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	17	answer	1	No, it is not even capable of oxidizing iodide to iodine.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	17	answer	2	Yes. Sometimes it also transfers an oxygen atom to the reducer.
