Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	21	question	-	How are water-soluble chromium III complexes ?:
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	21	answer	0	They are usually hexacoordinated and octahedral. They can be neutral, cationic or anionic.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	21	answer	1	They are usually flat squares.
