Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	26	answer	3	The cubic symmetry groups have a single main axis of symmetry.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	27	question	-	The surface tension:
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	27	answer	0	It is defined only for flat interfaces.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	27	answer	1	If it has a high value for a substance, it will force it to ascend through a capillary, if it is introduced inside it.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	27	answer	2	It exists because the liquid-vapor interfaces tend spontaneously to increase in size.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	27	answer	3	It is the constant of proportionality that relates the work necessary to increase the size of a liquid-vapor interface with the increase of the area of ​​said interface.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	28	question	-	The electrophoretic technique known as SDSPAGE is widely used in the determination of proteins. In her:
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	28	answer	0	Agarose polymer gels are used and the surfactant produces fragments of protein that are separated according to their charge / radius.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	28	answer	1	The sample dissolved in SDS is applied by gravity, so that the sample tank, raised above the high voltage source allows the injection in very restrictive gels.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	28	answer	2	Two-dimensional electrophoresis is produced, one on a polyacrylamide gel and the other on a solid medium modified with SDS.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	28	answer	3	Micelles form between the SDS and the protein so that they provide a negative charge per unit of constant mass, and the proteins can be separated according to their molar mass.
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	29	question	-	Can potentiometric titrations at constant intensity be carried out using two indicator electrodes of the same nature?
Cuaderno_2015_1_Q	29	answer	0	No, only potentiometric titrations can be done at i = 0.
