Cuaderno_2016_1_E	0	question	-	Regarding Inequalities in Health, it is true that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	0	answer	0	Numerous scientific studies show that inequalities in health are responsible for an excess of morbidity and mortality similar to most known risk factors for disease.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	0	answer	1	The different axes of inequality that determine hierarchies of power in society are social class, gender, age, ethnicity or race and territory.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	0	answer	2	They are not related to the concept of discrimination.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	0	answer	3	There is not enough scientific evidence to recommend that inequalities in health can be reduced if the appropriate public health and social interventions and policies are applied.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	1	question	-	In relation to the conceptual framework of the determinants of social inequalities in health, of the Commission to reduce Health Inequalities in Spain (2010), based on Solar and Irwin and Navarro, it is FALSE that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	1	answer	0	Social inequalities in health are the result of the action of the so-called structural determinants of inequalities and intermediate determinants.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	1	answer	1	The social structure determines inequalities in the intermediate factors, which, in turn, determine inequalities in health.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	1	answer	2	The intermediate determinants are composed of the socioeconomic and political context.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	1	answer	3	The health system also plays an important role in the generation of health inequalities, since, even in those places where coverage is universal and free, people with lower socioeconomic status find greater barriers to access.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	2	question	-	For the diagnosis of tuberculous infection from the tuberculin test, we must bear in mind that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	2	answer	0	The Mantoux technique is used, which consists of the subcutaneous injection of 0.1 ml of the purified protein derivative.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	2	answer	1	An 18-gauge needle is used, usually on the anterior aspect of the forearm in the middle and upper third, causing a papule of between 6 and 10 mm in diameter.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	2	answer	2	The reading of the test is done between the fifth and seventh day, and induration and erythema should be measured.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	2	answer	3	Induration ≥ 5 mm is considered positive in individuals at risk of developing the disease (intimate contacts with index or suspected cases of tuberculosis regardless of BCG, patients suspected of clinical or radiological tuberculosis and in patients with HIV).
