Cuaderno_2016_1_E	9	answer	1	Sorbitol.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	9	answer	2	Xylitol.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	9	answer	3	Aspartame
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	10	question	-	One of the following organizational measures is NOT a priority for improving the approach to chronicity in the healthcare system:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	10	answer	0	Strengthening of Primary Care teams.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	10	answer	1	Involvement of patients in their self-care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	10	answer	2	Reorganization of attention.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	10	answer	3	Copayment for the use of emergency services and primary care consultations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	11	question	-	You are in chronic consultation of a Health Center, attending a 61-year-old man, with high blood pressure, dyslipidemia, overweight and smoker. Which of the following parameters would you need to assess your cardiovascular risk with the SCORE table ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	11	answer	0	Blood pressure, cholesterol, age, sex and tobacco consumption.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	11	answer	1	Blood pressure, family history of premature cardiovascular disease, sex, body mass index and tobacco consumption.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	11	answer	2	Blood pressure, triglycerides, age, sex and waist circumference.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	11	answer	3	Blood pressure, cholesterol, waist circumference, presence of diabetes, tobacco use.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	12	question	-	You are a family nurse in a Health Center and a patient with Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, who persists in smoking and refuses to go to therapy groups for smoking cessation, has joined your quota. The nurse who treated him previously diagnosed him a year ago Ineffective Health Management. If the nursing diagnosis persists, which of the following manifestations could you detect in the patient's assessment ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	12	answer	0	Ineffective decisions in daily life to achieve health goals.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	12	answer	1	It exaggerates the negative feedback about itself.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	12	answer	2	Irritability.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	12	answer	3	Dysfunctional interaction with other people.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	13	question	-	The strategy for the Chronicity Approach in the National Health System establishes the measures for the reorientation of health care to chronicity. Of the following measures, a NO is intended for this purpose:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	13	answer	0	Enhance case management.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	13	answer	1	Guarantee the integral and multidisciplinary assessment of patients.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	13	answer	2	Guarantee the population quality information, true and unbiased, about health in general.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	13	answer	3	Implement individualized care plans.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	14	question	-	What is called, in qualitative research, the sampling in which the obtaining of data is guided by the concepts derived from the theory that is being constructed ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	14	answer	0	Sampling of convenience.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	14	answer	1	Sampling with purpose
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	14	answer	2	Theoretical sampling.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	14	answer	3	Sampling in snowball.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	15	question	-	In the process of qualitative research, when successive inquiries in both subjects and in the analysis does not provide new relevant information about the phenomenon studied. What concept is it referred to ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	15	answer	0	Suitability.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	15	answer	1	Theoretical saturation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	15	answer	2	Evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	15	answer	3	Coding.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	16	question	-	What is the key record in ethnographic research, where is recorded the research process and the impressions and feelings of the researchers? :
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	16	answer	0	Observation-participant.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	16	answer	1	Field diary.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	16	answer	2	Condensed report
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	16	answer	3	Extended report.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	17	question	-	When is it considered that a measuring instrument is reliable ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	17	answer	0	When recommended by a group of accredited experts.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	17	answer	1	When you measure the variable that you intend to measure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	17	answer	2	When it produces consistent results when applied on different occasions: stability or reproducibility.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	17	answer	3	When it is useful and sensitive to the health problem you have to evaluate.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	18	question	-	What is the validity of a measuring instrument ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	18	answer	0	It is the degree to which an instrument is sensitive to changes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	18	answer	1	It is the degree to which an instrument measures the variable it intends to measure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	18	answer	2	It is the degree to which an instrument produces consistent results.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	18	answer	3	It is the degree to which an instrument is stable in its measurements.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	19	question	-	What is simple random sampling ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	19	answer	0	It is the technique that decides the number of individuals that have to participate in the study.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	19	answer	1	It is the technique of selecting subjects where chance does not intervene.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	19	answer	2	It is the random technique of selection of study variables.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	19	answer	3	It is that technique in which each unit of the sampling frame has the same probability of being chosen.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	20	question	-	What is critical reading ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	20	answer	0	It is the reading of an article by a critical expert.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	20	answer	1	Critical reading is the systematic process developed to evaluate the design and methodology of the study, the quality of the data and analyze and interpret the results.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	20	answer	2	It is reading in discussion groups where a specific topic is discussed.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	20	answer	3	It is a reading where what is valued and criticized is the experience and capacity of the authors of the article.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	21	question	-	What is Evidence-based Nursing ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	21	answer	0	It is the conscious, explicit and judicious application of the best scientific evidence available regarding nursing knowledge to make decisions about patient care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	21	answer	1	Do research studies in nursing care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	21	answer	2	It is to administer care based on the opinions of the experts.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	21	answer	3	It is the application of nursing care that has been shown to be efficient.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	22	question	-	What is the correct answer regarding the incidence of AIDS in Spain in the last five years ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	22	answer	0	The sex route is the category of transmission that has the highest incidence of AIDS.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	22	answer	1	Those under 25 years of age have the highest incidence of AIDS.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	22	answer	2	People from sub-Saharan Africa have the highest incidence of AIDS.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	22	answer	3	The most frequent defining AIDS disease is Kaposi's sarcoma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	23	question	-	What is the correct answer regarding cervical cancer ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	23	answer	0	The diagnosis is made by serology.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	23	answer	1	The treatment is carried out with pharmacological measures.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	23	answer	2	The main causative agent is the Human Papilloma Virus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	23	answer	3	It is the first most frequent cancer in Spain.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	24	question	-	What is the correct answer regarding the adjustment of mortality rates ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	24	answer	0	The indirect method is preferably used for small populations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	24	answer	1	The indirect method is preferably used for large populations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	24	answer	2	The ratio of standardized rates indicates the difference in mortality rates in two different populations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	24	answer	3	The indirect method has the disadvantage that it needs more information for its elaboration.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	25	question	-	According to the World Health Organization, how should nurse care be organized in Primary Care ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	25	answer	0	Organization by specialized services and programs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	25	answer	1	Provide family assistance and home care to a limited number of families.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	25	answer	2	Organization in a medical team of a nursing family.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	25	answer	3	Organize specialized teams in home care and generalist nurses in consultations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	26	question	-	What is the process in which the options and services necessary to satisfy the health needs of a person are valued, planned, applied, coordinated, monitored and evaluated, articulating the communication and the available resources that promote quality results and result cost-effective ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	26	answer	0	Planning centered on the person.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	26	answer	1	Link Nursing.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	26	answer	2	Case management
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	26	answer	3	Continuity of care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	27	question	-	What phase of adaptation to the care situation corresponds to that in which the caregiver may have difficulty verbalizing the feelings provoked by the painful events of care ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	27	answer	0	Phase of denial or lack of Awareness of the Problem.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	27	answer	1	Search phase of information and appearance of negative feelings.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	27	answer	2	Reorganization phase.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	27	answer	3	Resolution Phase.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	28	question	-	What are the components and tools in the Friedman Family Assessment model ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	28	answer	0	Family development stage, structural stage, functional stage.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	28	answer	1	The family as a system, health as a workplace, learning as a process through which healthy behaviors are acquired.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	28	answer	2	Family adjustment phase, adaptation phase.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	28	answer	3	Identification of information, stage of family development, data of the environment, family structure, family functions, family coping.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	29	question	-	What questionnaire would you use to assess family functioning ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	29	answer	0	Apgar Familiar.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	29	answer	1	MOS questionnaire.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	29	answer	2	Duke-UNC questionnaire.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	29	answer	3	Social Readjustment Scale.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	30	question	-	In a diagnosis of community health it is true that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	30	answer	0	It is a test that is done prior to accessing the community.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	30	answer	1	The key tool is the use of information systems.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	30	answer	2	It is a diagnosis that mainly includes the health problems of an area.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	30	answer	3	It is necessary to directly contact the local population and local actors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	31	question	-	According to the asset-based community health model, what would you say are the elements that determine what an asset in health is ?: (Point out the INCORRECT response):
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	31	answer	0	Those that improve the capacity of people, populations and institutions to maintain and sustain health and well-being.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	31	answer	1	Those who can act at the individual, family or community level as protective elements to counteract stress situations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	31	answer	2	Those factors that are defined by the health professional from the health center.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	31	answer	3	Those factors that imply a change in the view of populations and institutions to the context and focus on what improves health.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	32	question	-	It would be a health promotion strategy:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	32	answer	0	Installation of condom vending machines in the Metro network and transport interchanges.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	32	answer	1	Equipment and training of professionals for the expansion of congenital diseases to be included in screening tests.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	32	answer	2	Creation of integration forums and coexistence tables in areas at risk of exclusion.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	32	answer	3	Workshop on accidents in the elderly population, for its execution in the health center, that updates and favors reflection on injuries and facilitates the training of skills.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	33	question	-	The term equity in health means:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	33	answer	0	That it is necessary to invest in health technology in the different autonomous communities, as we are told in the Strategy of the Ministry of Health to address social inequalities.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	33	answer	1	That no person should be at a disadvantage to develop their potential.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	33	answer	2	That there should be the same number of health centers per Autonomous Community.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	33	answer	3	That all people have health care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	34	question	-	What is the definition of Melena ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	34	answer	0	Emission of red blood through the anal sphincter, usually originated in the lower part of the digestive tract.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	34	answer	1	It is the presence of red blood in the stool, not modified by the action of digestive enzymes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	34	answer	2	Emission through the anus of digested blood. Sticky stools and a characteristic foul odor that usually come from the upper digestive tract.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	34	answer	3	Vomiting of blood or clots from the upper part of the digestive tract.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	35	question	-	The agents involved in a community participation process are three (indicate the correct answer):
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	35	answer	0	Services that include technicians and professionals, citizenship and administration.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	35	answer	1	Professionals of Social Work, Medicine and Nursing.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	35	answer	2	Politicians, health personnel and education personnel.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	35	answer	3	Health personnel, personnel of the educational field and personnel of the social sector.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	36	question	-	Health promotion is understood as:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	36	answer	0	A strategy that has several elements comprising in an integrated manner several programs aimed at populations for general health.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	36	answer	1	Set of instruments and decisions of a certain society that assigns social functions and at the same time resources to reach a health goal of a population.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	36	answer	2	Global political and social process aimed at increasing people's control over the determinants of health.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	36	answer	3	Measures designed not only to prevent the onset of the disease, such as the reduction of risk factors, but also to stop its progress and mitigate its consequences once established.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	37	question	-	The declaration of JAKARTA identifies as a priority in the work in health promotion:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	37	answer	0	Increase the capacity of the community and the empowerment of individuals.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	37	answer	1	Reorient public services.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	37	answer	2	Develop personal skills
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	37	answer	3	Promote the concept of primary care in all countries.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	38	question	-	A group education technique is applied to the development of diabetes knowledge in a group of 40 people who suffer from this disease. The goal is for the whole to handle a considerable amount of information in a short time, analyze it, synthesize it and share it as a team. At first, each of the members of the teams addresses the part of the assigned material (theory and practice). Everyone has the responsibility to learn the subject. After a new team is formed and each of the members of the previous teams assumes the responsibility to teach their new colleagues the topic learned in the first moment. At the end of the application of the technique, the entire population must handle the contents of the class. What is the name of this group educational technique ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	38	answer	0	Phillips 8/8.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	38	answer	1	Grating.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	38	answer	2	Bronfenbrenner technique.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	38	answer	3	Delphi technique.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	39	question	-	In a Health Center, an intervention in Health Education has been carried out with 15 patients, aimed at reducing the prevalence of anxiety disorders. The evaluators analyzed the time that each session lasted, as well as the degree of participation. We can say that an evaluation has been carried out:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	39	answer	0	Impact evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	39	answer	1	Outcome evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	39	answer	2	Process evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	39	answer	3	Implementation evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	40	question	-	A person goes to our Primary Care office to see what diet to follow, says he has bought a book on dietary advice for months. He has decided that he wants to start losing weight already. In which phase is it found according to the Stages of Change or Transtheoretical Model ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	40	answer	0	Precontemplation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	40	answer	1	Contemplation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	40	answer	2	Preparation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	40	answer	3	Action.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	41	question	-	A person has Type 2 Diabetes for ten years. He is currently being treated with oral medication, but his disease is getting worse, so the administration of subcutaneous insulin is considered. She says that she will not be able to get punctured, she says that her mother was also diabetic, she tried and could not. Indicate what behavioral determinant (to inject insulin) appears in this case, according to the model of Health Beliefs:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	41	answer	0	Negative attitude.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	41	answer	1	Social influence.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	41	answer	2	Social pressure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	41	answer	3	Self-control or self-efficacy
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	42	question	-	According to the definition provided by the radical model of Health Education, what people would be appropriate to carry out the design of this Health Education program ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	42	answer	0	Only the managers, since only they can impose organizational measures.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	42	answer	1	The whole population as a whole.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	42	answer	2	Only the managers, since they have control over the entire process and can carry a proper evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	42	answer	3	Only health professionals, since it is a question that affects health.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	43	question	-	In the context of primary care consultation, the main difficulties in identifying gender violence by the professional are (point out the INCORRECT response):
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	43	answer	0	Being immersed in the same process of sexist socialization as the rest of society.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	43	answer	1	Fundamentally biologicist training (not addressing psychosocial problems).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	43	answer	2	Distrust in the health system.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	43	answer	3	Scarce training in communication skills in the clinical interview.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	44	question	-	A primary care doctor visits a mother with her 13-year-old son who refers to discontinuous sleep, with night awakenings and not feeling rested. After the assessment, the nurse identifies a sleep pattern disorder and makes a series of general recommendations for the family and the adolescent himself. Point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	44	answer	0	You have to practice regular physical exercise, especially in the last third of the afternoon. The tiredness and the endorphins secreted during it, improve the conciliation of sleep.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	44	answer	1	It is important for the family to have information about the changes in adolescence, especially about the normal delay of the onset of sleep and the alterations that occur in sleep using mobile phones, the Internet ... immediately before going to bed.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	44	answer	2	Try to prevent the young person from compensating for the accumulated sleep deficit during the week with an increase in sleep hours on weekends, beyond what is reasonable (a couple of hours).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	44	answer	3	If you nap nap, it should be short, and early in the afternoon.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	45	question	-	A 47-year-old man with overweight, sedentary lifestyle and smoker of 10 cigars / day comes to the demand for nursing in primary care. Among the recommendations for the prevention of cardiovascular disease include:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	45	answer	0	Advise and support the abandonment of tobacco, make dietary changes that include hypocaloric diet to reach normal weight and 30 minutes of moderate physical activity a day.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	45	answer	1	It is enough to advise smoking cessation and offer support in the process since there is no cardiovascular disease and there is no obesity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	45	answer	2	Recommend at least 30 minutes of intense physical activity per day.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	45	answer	3	The intake of fats should be reduced to 5% of the total caloric intake.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	46	question	-	A 58-year-old woman was followed up in the primary care nursing consultation for the control of chronic diseases and the promotion of self-care, with a history of chronic venous insufficiency. She presented an ulcer in the lower distal third of the right leg for 3 months, preserved pulses, serous exudate and macerated periulceral skin. It has an Arm Ankle Index (ITB) of 0.9 What type of compression would you apply ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	46	answer	0	In spite of the symptoms, the ITB indicates that we are facing a severe ischemia in which compression is contraindicated.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	46	answer	1	The ITB indicates that we are facing a mixed ulcer, in which strong compression is contraindicated and compression of 20 mmHg can be performed under medical prescription.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	46	answer	2	The ITB is unnecessary. Symptoms show a venous ulcer that requires compression with a layer elastic bandage.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	46	answer	3	The ITB indicates that we are facing a venous ulcer in which the application of strong compression of 40 mm Hg is indicated by a multilayer bandage.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	47	question	-	A mother with her 5-year-old son comes to the primary care nursing consultation and we find that the vaccination status is inadequate. To begin the accelerated rescue immunization, we must bear in mind that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	47	answer	0	When in doubt, the potential harmful effects of an overvaccination will always be greater than the suffering of an avoidable disease.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	47	answer	1	It is not recommended to follow accelerated calendars or to combine the maximum of compatible antigens, since we would reduce the immune response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	47	answer	2	If the previous vaccination is known and documented, it will be necessary to restart the interrupted regimen, not being enough to administer the pending doses.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	47	answer	3	The goal is to reach the correct vaccination for their age, or reach, in any case, sufficient coverage in the shortest time possible, prioritizing the most preventable diseases of greater risk for the child at that time.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	48	question	-	The Portfolio of Common Services of the National Health System defines the diagnostic and therapeutic procedures accessible at the Primary Care level. Point out the procedures that are NOT considered basic diagnostic procedures:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	48	answer	0	Spirometry, maximum expiratory flow measurement and pulse oximetry.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	48	answer	1	Cardiovascular explorations: electrocardiography, oscillometry and / or Doppler.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	48	answer	2	Psychoaffective, social, morbidity and / or quality of life tests.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	48	answer	3	Pathological anatomy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	49	question	-	According to Royal Decree1093 / 2010, of 3 September, which approves the minimum data set of clinical reports in the National Health System, the data have a "minimum set" (CM) character when their presence is required in any report model defined by any health service. They are "recommendable" (R) when their presence or not in the reports, is at the discretion of each autonomous community. Indicate which of the following data is recommended (R) in the Data Set of the Nursing Care Report:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	49	answer	0	Additional information / Observations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	49	answer	1	Care protocols in which it is included.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	49	answer	2	Active evaluation
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	49	answer	3	Reason for Discharge / Nurse Derivation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	50	question	-	The ability of the patient to make decisions, the reports of the preferences about the treatment, the conflict between the patient and the family in terms of decision making, in which functional health pattern of Marjory Gordon are valued:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	50	answer	0	Cognitive-Perceptive.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	50	answer	1	Self-perception-Self-concept
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	50	answer	2	Role-Relations
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	50	answer	3	Values-Beliefs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	51	question	-	With respect to critical thinking, which of the following terms used by Richard Paul as characteristics of critical thinkers is INCORRECT. The critical thinkers are:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	51	answer	0	Humble.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	51	answer	1	Realistic
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	51	answer	2	Reagents
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	51	answer	3	Good communicators.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	52	question	-	When formulating the objectives in the Care Plan it is fundamental to formulate them:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	52	answer	0	In the form of nursing activities, to be able to verify with certainty their achievement, according to whether they have been carried out or not.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	52	answer	1	Using terms that indicate the changes the nurse intends to achieve, such as; facilitate, make capable, allow or similar verbs followed by the words to the patient.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	52	answer	2	In terms of responses from the person to whom the plan is directed.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	52	answer	3	Trying to get an objective to solve the maximum possible diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	53	question	-	Mrs. PH had a fall that caused fractures with displacement in two ribs. One month after this episode he goes to the clinic, he complains of pain when breathing. In the physical assessment, Nurse Fernandez identifies that this lady presents: a BMI of 30, superficial breathing with a respiratory rate of 24 rpm. Auscultation reveals reduced vesicular murmur in the right lung. She also notes that the patient has nasal flaring and breathes with pursed lips. After analyzing the data, Nurse Fernandez concludes that Mrs. PH has a breathing that does not provide adequate ventilation. Based on this information formulates the nursing diagnosis of:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	53	answer	0	Ineffective respiratory pattern r / c bone deformity and pain m / p alterations in respiratory depth and decreased ventilation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	53	answer	1	Ineffective health management r / c obesity m / p pain.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	53	answer	2	Anxiety related to shortness of breath r / c alterations in respiratory depth and decreased ventilation m / p bone deformity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	53	answer	3	Acute pain (thoracic) r / c cough secondary to pneumonia m / p nasal flaring and excess secretions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	54	question	-	One of the fundamental objectives of the NANDA, NOC and NIC classifications is to respond to the need to systematize the clinical nurse practice that is developed according to the Nursing Process. Starting from the fact that, because it is a process, all phases are interrelated, more significant relationships can be established between each of the classifications and the different phases. Of those established below, it is correct that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	54	answer	0	NANDA acquires greater meaning in the Planning phase.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	54	answer	1	The NOC Indicators are important, fundamentally, in the Valuation phase.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	54	answer	2	The NIC Activities acquire their maximum significance in the Evaluation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	54	answer	3	The NOC is more directly related to Planning.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	55	question	-	Hepatic encephalopathy is a complex neuropsychiatric syndrome characterized by disorders of mental state and neuromuscular function. It is classified into four grades depending on the neurological involvement. What is the definition that corresponds to grade II ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	55	answer	0	Agitation and stupor with responses to verbal stimuli, aggressive and uncontrollable behavior, intense flapping, muscle rigidity and hyperreflexia, language disorder.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	55	answer	1	Mild motor incoordination, alteration of sleep rhythm, bradypsychia, change of character.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	55	answer	2	Eat of variable depth, seizures and decerebrate posture.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	55	answer	3	Tempor-spatial disorientation, memory loss, lethargy, flapping tremor.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	56	question	-	Within the theoretical statements developed by Peplau, highlights:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	56	answer	0	The importance of the concepts of need, independence and dependence.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	56	answer	1	The meaning given to the levels established by the nurse in relation to the patient. Substitution, help, guidance, advice and accompaniment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	56	answer	2	The concept of conservation, which describes based on the principles of: Energy and structural integrity, personal and social.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	56	answer	3	The nurse - patient interpersonal relationship, which divides into four phases: Guidance, identification, exploitation and resolution.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	57	question	-	According to Kérouac and collaborators, within the paradigm of categorization and from the orientation "to the disease", the person:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	57	answer	0	It has the physical, intellectual, emotional and spiritual components.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	57	answer	1	Orient care according to your priorities.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	57	answer	2	Does not participate in their care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	57	answer	3	You have the responsibility to change your situation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	58	question	-	Raile and Marriner, classify the theoretical works nurses in:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	58	answer	0	Philosophies, conceptual models, theories and intermediate theories.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	58	answer	1	Schools: Of the needs, the interaction, the desirable effects, the promotion of health, of the unitary human being and of caring.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	58	answer	2	Paradigms: Categorization, integration and transformation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	58	answer	3	Orientations: Ecologist, existentialist, cosmic and sociological.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	59	question	-	Within the gastroenteropancreatic tumors, what is known as the one that represents almost 70% of pancreatic endocrine tumors, which originates in the beta cells of the islets, are benign in the vast majority and are small and distributed throughout the pancreas ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	59	answer	0	Glucagonoma
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	59	answer	1	Gatrinoma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	59	answer	2	Insulinoma
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	59	answer	3	Vipoma
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	60	question	-	A 78-year-old patient with reduced mobility enters our internal medicine facility to study hyperthermia of unknown origin. At the end of the afternoon, we decided to change the sheets on the bed to improve the patient's comfort. The patient is in the supine position and we lift our head with our hands to remove the pillow, at which point we see that he flexes his knees and complains of pain. What could you tell us ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	60	answer	0	The patient has a positive Kerning sign, making us suspect meningeal irritation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	60	answer	1	The patient has a negative Brudzinski sign, making us suspect meningeal irritation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	60	answer	2	The patient has a positive Brudzinski sign, making us suspect meningeal irritation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	60	answer	3	The patient has a negative Kerning sign, making us suspect meningeal irritation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	61	question	-	A 25-year-old male patient, admitted to a meningioma, enters the neurology facility. Among the nursing care prescribed, we have to assess the level of awareness. What parameters should we assess ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	61	answer	0	Verbal response, eye opening and motor response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	61	answer	1	Sensory response, eye opening and motor response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	61	answer	2	Ocular opening, response to simple commands and motor response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	61	answer	3	Motor response, verbal response and coordinated movements.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	62	question	-	You are a nurse in a winter municipal swimming pool, after a swimming initiation class for adults, one of them, before starting the activity, falls to the ground and starts to convulse (his monitor says he is epileptic). What kind of care? at that time should NOT be done ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	62	answer	0	Protect the person from possible trauma and even from falling into the pool.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	62	answer	1	Avoid immobilizing the person by force during the epileptic crisis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	62	answer	2	Wait until you finish convulsing to call the emergency service, even if it is more than 5 minutes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	62	answer	3	Do not put any object in your mouth, even a May cannula (guedel).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	63	question	-	At our primary care clinic, a 72-year-old man who has been discharged from hospital after an ischemic stroke (ACVl), in the continuity of care report, indicates that the patient reports moderate dysphagia. Which of the following cares would NOT be recommended ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	63	answer	0	He has to eat in a relaxed and unhurried environment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	63	answer	1	You can put the television to entertain while eating.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	63	answer	2	You must place the patient to eat in a sitting position or if he is bedridden in Fowler.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	63	answer	3	Introduce small amounts in the mouth.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	64	question	-	A patient from the outpatient emergency department with moderate head trauma enters the critical care unit, who has been fitted with an intraventricular catheter, since we want to monitor the intracranial pressure (ICP). Which of the following cares would NOT be an adequate option to prevent this PIC from increasing ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	64	answer	0	Maintain a quiet environment free of stimuli.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	64	answer	1	Avoid actions that promote the Valsalva maneuver.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	64	answer	2	Try to make the person as calm as possible.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	64	answer	3	The patient's legs will be elevated in the supine position.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	65	question	-	According to the American Heart Association's latest recommendations on CPR, which of the following statements is NOT correct ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	65	answer	0	In the case of a cardiac arrest in an adult victim with an eyewitness and with immediate availability of an AED (Automatic External Defibrillator), it is reasonable to use the defibrillator as soon as possible.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	65	answer	1	In victims of cardiac arrest, it is reasonable for rescuers to apply a frequency of 100 to 120 compressions per minute.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	65	answer	2	Cardiopulmonary Extracorporeal Resuscitation can be considered an alternative to conventional cardiopulmonary resuscitation in certain patients when it is suspected that the cause of cardiac arrest could be reversible.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	65	answer	3	The use of mechanical thoracic compression devices against chest compressions in patients with cardiac arrest is strongly recommended.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	66	question	-	Of the factors listed below that favor the appearance of kidney stones, one is NOT correct:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	66	answer	0	Sedentary lifestyle
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	66	answer	1	Hereditary cystinuria.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	66	answer	2	Drop or prophylactic treatment of it.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	66	answer	3	Wet climates that increase fluid retention.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	67	question	-	Indicate which of the following characteristics does NOT belong to moderate (or persistent moderate) asthma:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	67	answer	0	It presents symptoms daily.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	67	answer	1	Nocturnal symptoms more than once a week.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	67	answer	2	Daily use of rescue medication (frequently β2 agonists).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	67	answer	3	Presents a FEV between 50% to 70% of the theoretical value.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	68	question	-	A patient enters our nursing consultation accompanied by a family member holding his arm, seems to walk with a broad, irregular and insecure base, as if he could not keep his balance well, with difficulty in coordinating the steps, resulting in an unstable wandering. What type of gear could we say that this patient has ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	68	answer	0	March with "fallen foot".
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	68	answer	1	March of the "lacunares".
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	68	answer	2	March "spastic".
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	68	answer	3	March "ataxic".
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	69	question	-	Which of the following opioid drugs is NOT considered a pure agonist ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	69	answer	0	Morphine.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	69	answer	1	Tramadol
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	69	answer	2	Fentanyl
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	69	answer	3	Pentazocine
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	70	question	-	María, 81 years old, is the main caretaker of her husband for 3 years. A few months ago when going to his home, we identified a diagnosis of "Low situational self-esteem". Among all the activities we can do, which would be more appropriate to help Maria overcome this situation ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	70	answer	0	Promote the learning of the necessary techniques for the care of the dependent person.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	70	answer	1	Assess both the physical and psychological symptoms and refer to medical consultation for prescription of pharmacological treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	70	answer	2	Insist on the importance of taking time for your own care and help find alternatives to share time with friends and carry out leisure activities.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	70	answer	3	Facilitate knowledge and skills on basic self-care actions for daily life activities.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	71	question	-	The functions of the Triage Box are several, EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	71	answer	0	Classification of patients in order to prioritize urgent care according to its severity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	71	answer	1	Determine the time of attention and the most appropriate resource in each case.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	71	answer	2	Specify the medical diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	71	answer	3	Allow the simultaneous work of two professionals in situation of peak demand for care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	72	question	-	When facing a victim of a fire, what is the first step to be taken ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	72	answer	0	Separate and / or protect the victim from thermal aggression.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	72	answer	1	Perform a meticulous physical exploration.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	72	answer	2	Start the contribution of liquids.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	72	answer	3	Secure the airway.
