Cuaderno_2016_1_E	77	answer	3	Adrenalin.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	78	question	-	Within the classification TNM (Tumor, Ganglion [Node], Metastasis). What would indicate the classification T1N0M0:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	78	answer	0	There is no evidence of a primary tumor.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	78	answer	1	There is involvement of regional lymph nodes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	78	answer	2	There is distant metastasis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	78	answer	3	There is no distant metastasis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	79	question	-	What is the symptomatic NO pharmacological treatment of dyspnea in advanced cancer ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	79	answer	0	Corticosteroids
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	79	answer	1	Ensure there is fresh air with sufficient humidity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	79	answer	2	Do not apply relaxation techniques to reduce anxiety, since these would increase dyspnea.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	79	answer	3	Opiates
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	80	question	-	What chemotherapeutic drug belongs to the antimetabolite group ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	80	answer	0	Cyclophosphamide
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	80	answer	1	Doxorubicin
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	80	answer	2	Anastrozole
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	80	answer	3	5-Fluorouracil.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	81	question	-	A patient reports xerostomia after receiving chemotherapy: Which drugs favor the secretion of saliva ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	81	answer	0	Pilocarpine.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	81	answer	1	Megrestol
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	81	answer	2	Metoclopramide.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	81	answer	3	Mirtazapine
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	82	question	-	What recommendations would we give to a patient who presents with xerostomia after receiving chemotherapy ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	82	answer	0	Chew acidic gum without sugar or pieces of natural pineapple.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	82	answer	1	Take hot drinks.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	82	answer	2	Restrict fluid intake.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	82	answer	3	Avoid taking juices.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	83	question	-	Among the causes of upper gastrointestinal bleeding not secondary to portal hypertension is NOT found:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	83	answer	0	Peptic ulcer.
