Cuaderno_2016_1_E	84	answer	1	Hepatic encephalopathy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	84	answer	2	Diarrhea.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	84	answer	3	Jaundice.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	85	question	-	The pattern of elimination is altered in patients diagnosed with colon cancer. Point out the NO correct answer:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	85	answer	0	It can also refer to rectal bleeding and a sensation of a straight rectum.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	85	answer	1	The patient maintains a normal intestinal rhythm.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	85	answer	2	Usually the size of the stools is decreased (pencil or ribbon shape)
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	85	answer	3	The patient refers changes in the depositional rhythm, alternating periods of diarrhea and constipation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	86	question	-	Is the pancreas a secretion gland ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	86	answer	0	Mixed (endocrine and exocrine).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	86	answer	1	Exocrine
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	86	answer	2	It is not a secretory gland.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	86	answer	3	Endocrine
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	87	question	-	Point out the constipation risk factor that is NOT correct:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	87	answer	0	Advanced age.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	87	answer	1	Male sex
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	87	answer	2	Dietary factors: low fiber intake, low caloric intake.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	87	answer	3	Others: drug use, depression, history of physical or sexual abuse.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	88	question	-	In a patient with neurological dysfunction after a traumatic brain injury and brain surgery, what is the typical position description of decortication ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	88	answer	0	Flexion of upper extremities, internal rotation of lower extremities and plantar flexion of the feet.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	88	answer	1	Extension of upper extremities, internal rotation of lower extremities and plantar extension of the feet.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	88	answer	2	Flexion of upper extremities, external rotation of lower extremities and plantar extension of the feet.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	88	answer	3	Extension of upper extremities, external rotation of lower extremities and plantar extension of the feet.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	89	question	-	Which of the following actions could trigger a picture of autonomic dysreflexia in spinal injured patients ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	89	answer	0	Venipuncture to obtain a blood sample.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	89	answer	1	Elevation of upper limbs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	89	answer	2	Painful administration of suppositories and / or enemas.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	89	answer	3	Oxygen therapy at high flow.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	90	question	-	Which of the following patient positions should be AVOIDED in case of increased intracranial pressure after brain surgery ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	90	answer	0	Supine position with raised head.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	90	answer	1	Trendelemburg position.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	90	answer	2	Position of Anti Trendelemburg.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	90	answer	3	Head in neutral position, centered on the midline.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	91	question	-	In a patient undergoing tibial skeletal traction, when should the traction weights be removed? Point out the correct option:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	91	answer	0	In the postural changes, in order to allow an adequate mobilization of the patient.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	91	answer	1	During the moments of cleanliness and hygiene of the patient, to facilitate the work of the professionals.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	91	answer	2	Skeletal traction weights should not be removed until the end of their prescription, unless a situation that jeopardizes the patient's integrity occurs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	91	answer	3	The weights can be removed when the patient must leave the room to undergo diagnostic imaging tests. In this case, the traction may be temporarily suspended.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	92	question	-	A patient who takes a week of absolute rest after pelvic surgery, begins to do isometric exercises of the lower limbs. In this situation, what nursing diagnosis do you think adequately addresses the situation of this patient ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	92	answer	0	Disorder of the personal identity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	92	answer	1	Decay of skin integrity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	92	answer	2	Body image disorder.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	92	answer	3	Risk of intolerance to activity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	93	question	-	One of the risks associated with intramedullary osteosynthesis surgery is pulmonary fat embolism, which of the following signs would alert you to the appearance of such a picture ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	93	answer	0	Increase in the level of consciousness.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	93	answer	1	Petechiae in the anterior thoracic region and neck.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	93	answer	2	Fever higher than 39.5ºC.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	93	answer	3	Polaquiuria.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	94	question	-	Which of the following interventions should AVOID in the care of a patient with compartment syndrome in his left forearm ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	94	answer	0	Application of local ice and elevation of the affected limb.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	94	answer	1	Evaluation of the distal capillary filling periodically.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	94	answer	2	Placement of the patient in the supine position.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	94	answer	3	Assessment of the presence of paresthesias by superficial palpation of the affected limb.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	95	question	-	In a patient undergoing total joint hip replacement surgery, which of the following recommendations is correct ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	95	answer	0	As an exercise that contributes to their rehabilitation, the patient must cross the operated leg and direct the knee to the thorax, several times a day.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	95	answer	1	It is necessary that the patient, when using the toilet, is as low as possible, in order that the operated hip is in a position inferior to the knee.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	95	answer	2	When in bed, the patient will use pillows or appropriate devices between the legs to maintain a light abduction of the operated limb.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	95	answer	3	As an element of early rehabilitation, the patient will exercise by flexing the hip operated more than 90 degrees, several times a day.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	96	question	-	What do we mean by the Health System ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	96	answer	0	Set of hospitals and health centers that make up the public health network.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	96	answer	1	Joint public and private institutions directly involved in health care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	96	answer	2	Set of establishments and health professionals responsible for the healing of individuals.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	96	answer	3	Public structural model that covers the health needs of the population.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	97	question	-	What is the permanent organ of communication and information between the different health services and with the central administration of the State currently in Spain ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	97	answer	0	The Health Areas.
