Cuaderno_2016_1_E	97	answer	2	The Interterritorial Council of the National Health System.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	97	answer	3	The Regional Health Council of the Spanish State.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	98	question	-	What is a budget ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	98	answer	0	Plan for the allocation of resources and a means of control so that the results fit the projects.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	98	answer	1	It is the balance between direct and indirect costs and income.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	98	answer	2	Economic program to be taken into account in strategic planning.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	98	answer	3	Process of allocation of material resources to the different assistance programs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	99	question	-	According to Avedis Donabedian, what are the elements of health care to focus the evaluation of quality ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	99	answer	0	The results, the strategy and the processes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	99	answer	1	The structure, the processes and the interventions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	99	answer	2	The process, the result and the criteria.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	99	answer	3	The structure, the process and the result.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	100	question	-	Strategic planning, with respect to time, is it planning ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	100	answer	0	In the medium term.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	100	answer	1	Long-term.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	100	answer	2	Short term.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	100	answer	3	Without term.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	101	question	-	What is an Organigram ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	101	answer	0	A model of partial organizational structure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	101	answer	1	An indicator to measure the quality of assistance.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	101	answer	2	A strategic planning
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	101	answer	3	A chart that shows the relationships between the different parts of an organization.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	102	question	-	If we participate in a process of accreditation of a health center and point out that "There is a protocol for transferring patients to another organization to meet their needs for continuity of care" Are we referring to ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	102	answer	0	A standard
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	102	answer	1	An indicator
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	102	answer	2	One criterion
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	102	answer	3	An obligation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	103	question	-	How would you define the figure of nurse Case Manager ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	103	answer	0	Nurse that facilitates the participation of family members in the emotional and physical care of the patient.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	103	answer	1	Nurse who directs support groups to provide emotional support and health-related information to their members.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	103	answer	2	Nurse that facilitates the ability of a sick person to interact with others.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	103	answer	3	Nurse who coordinates the assistance and defense of individuals and populations in different contexts to reduce costs, reduce the use of resources, improve the quality of assistance and achieve the desired results.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	104	question	-	What are the Health Areas, according to the current Spanish legislation ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	104	answer	0	The set of establishments and health professionals responsible for providing health care to individuals.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	104	answer	1	The permanent organ of communication and information of the health professionals in its scope of action.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	104	answer	2	The fundamental structures of the health system, responsible for the unitary management of the centers and establishments of the Health Service of the Autonomous Community in their territorial demarcation and of the health services and health programs to be developed by them.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	104	answer	3	The geographical boundaries legally established where the health resources are located to provide specialized care.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	105	question	-	Of the following, which is NOT a complication associated with immobility in the elderly ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	105	answer	0	Protein anabolism.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	105	answer	1	Osteoporosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	105	answer	2	Urinary stasis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	105	answer	3	Atelectasis
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	106	question	-	The anatomical and physiological changes that occur as you age modify the pharmacokinetic characteristics of medications. Of the following, indicate what pharmacokinetic change will affect the elderly patient:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	106	answer	0	The renal excretion will be increased.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	106	answer	1	Decreases the volume of distribution of fat-soluble drugs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	106	answer	2	It decreases the metabolism of drugs with high extraction.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	106	answer	3	Increases the volume of distribution of water-soluble drugs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	107	question	-	Of the following scales of functional assessment, which of them will be indicated to assess the instrumental activities of daily life ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	107	answer	0	Katz Index.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	107	answer	1	Scale of physical disability of the Red Cross.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	107	answer	2	Barthel Index.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	107	answer	3	Scale of Lawton and Brody.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	108	question	-	Concepción, the main caretaker of her father with vascular dementia, goes to the nursing office, where she tells us that she feels less and less able to take care of her father, and that her social life has been greatly diminished since she takes care of him. Which of the following instruments would we use in order to assess the caregiver's burden ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	108	answer	0	Family health scale (APGAR).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	108	answer	1	Scale of evaluation of the intrafamilial relations (ERI).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	108	answer	2	Scale of evaluation of family functioning.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	108	answer	3	Scale of Zarit.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	109	question	-	Point out what change at the level of the sense organs is associated with the aging process:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	109	answer	0	Larger pupillary size
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	109	answer	1	Hypergeusia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	109	answer	2	Atrophy of the organ of Corti.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	109	answer	3	Hyperosmia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	110	question	-	Point out the correct statement regarding urinary incontinence:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	110	answer	0	Overflow incontinence affects men with benign prostatic hyperplasia to a greater extent.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	110	answer	1	Urgent or imperious incontinence has etiology in the weakness of the external sphincter.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	110	answer	2	Functional incontinence is characterized by mild loss of urine in the face of increased intra-abdominal pressure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	110	answer	3	Stress incontinence is characterized by large losses of urine.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	111	question	-	Which of the following is an instrument for the screening of patients with cognitive disorders ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	111	answer	0	Katz Index.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	111	answer	1	Pfeiffer questionnaire.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	111	answer	2	Karnofsky index.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	111	answer	3	Scale of Lawton and Brody.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	112	question	-	Point out the correct statement regarding pressure ulcers:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	112	answer	0	On the Norton scale, high scores indicate an increased risk of developing pressure ulcers.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	112	answer	1	Due to the classification of pressure ulcers of the European Pressure Ulcer Advisory Panel (EPUAP) and the National Pressure Ulcer Advisory Panel (NPUAP), category / stage I pressure ulcers are characterized by the presence of whitening erythema.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	112	answer	2	It has to perform the cure in humid environment (CAH), since the materials used have shown a better repair of the cutaneous integrity that the treatment in dry environment, besides being more cost-effective and better manage the exudate.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	112	answer	3	As a rule, and following the instructions of the European Pressure Ulcer Advisory Panel (EPUAP) and the National Pressure Ulcer Advisory Panel (NPUAP), the pressure ulcer should be cleaned with local antiseptics.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	113	question	-	Which of the following is NOT part of the criteria proposed by Fried et al. to define the syndrome of fragility ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	113	answer	0	Unintentional weight loss equivalent to 10 Kg, or 10% of body weight in the last year.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	113	answer	1	Slowness in the march.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	113	answer	2	Degree of low physical activity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	113	answer	3	Low energy and resistance.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	114	question	-	From the following scales, which one should be used to evaluate the pain of a critical patient under sedation and connected to mechanical ventilation ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	114	answer	0	Ramsay scale.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	114	answer	1	Visual analog scale.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	114	answer	2	Richmond Agitation Sedation Scale scale (RASS).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	114	answer	3	Campbell Scale.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	115	question	-	The most frequent location of cerebral aneurysms is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	115	answer	0	Anterior Communicating Artery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	115	answer	1	Internal Carotid Artery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	115	answer	2	Basilar Artery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	115	answer	3	Middle Cerebral Artery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	116	question	-	Which of the following activities should NOT be performed on a critical patient in a prone position ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	116	answer	0	Rotate the head and arms placement periodically, placing one arm on one side of the head, where you look at the face, and the other along the trunk.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	116	answer	1	Place the bed in the trendelemburg position to avoid facial and eye edema and facilitate tolerance to the diet.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	116	answer	2	Elevate the feet with pillows so that the ankle joint is at a 45º angle and the toes free of pressure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	116	answer	3	Check the correct alignment of the spine and lower limbs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	117	question	-	Before a patient with traumatic brain injury, what score on the Glasgow Coma Scale does it show if we observe that it emits inappropriate words, opens its eyes when speaking to it and makes a withdrawal response when applying a painful stimulus ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	117	answer	0	eleven.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	117	answer	1	10
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	117	answer	2	9
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	117	answer	3	8
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	118	question	-	As soon as the patient enters the Post-Anesthesia Care Unit (PACU), the PRIORITY assessment of the nurse is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	118	answer	0	Urinary excretion
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	118	answer	1	ECG monitoring.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	118	answer	2	Consciousness state.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	118	answer	3	Permeability of the airway and respiratory status.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	119	question	-	In preoperative care, the primary objectives in the interview with the patient are the following EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	119	answer	0	Obtain information on the patient's health.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	119	answer	1	Determine the patient's expectations about surgery and anesthesia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	119	answer	2	Determine if the patient's surgery should be performed as admitted, ambulatory or the same day of admission.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	119	answer	3	Assess the patient's emotional state and their preparation for surgery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	120	question	-	The pharyngeal cannulas:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	120	answer	0	They allow the isolation of the airway.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	120	answer	1	In the presence of craniofacial trauma, both nasal and oral can be used indistinctly.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	120	answer	2	There is a single universal size.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	120	answer	3	Oropharyngeal cannulas should not be used in conscious patients.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	121	question	-	With respect to sutures, which of the following statements is FALSE:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	121	answer	0	It must be taken into account that greater thickness does not always imply greater resistance; It will only be more resistant if it is the same material.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	121	answer	1	The minimum thickness of suture that allows to assume the tension of the procedure should be used. Each suture, depending on the material that composes it, will support greater or lesser stresses. The smaller the thickness, the smaller the tissue trauma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	121	answer	2	The resistance is measured according to the tension that the suture is able to withstand, after being knotted, before breaking.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	121	answer	3	The thickness of the suture is measured by a system of zeros. The suture with the smallest diameter is the one with the least number of zeros in its numbering.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	122	question	-	In the realization of an access to the intracranial space through a hole in the skull bone, the surgical position is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	122	answer	0	Patient in supine decubitus with support under the head (roller).
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	122	answer	1	Semisentado
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	122	answer	2	Patient in prone position on sled.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	122	answer	3	Mahometana
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	123	question	-	To prevent excess pressure in the tracheal capillaries, the pressure in the cuff of the tracheostomy tube should be:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	123	answer	0	Controlled every 2-3 days.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	123	answer	1	Less than 20 mmHg or 25 cm of water.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	123	answer	2	Greater than 30 mmHg or 35 cm of water.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	123	answer	3	Enough to fill the pilot balloon until it is in tension.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	124	question	-	Of the following, what is the correct statement to refer to the fast evacuation syndrome or Dumping syndrome ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	124	answer	0	Symptoms begin about two hours after meals, with cramps, urge to defecate and audible bowel sounds.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	124	answer	1	It affects one third of patients undergoing colon resection surgery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	124	answer	2	Entrapment of fluid in the intestinal lumen as a result of the arrival of a large amount of hypertonic fluid in the intestine.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	124	answer	3	It is the result of the surgical removal of a large portion of the small intestine.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	125	question	-	What is not a characteristic used in the assessment of second intention healing in a surgical wound ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	125	answer	0	Exudate or necrotic tissue.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	125	answer	1	Borders of the wound.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	125	answer	2	Type of suture
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	125	answer	3	Granulation tissue.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	126	question	-	During the postoperative period, the patient with an amputation should be instructed that the residual limb, after the first 24 hours, should not be routinely elevated because:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	126	answer	0	That position reduces the development of phantom pain.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	126	answer	1	The unnecessary movement of the limb can cause dehiscence of the wound.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	126	answer	2	Can promote contracture in flexion.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	126	answer	3	This position promotes the formation of clots at the site of the incision.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	127	question	-	There are several types of drainage. Within the aspiration or hypobaric is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	127	answer	0	Saratoga
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	127	answer	1	Kher.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	127	answer	2	Silastic.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	127	answer	3	Penrose.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	128	question	-	For the performance of Cardiac Surgery, an Extracorporeal Circuit is used, whose main function is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	128	answer	0	Replace cardiac, pulmonary and renal function.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	128	answer	1	Derive blood from the heart and lung to a machine that performs these functions and return it to the body.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	128	answer	2	Derive the blood from the lungs to the organism.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	128	answer	3	Perform the functions of external pacemaker.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	129	question	-	The blood from the lungs flows through the four pulmonary veins to:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	129	answer	0	Right atrium.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	129	answer	1	Left atrium.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	129	answer	2	Right ventricle.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	129	answer	3	Left ventricle.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	130	question	-	In Cardiac Surgery, Central Venous Pressure (PVC) monitoring determines:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	130	answer	0	The cardiac preload.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	130	answer	1	Pulmonary capillary pressure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	130	answer	2	Saturation Mixed Venosa.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	130	answer	3	The afterload of the Left Ventricle.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	131	question	-	In cardiovascular evaluation, the main causes of perioperative morbidity and mortality are:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	131	answer	0	Arterial Hypertension, Ischemic Heart Disease and Valvulopathies.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	131	answer	1	Congenital heart disease, Diabetes, Arterial Hypertension.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	131	answer	2	Arterial Hypertension, Coagulopathies, Valvulopathies.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	131	answer	3	Hypertension, Hyperlipidemias, Diabetes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	132	question	-	In which cardiac cavity, the coronary sinus empties:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	132	answer	0	Left atrium.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	132	answer	1	Right atrium.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	132	answer	2	Right ventricle.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	132	answer	3	Left ventricle.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	133	question	-	Regarding the Shock, point out the WRONG response:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	133	answer	0	In the anaphylactic Shock an increase of the cellular permeability takes place, producing edema.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	133	answer	1	In neurogenic Shock there is a loss of sympathetic tone, which produces peripheral vasoconstriction and severe hypotension.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	133	answer	2	Hypovolemic Shock occurs by a large decrease in the volume of circulating fluid that causes the metabolic needs of the body can not be satisfied.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	133	answer	3	Cardiogenic shock occurs when the heart can not produce adequate cardiac output to maintain the metabolic requirements of body tissues.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	134	question	-	Heat stroke is a systemic inflammatory response characterized by a body temperature:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	134	answer	0	Between 38ºC and 40ºC.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	134	answer	1	Greater than 40.6ºC.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	134	answer	2	Less than 40.6ºC.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	134	answer	3	38ºC.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	135	question	-	The presence of free hemoglobin in blood and urine collected at the beginning of a transfusion reaction is proof that a:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	135	answer	0	Acute hemolytic reaction.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	135	answer	1	Delayed hemolytic reaction.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	135	answer	2	Febrile reaction
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	135	answer	3	Transfusion reaction produced by plasma proteins.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	136	question	-	What is the operation of the infusion pumps based on ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	136	answer	0	In the gravity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	136	answer	1	In the supplied volume.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	136	answer	2	In the formation of the nursing team.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	136	answer	3	In its ability to calculate the dose to be infused.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	137	question	-	The Glasgow coma scale:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	137	answer	0	It is the sum of the result of the evaluation of 3 areas: eye opening, verbal response, motor response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	137	answer	1	It is the sum of the result of the evaluation of 3 areas: eye opening, verbal response, electrolyte levels.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	137	answer	2	It is the sum of the result of the evaluation of 3 areas: verbal response, motor response, cardiac response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	137	answer	3	It is the sum of the result of the evaluation of 3 areas: ocular opening, parenchymal response, motor response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	138	question	-	The administration of insulin in patients with diabetes Mellitus type 1:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	138	answer	0	It should always be done by a nursing professional.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	138	answer	1	It can be done orally in some cases.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	138	answer	2	The patient can do it after being instructed.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	138	answer	3	It is not necessary to check the amount to be injected, it will always be the same.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	139	question	-	In acute myocardial infarction:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	139	answer	0	Pain is always the same, precordial and very intense.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	139	answer	1	If the patient lies down and remains at rest, the pain subsides.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	139	answer	2	In elderly or diabetic patients, a silent infarction can occur without pain.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	139	answer	3	Pain subsides with sublingual nitroglycerin.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	140	question	-	Mario G. has undergone surgery and has undergone an esophagectomy due to esophageal cancer. In the postoperative period, tolerance begins with a liquid diet and Mario begins to have intense pain, fever and dyspnea. The nursing staff knows that these symptoms are indicative of:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	140	answer	0	Intolerance to food.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	140	answer	1	The tumor has spread to the aorta.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	140	answer	2	There is a gastric perforation with the formation of a fistula towards the lung.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	140	answer	3	An extravasation of fluids and food to the mediastinum.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	141	question	-	Paula L. goes to the doctor for presenting a long time epigastric discomfort, regurgitation and heartburn after meals. After the studies and complementary tests, a hiatus hernia is diagnosed. After some time with medical treatment without improvement, he undergoes a surgical intervention (fundoplication) to correct this reflux. Which advice about nutritional treatment is NOT correct ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	141	answer	0	Take a diet low in fat and rich in protein, avoiding alcohol, caffeine, chocolate and mint.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	141	answer	1	Eat meals in small and frequent portions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	141	answer	2	Drink always natural orange, lemon and tomato juices.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	141	answer	3	Advise him to drink water after eating to clean the esophagus from residual food that may irritate the lining of the esophagus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	142	question	-	Mrs. Carmen C., 47 years old, carries a sigmoid colostomy. Which of the following recommendations on changing the device is NOT correct ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	142	answer	0	Remove feces with toilet paper and wash the periostomal skin with warm water and neutral soap (optional) and a wipe to clean the skin and stoma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	142	answer	1	Dry the area well, dabbing with a towel and evaluate the stoma and periostomal skin.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	142	answer	2	Apply the skin barrier (optional) and place the bag by pressing gently for 30 seconds to activate the adhesive.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	142	answer	3	The bag should be changed at most once a day to avoid damaging the periostomal skin.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	143	question	-	Margarita R. has been operated eight hours after a fracture of the tibia and has a plaster placed. She calls because she has a lot of pain despite having given her the painkiller one hour ago. The nurse suspects an acute compartment syndrome. What is NOT indicated ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	143	answer	0	Evaluate the edges of the plaster if it is damaging the skin and if it is too tight.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	143	answer	1	Give the scheduled analgesia and re-evaluate its effectiveness after one hour.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	143	answer	2	Make a neurovascular assessment at regular intervals by checking the temperature, movement and sensitivity and immediately notify the responsible physician in case of alterations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	143	answer	3	Apply ice and elevate the affected leg.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	144	question	-	Francisco R., 89, has a sprain on his right foot and a compressive bandage. He has been told to walk with a cane to avoid carrying too much weight on the affected foot. What is the correct way to use a cane ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	144	answer	0	With the cane in the left hand and the elbow slightly flexed, advance the cane and the right leg at the same time. Then overtake the left leg.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	144	answer	1	The most correct way is the one with which the patient is safer and develops better.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	144	answer	2	With the stick in the right hand and the elbow stretched, advance the cane and the right leg at the same time. Then overtake the left leg.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	144	answer	3	With the cane in the right hand and the elbow stretched, advance both feet at the same time supporting all the weight in the left foot.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	145	question	-	In a collective emergency, it must be clear that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	145	answer	0	Advanced medical posts will always be placed within the rescue zone.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	145	answer	1	The objective is not to ensure the survival of the affected population, but its evacuation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	145	answer	2	The priority of care will be the possibility of survival, not gravity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	145	answer	3	The existence of victims is not the main justification for their intervention.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	146	question	-	In caring for people who have mental health problems, it is important to take into account the sociocultural aspects that may influence the health / disease process due to:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	146	answer	0	The diagnosis of mental disorders in people of other cultures must be different from that of the rest of the patients.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	146	answer	1	Culture influences the expression, presentation, recognition and labeling of mental health and mental pathology.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	146	answer	2	The sociological characteristics of each group of individuals affect therapeutic malpractice.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	146	answer	3	Nurses from other cultures plan different therapeutic strategies.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	147	question	-	One of the most characteristic symptoms of Nervous Anorexia would be:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	147	answer	0	Bingeings hidden.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	147	answer	1	Binge followed by purges.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	147	answer	2	Distortion of the personal scheme.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	147	answer	3	Insomnia of conciliation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	148	question	-	In people with Schizophrenic Disorder the need to work and perform, shows manifestations of dependence mainly due to:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	148	answer	0	Abulia and anhedonia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	148	answer	1	Glossolalia and bizarre language.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	148	answer	2	Mystical delusions
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	148	answer	3	Somatization.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	149	question	-	The main clinical characteristic of OT (obsessive disorders) is the obsessive thoughts that are characterized by:
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	149	answer	0	Its unusual character, intruder and parasite, who experience themselves as strangers.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	149	answer	1	The unconscious control of automatic behaviors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	149	answer	2	Stereotyped behaviors that are repeated over and over again.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	149	answer	3	An accused and persistent fear, excessive, irrational and parasitic.
Cuaderno_2016_1_E	150	question	-	Among the symptoms that can occur in patients with a Depressive Disorder would be deliroid ideas that revolve around:
