Cuaderno_2016_1_M	20	question	-	Question linked to image nº21 A 65-year-old man with chronic renal insufficiency and hypertensive treatment with enalapril. He goes to the emergency room for general malaise and nausea without chest pain. Upon arrival at the hospital an ECG was performed, which is shown below. What test would you request to confirm the suspected diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	20	answer	0	Urgent coronary angiography.
