Cuaderno_2016_1_M	41	answer	0	Present a size greater than 70%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	41	answer	1	An increase in fibroblast growth factors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	41	answer	2	Decrease in metalloproteases and fibrolysins.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	41	answer	3	An increase in macrophages with a high content of lipid material.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	42	question	-	In renal physiology, one of these statements is true:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	42	answer	0	The loop segments of Henle reabsorb NaCl with an excess of water, an essential effect for the excretion of urine with osmolarity different from that of plasma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	42	answer	1	The reabsorption of bicarbonate in the nephron is mainly performed in the distal convoluted tubule.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	42	answer	2	The urinary excretion of Na and water is equal to the sum of the amount filtered through the glomeruli and the amount reabsorbed by the tubules.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	42	answer	3	Under normal conditions, 80% of the filtered glucose is reabsorbed in the proximal convoluted tubule and returned to the systemic circulation by the peritubular capillaries.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	43	question	-	When does the coronary blood flow of the left ventricle reach its maximum value?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	43	answer	0	At the beginning of diastole.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	43	answer	1	At the beginning of isovolumetric systole.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	43	answer	2	When the aortic pressure is maximum.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	43	answer	3	When the aortic blood flow is maximum.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	44	question	-	In the study of gastric secretion, which of the following tests is worthless?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	44	answer	0	Urease test.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	44	answer	1	Determination of pepsinogens.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	44	answer	2	Stimulation with pentagastrin.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	44	answer	3	Test of the fictitious food.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	45	question	-	A 19-year-old woman with primary amenorrhea is diagnosed with Turner syndrome by a cytogenetic study. What karyotype does it present?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	45	answer	0	47, XYY.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	45	answer	1	47, XXY.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	45	answer	2	45, X.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	45	answer	3	47, XXX.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	46	question	-	A 27-year-old woman goes to the genetic counseling clinic after having a child with Down syndrome. In the child, a trisomy 21 with translocation 21/21 inherited from the mother is identified. What would be the risk of recurrence of Down syndrome in the future children of this woman?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	46	answer	0	The risk of recurrence will be 10-15%, as in the rest of translocations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	46	answer	1	100% of viable fetuses will be born with Down syndrome.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	46	answer	2	The risk of recurrence will be very low (12%).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	46	answer	3	The risk of recurrence will be 50%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	47	question	-	A 3-year-old child referred for genetic consultation to assess psychomotor retardation, language delay and hyperactivity without significant dysmorphic features or associated malformations. He is the first child of a healthy, young and non-consanguineous couple. A maternal uncle has mental retardation and the maternal grandmother presented early ovarian failure. Which of the following diagnostic tests would be the most appropriate to establish the diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	47	answer	0	Genetic study of triplet expansion of the FMR1 gene.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	47	answer	1	Complete metabolic study.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	47	answer	2	High resolution karyotype
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	47	answer	3	Psychometric evaluation
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	48	question	-	Opsonins are molecules capable of recognizing structures on the surface of microorganisms and thus facilitate:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	48	answer	0	The lysis of said microorganisms.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	48	answer	1	Phagocytosis of said microorganisms.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	48	answer	2	Type I hypersensitivity reactions to said microorganisms.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	48	answer	3	The anergy of specific T cells against said microorganisms.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	49	question	-	Among the most important functions of secretory immunoglobulin A is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	49	answer	0	The defense of mucous membranes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	49	answer	1	The secondary response acquired in transplant.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	49	answer	2	The cytotoxic activity dependent on antibodies, by means of receptors for its constant fraction in the macrophage.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	49	answer	3	The cellular response T allogenic.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	50	question	-	Certain autoimmune diseases have been associated with genetic deficiencies of the complement system. Specifically, the deficiency in C4 has been associated with:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	50	answer	0	Systemic lupus erythematosus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	50	answer	1	Rheumatoid arthritis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	50	answer	2	Myasthenia gravis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	50	answer	3	Diabetes mellitus type 1.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	51	question	-	6-month-old girl, first daughter of a consanguineous Spanish couple with no family history of interest. He went to the emergency room in winter due to a high fever (39-40.5ºC) of three days of evolution, prostration, loss of appetite and marked respiratory distress. On examination, a significant delay in weight was observed, absence of thymic shadow on the chest radiograph, and a circulating lymphocyte level of 920 / mm3 was detected in the hemogram. Point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	51	answer	0	Agammaglobulinemia linked to the X chromosome should be suspected and the quantification of circulating B lymphocytes should be urgently requested.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	51	answer	1	It is a respiratory infection typical of the time of year, which requires antibiotic treatment without the need for additional tests.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	51	answer	2	A common variable immunodeficiency must be suspected and the ability to produce antibodies should be requested by in vitro functional assays.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	51	answer	3	A combined severe immunodeficiency should be suspected and the quantification of the T, B and NK lymphocyte subpopulations should be requested.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	52	question	-	80 year old patient from a nursing home. Presents sepsis of urinary origin that does not respond to empiric treatment with ceftriaxone. In the blood cultures and urocultures, E. coli resistant to cephalosporins grows. The laboratory informs us that it is a strain that produces beta-lactamases with an extended spectrum. Which antibiotic, among the following, should be used?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	52	answer	0	Ertapenem
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	52	answer	1	Amoxicillin clavulanic.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	52	answer	2	Piperacillin / Tazobactam
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	52	answer	3	Ciprofloxacin
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	53	question	-	A patient presents a lithogenic urinary infection due to the formation of struvite stones. Which of the following microorganisms is probably the causative agent of the infection?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	53	answer	0	Enterobacter aerogenes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	53	answer	1	Staphylococcus aureus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	53	answer	2	Yersinia enterocolitica.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	53	answer	3	Proteus mirabilis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	54	question	-	Prior to performing an organ transplant, the serological status (presence of antibodies) of both the donor and the possible recipient is systematically determined against certain microorganisms, including cytomegalovirus (CMV). In which of the following situations does the highest incidence of CMV disease occur in recipients of a solid organ transplant?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	54	answer	0	When both the donor and the recipient of the organ have positive serology against CMV.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	54	answer	1	When the donor has negative serology against CMV and the positive receptor.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	54	answer	2	When both the donor and the recipient of the organ have negative serology against CMV.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	54	answer	3	When the donor has positive serology against CMV and the negative receptor.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	55	question	-	In a patient infected with the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), antiretroviral treatment is initiated. For the evolutionary follow-up of the infection and control of the treatment, which of the following determinations is more useful:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	55	answer	0	Detection of antibodies by Western blot technique.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	55	answer	1	Detection of p24 antigen.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	55	answer	2	Quantification of viral load in plasma by genomic amplification techniques.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	55	answer	3	Detection of antibodies by ELISA technique.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	56	question	-	From the following list of antimicrobials, which one would you NOT choose as a sequential treatment in a patient who is going to be discharged from your home?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	56	answer	0	Amoxicillin clavulanic.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	56	answer	1	Clarithromycin
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	56	answer	2	Gentamicin
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	56	answer	3	Ciprofloxacin
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	57	question	-	A 35-year-old man is valued for having suffered a syncope. In the electrocardiogram, deep Q waves are observed and on auscultation, the presence of a systolic murmur in the low left sternal border is highlighted. What is your most likely diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	57	answer	0	Obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	57	answer	1	Mitral stenosis
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	57	answer	2	Aortic insufficiency
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	57	answer	3	Interauricular communication.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	58	question	-	The arterial bypass graft (coronary artery bypass) that presents a greater long-term patency (greater than 90% at 10 years after surgery) and, therefore, is used preferentially for coronary artery bypass surgery is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	58	answer	0	Autologous saphenous vein.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	58	answer	1	Autologous cephalic vein.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	58	answer	2	Thoracic or internal mammary artery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	58	answer	3	Radial artery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	59	question	-	In relation to the treatment of severe mitral regurgitation, indicate which of the following statements is FALSE:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	59	answer	0	Repair of the mitral valve maintains the function of the left ventricle to a greater degree than valve replacement.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	59	answer	1	Surgical treatment is indicated in asymptomatic patients when there is left ventricular dysfunction (left ventricular ejection fraction <60% and / or left ventricular end-systolic diameter> 40 mm).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	59	answer	2	Surgical treatment is indicated in symptomatic patients, especially above a 30% left ventricular ejection fraction.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	59	answer	3	Mitral valve repair has a surgical risk superior to mitral valve replacement surgery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	60	question	-	Among the factors associated with the appearance of cardiogenic shock in acute myocardial infarction, it is NOT found:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	60	answer	0	Monomorphic ventricular extrasystole.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	60	answer	1	History of arterial hypertension and / or diabetes mellitus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	60	answer	2	Advanced age.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	60	answer	3	History of previous myocardial infarction.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	61	question	-	A 47-year-old man with no history of interest is diagnosed with high blood pressure a year ago. He continues treatment with amlodipine 10 mg (1-0-0) and losartan / hydrochlorothiazide 100/25 mg (1-0-0), and performs a low sodium diet, with good adherence. Despite this, it has figures of PA 168/92 mmHg. What is the next step to make?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	61	answer	0	Add a fourth drug.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	61	answer	1	Increase the dose of any of the ones you are taking.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	61	answer	2	Perform ambulatory blood pressure monitoring (ABPM).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	61	answer	3	Conduct a study to rule out secondary arterial hypertension.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	62	question	-	A 76-year-old man diagnosed with heart failure, in chronic atrial fibrillation, with severe systolic dysfunction (ejection fraction 33%). Continues treatment with angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor, beta-blocker and thiazide diuretic. Despite this, it is symptomatic, in functional class II of the NYHA. What would be the attitude to follow?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	62	answer	0	I would add spironolactone.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	62	answer	1	I would discontinue beta-blocker treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	62	answer	2	I would add amiodarone to the treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	62	answer	3	I would add verapamil to the treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	63	question	-	Of the following diseases, one of them can be manifested with absence of jugular venous pulse:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	63	answer	0	Constrictive pericarditis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	63	answer	1	Superior vena cava syndrome.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	63	answer	2	Tricuspid insufficiency.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	63	answer	3	Heart failure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	64	question	-	A 25-year-old man, a military man by profession, is found in a coma with a temperature of 41ºC after vigorous physical exercise at noon on a hot day. His blood pressure despite the contribution of 3 liters of crystalloids is 80 mm Hg, with oliguria and lactate rise. His heart rate is 125 bpm with ECG showing a supraventricular tachycardia. In the analytical one highlights a prothrombin activity of 30% and INR of 3. Indicate the true answer:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	64	answer	0	The elevation of muscle enzymes is higher in the classic heat stroke than in heat stroke by exercise.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	64	answer	1	A lumbar puncture should be performed to diagnose the condition.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	64	answer	2	Digoxin must be administered to control the heart rate.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	64	answer	3	Peripheral vasoconstrictors should be avoided for the treatment of hypotension.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	65	question	-	The most important hemodynamic method in the diagnosis of chronic ischemia of the lower extremities is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	65	answer	0	Analysis of flow curves by Doppler velocimetry.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	65	answer	1	Segment measurement of pressures.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	65	answer	2	Valuation of the ankle-brachial index or Yao index.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	65	answer	3	Plethysmography at the distal level of the extremities.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	66	question	-	In relation to the clinical forms of erythema multiforme, all of the following statements are correct EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	66	answer	0	Minor forms are associated with Herpes simplex virus infection and are characterized by so-called target lesions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	66	answer	1	The major forms, or Stevens Johnson syndrome, are characterized by the absence of mucous membrane involvement.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	66	answer	2	Mucosal involvement in minor forms is observed in about 25% of cases and is limited to the oral mucosa.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	66	answer	3	The toxic epidermal necrolysis, characterized by the detachment of large areas of the skin, represents the most severe form of erythema multiforme major and is related to the intake of drugs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	67	question	-	A 43-year-old man consults for presenting a congenital nevus in his arm that in the last month has changed shape and color. Surgical resection of the lesion was performed and the anatomopathological diagnosis was as follows: melanoma with a non-ulcerated surface extension of 1.3 mm vertical invasion, 1 mitosis / mm2, which is 2 mm from the closest resection margin. In the physical examination regional lymph nodes are not palpated What is the attitude to follow next ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	67	answer	0	Perform a PET / CT to investigate if there are visceral metastases.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	67	answer	1	Perform extension of surgical margins to 1 cm and selective sentinel lymph node biopsy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	67	answer	2	Perform extension of surgical margins to 1 cm and axillary lymphadenectomy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	67	answer	3	It is only necessary to enlarge surgical margins to 2 cm and then periodic follow-up.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	68	question	-	A 45-year-old woman with a history of xerophthalmia and xerostomia, who presented in July 2014 due to an eruption of annular erythematous lesions, with more active edges, on the neckline and upper back for 15 days, coinciding with some vacation in Menorca. At the time of the examination we observed that some of the lesions tend to resolve without leaving a scar. It has good general condition and the rest of the physical examination is normal. What is the most likely diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	68	answer	0	Subacute lupus erythematosus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	68	answer	1	Tinea corporis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	68	answer	2	Cutaneous porphyria takes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	68	answer	3	Annular erythema centrifugal.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	69	question	-	Which of the following is NOT considered a general complication of laparoscopic access in abdominal surgery?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	69	answer	0	Hemorrhage of solid organs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	69	answer	1	Paralytic ileus.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	69	answer	2	Hernia in the abdominal access holes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	69	answer	3	Pneumomediastinum.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	70	question	-	A 53-year-old man with no history of interest presented pain in the right iliac fossa of 12 days of evolution. Her family doctor prescribed oral antibiotics and analgesia for suspected urine infection. Goes for persistence of pain and fever. On tomography, an appendicular plastron and an abscess of 7 centimeters are detected. Indicate the most appropriate treatment:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	70	answer	0	Urgent appendectomy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	70	answer	1	Antibiotherapy, percutaneous drainage of the collection and schedule appendectomy in 12 weeks.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	70	answer	2	Urgent intervention with right hemicolectomy and intestinal resection with drainage of abscess.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	70	answer	3	Nasogastric aspiration, iv fluid therapy, iv ertapenem and reevaluation in one week.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	71	question	-	An 83-year-old man, institutionalized, dependent for activities of daily living, diabetic and hypertensive, with no history of previous abdominal surgery. He goes to the emergency room due to abdominal distention, absence of gas and stool emission. During the examination, the abdomen is distended and tympanized, something painful, without peritonism. Hernias are not palpated. Normal analytics In the simple radiography an image in the abdomen is detected in "coffee grain in sigma". Indicate according to the diagnosis that you suspect the most correct attitude to follow of the following:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	71	answer	0	Perform abdominal CT for suspicion of diverticulitis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	71	answer	1	Urgent delivery of arteriography due to suspicion of mesenteric ischemia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	71	answer	2	Devolvulation by low digestive endoscopy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	71	answer	3	Infusion of neostigmine under hemodynamic control for Ogilvie syndrome.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	72	question	-	A 35-year-old man comes to the consultation referring to the appearance of a lump in the right inguinal region that does not produce any symptoms. A clinical examination suggests an inguinal hernia. All of the following statements are correct EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	72	answer	0	An ultrasound should be done to confirm the diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	72	answer	1	The physical examination should be performed both in the supine position and in the standing position.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	72	answer	2	It is highly probable that it is an indirect inguinal hernia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	72	answer	3	In the case of surgical treatment, the technique of choice would be a tension-free repair with a prosthetic mesh.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	73	question	-	A 55-year-old patient, with a 15-year history of ulcerative colitis, presented in a control colonoscopy a rectal cancer eight cm from the anal margin and moderate activity of his colitis, especially on the left side of the colon. It is staged as T2N0M0 after performing image tests. What is the correct intervention for your treatment?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	73	answer	0	Pantoctocolectomy with ileoanal reservoir and protection ileostomy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	73	answer	1	Anterior resection of rectum with protective lateral ileostomy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	73	answer	2	Abdominoperineal rectum amputation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	73	answer	3	External radiotherapy, and if there is good response, do a local surgery and maintain medical treatment of your inflammatory bowel disease.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	74	question	-	A 57-year-old man with rheumatoid arthritis undergoes regular treatment with corticosteroids. It is under study for presenting a picture of pain in the epigastrium, with occasional nausea and decreased appetite. In the analysis it presents: Hb 15 g / dL, Fe 55 ug / dL, PCR 3 mg / dL, ESR 42 mm at the first hour. Fibrogastroscopy: hiatus hernia of 3 cm and an ulcer at the level of the antrum, excavated, of 1 cm, with high and regular borders and with confluence of folds, which is biopsied. The histological study shows signs of acute inflammation and intestinal metaplasia. Normal abdominal CT What attitude, of those mentioned below, do you consider to be the most appropriate for the treatment of this patient?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	74	answer	0	Eradicating treatment of Helicobacter pylori.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	74	answer	1	Treatment with proton pump inhibitors and a control gastroscopy with biopsy at 8 weeks.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	74	answer	2	Suspend corticosteroids.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	74	answer	3	Surgical treatment (Billrroth I).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	75	question	-	A 63-year-old patient with a first-degree family history of colorectal cancer at 56 years of age. In his personal history, an episode of rectorrhagia secondary to the hemorrhoidal syndrome was highlighted 15 years ago, so a colonoscopy was performed that was normal and did not present rectal bleeding. Goes to the emergency room for a hematochezic episode. FC 120 bpm and BP 70/40 mmHg. The blood test shows a hemoglobin of 8 g / dL. Point out the INCORRECT response in regards to the management of this patient:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	75	answer	0	Even if hemodynamic stability is not achieved, it is necessary to insist on colon preparation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	75	answer	1	If the colonoscopy is normal, an upper digestive endoscopy can give the diagnosis in 10-15% of the cases.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	75	answer	2	Colonoscopy is the exploration with the best cost / effectiveness ratio for its safety, sensitivity and therapeutic potential.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	75	answer	3	The scintigraphy with Tc99m is of proven utility if a Meckel's diverticulum is suspected.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	76	question	-	A 63-year-old man with a history of stable alcoholic liver cirrhosis, who does not follow-up or treatment after living abroad, comes to his office. It does not present data of encephalopathy, there is moderate ascites to the exploration and in the analytic it presents a bilirubin of 1,8 mg / dL, an albumin of 3,4 g / dL and a prothrombin activity of 50% (Child-Pugh B- 8). It provides complementary tests performed two years ago: an abdominal ultrasound without ascites, portal vein of 15 mm in diameter and splenomegaly, as well as an oral endoscopy with the presence of grade IV esophageal varices, although it has not had known upper gastrointestinal bleeding to date. Which of the following statements do you think is LESS adequate for this patient?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	76	answer	0	Although it is stable and does not have fever or pain, a diagnostic paracentesis must be performed, since it is the first known episode of ascites.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	76	answer	1	A new ultrasound is indicated to rule out causes that may cause de novo ascites (portal vein thrombosis, hepatocarcinoma, etc.).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	76	answer	2	The initiation of treatment with non-cardioselective beta-blockers is indicated because it has large varicose veins, although there is never bleeding, since they prolong survival.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	76	answer	3	The initiation of diuretic therapy should be initiated in a short period of hospitalization to ensure that there is no renal failure or associated severe hyponatremia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	77	question	-	In the diagnosis of hepatocellular carcinoma, indicate the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	77	answer	0	The histological study is mandatory in all cases.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	77	answer	1	In cirrhotic patients, the diagnosis can be made using dynamic imaging techniques.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	77	answer	2	In cirrhotic patients, the diagnosis can be made with clinical suspicion and alpha fetoprotein levels greater than 100 ng / dL.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	77	answer	3	Arteriography is the only technique that reliably demonstrates the fundamental characteristic of this tumor, which is arterial hypervascularization.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	78	question	-	A 57-year-old man with alcoholic liver cirrhosis, abstinence of more than 6 years, has a Child's grade A liver function, grade II esophageal varices and good clinical status (ECOG 1). He is diagnosed with hepatocellular carcinoma in the right hepatic lobe, 8 cm in diameter and with thrombosis of the adjacent portal branch. The most indicated treatment is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	78	answer	0	Liver transplant
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	78	answer	1	Surgical resection
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	78	answer	2	Transarterial chemoembolization with drug-releasing microspheres (TACE-DEB).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	78	answer	3	Sorafenib.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	79	question	-	In the differential diagnosis of a patient with ascites, the sero-ascitic albumin gradient is very important. Which of the following clinical situations is NOT associated with a gradient greater than 1.1 g / dL?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	79	answer	0	Hepatic cirrhosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	79	answer	1	Peritoneal carcinomatosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	79	answer	2	Budd-Chiari syndrome
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	79	answer	3	Acute liver failure (fulminant hepatitis).
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	80	question	-	Given the clinical suspicion of intestinal bacterial overgrowth, all of the following statements are true EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	80	answer	0	The biopsy is the diagnostic test.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	80	answer	1	Presence of anemia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	80	answer	2	History of gastrointestinal surgery.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	80	answer	3	Presence of diarrhea.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	81	question	-	About celiac disease, which of the following statements is FALSE?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	81	answer	0	Serological studies for the diagnosis of celiac disease should be performed with the individual on a diet that includes gluten.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	81	answer	1	The most common cause of persistence of high serological titers is the lack of dietary compliance or the inadvertent intake of gluten.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	81	answer	2	The initial serological test for celiac disease screening is anti-transglutaminase IgA.
