Cuaderno_2016_1_M	142	answer	3	Tuberous sclerosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	143	question	-	A 62-year-old woman diagnosed with arterial hypertension treated with amlodipine 10 mg / day and osteoporosis established on denosumab 60 mg sc every 6 months. Consultation by a clinic of 4 months of evolution, consisting of general syndrome, fever of 38ºC and continuous pain in the right lumbar fossa. The examination shows a positive renal fist. An analytical sample showing leukocytes 14,000 / mm3 without left deviation is requested, with Hb 9 g / dL and a VSG of 82 mm at the first hour. The urinary sediment presents leukocyturia and the urine cytology shows abundant macrophages with a foamy appearance. Point out the most likely diagnosis:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	143	answer	0	Renal tuberculosis
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	143	answer	1	Xanthogranulomatous pyelonephritis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	143	answer	2	Kidney abscess
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	143	answer	3	Renal adenocarcinoma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	144	question	-	In a patient who presents with an asthma attack, which of the following findings is the one that indicates worse evolution?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	144	answer	0	Auscultatory silence.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	144	answer	1	Tachypnea.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	144	answer	2	Prolonged expiration.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	144	answer	3	Presence of wheezing on auscultation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	145	question	-	Among the following clinical situations described, indicate which one does NOT require a thoracic drainage as the treatment of choice:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	145	answer	0	Right primary spontaneous pneumothorax of 50% in a 30-year-old patient with a baseline saturation of 89% and pain on the right hemithorax.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	145	answer	1	A 59-year-old man with radiological semiology of veiling of the entire left hemithorax with contralateral mediastinal shift, hypotension of 70/40 mm Hg and heart rate of 120 beats per minute, after a traffic accident.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	145	answer	2	A 67-year-old patient with pulmonary adenocarcinoma of the distal third of the right main bronchus with extension over the intermediate bronchus with complete obstruction of the right lower lobe and middle lobe presenting dyspnea at high stress and radiological semiology of veiling of the lower third of the right hemithorax with ipsilateral mediastinal shift .
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	145	answer	3	A 45-year-old smoker with pneumococcal pneumonia of the left upper lobe and left basal hypophonosis on auscultation. Radiologically, ipsilateral pleural effusion occupying the lower third of the left hemithorax and diagnostic thoracocentesis with pH of the pleural fluid of 6.7.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	146	question	-	Regarding the mechanical ventilation mode with pressure support or PSV (acronym in English "Pressure-Support Ventilation") it is true that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	146	answer	0	The respiratory rate and the "tidal" volume or current are determined by the doctor.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	146	answer	1	The patient receives ventilatory assistance only when the ventilator detects an inspiratory effort.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	146	answer	2	The most frequent complication of this ventilatory mode is barotrauma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	146	answer	3	It is the most frequent mode used at the beginning of mechanical ventilation because it ensures minute volume in patients who do not breathe spontaneously.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	147	question	-	One of the following interventions has NOT been shown to influence the evolution of patients with COPD:
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	147	answer	0	Oxygen therapy in patients with chronic hypoxemia.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	147	answer	1	Volume reduction surgery in selected patients with emphysema.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	147	answer	2	Treatment with N-acetylcysteine.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	147	answer	3	Interruption of smoking.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	148	question	-	In the study of a patient with dyspnea, arterial blood gas analysis is performed. In this examination, a partial pressure of oxygen (PaO2) of 54 mmHg, a partial pressure of carbon dioxide (PaCO2) of 65 mmHg and an alveolar-arterial oxygen gradient of 14. In view of these results, which of The following diagnoses is more likely?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	148	answer	0	Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.
