Cuaderno_2016_1_M	212	answer	3	Anticomicials.
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	213	question	-	89-year-old woman diagnosed with a colon adenocarcinoma with liver metastases. He attended the consultation three weeks after the diagnosis with constipation of three days of evolution without nausea or vomiting. On clinical examination the abdomen is soft, depressible and with noises present. The patient takes 20 mg of morphine chloride day after diagnosis, with controlled abdominal pain. What do you consider to be the most appropriate therapeutic attitude?
Cuaderno_2016_1_M	213	answer	0	Lower doses of opioids in half.
