Cuaderno_2016_1_P	62	answer	3	Apraxias
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	63	question	-	The "temporary lagoon" is characterized because:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	63	answer	0	It is a pathological alteration of the typical memory in patients with Korsakoff Syndrome.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	63	answer	1	It is an alteration that occurs regardless of the ability level of the subject in the task you are doing.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	63	answer	2	There is no persistent spatio-temporal disorientation.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	63	answer	3	The subject registers the events that work as time markers, but later can not recover them.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	64	question	-	The dysmegalopsias are characterized because:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	64	answer	0	They are a form of visual hallucinations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	64	answer	1	They are pathological images called pseudoperceptions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	64	answer	2	They are alterations of the spectrum of megalomaniacal symptoms.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	64	answer	3	They are perceptive distortions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	65	question	-	Functional hallucinations are characterized because:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	65	answer	0	The stimuli coming from an external object are combined with a mental image giving rise to a false interpretation of reality.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	65	answer	1	There is an incorrect perception of an external stimulus, which is why some authors do not consider it as a true hallucination but as a special form of illusion / distortion.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	65	answer	2	They are morbid phenomena that only occur in populations with brain disorders.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	65	answer	3	A stimulus belonging to a sensory modality, which is correctly perceived, produces and overlaps an hallucination in the same sensory modality that appears and disappears with them.
