Cuaderno_2016_1_P	120	answer	1	Venlafaxine
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	120	answer	2	Imipramine
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	120	answer	3	Paroxetine
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	121	question	-	Which of the following theoretical contributions in the understanding of depression hypothesizes that it is due to specific deficits in self-observation, self-assessment and self-reinforcement ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	121	answer	0	Behavioral focus of Lewinsohn.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	121	answer	1	Interpersonal approach of Coyne.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	121	answer	2	Systemic procedural approach of Guidano.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	121	answer	3	Self-control approach of Rehm.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	122	question	-	Which of the following therapies for depression is based on the basic idea that patients present significant difficulties in recognizing the connection between their behavior and its consequences in the interpersonal context ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	122	answer	0	Behavioral Cognitive Analysis System of Psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	122	answer	1	Interpersonal therapy
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	122	answer	2	Psychodynamic psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	122	answer	3	Brief psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	123	question	-	What is the most commonly used drug for bipolar disorder ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	123	answer	0	Carbamazepine
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	123	answer	1	Lamotrigine
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	123	answer	2	Valproate.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	123	answer	3	Lithium.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	124	question	-	According to the reformulated theory of learned helplessness applied to depression, what two expectations does the person with depression have ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	124	answer	0	Expectations of low confidence and emotional control.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	124	answer	1	The expectations of damage and uncontrollability.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	124	answer	2	The expectations of low self-efficacy and result.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	124	answer	3	Expectations of sensitivity to anxiety and failure.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	125	question	-	One of the characteristics of behavioral dialectic therapy for borderline personality disorder, which differentiates it from classical cognitive behavioral therapy, is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	125	answer	0	The emphasis on the framing of the disorder from a systems perspective, in which the family is the key element.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	125	answer	1	The emphasis on the change of cognitive contents (eg cognitive distortions).
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	125	answer	2	The importance given to work with the behaviors that interfere in the therapy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	125	answer	3	The importance given to dysfunctional cognitive schemes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	126	question	-	The theoretical orientation of therapy based on mentalization for personality disorders is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	126	answer	0	Cognitive
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	126	answer	1	Psychodynamics
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	126	answer	2	Systemic
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	126	answer	3	Gestalt
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	127	question	-	One of the characteristics of the STEPPS program (Systems Training for Emotional Predictability and Problem Solving) for the treatment of personality disorders is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	127	answer	0	It is an individual treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	127	answer	1	The use of different formats: individual, group and telephone consultations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	127	answer	2	Its exclusively group format.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	127	answer	3	His emphasis on transfer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	128	question	-	What are the Personality Disorders classified in group B ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	128	answer	0	Antisocial, Narcissistic, Limit and Histrionic.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	128	answer	1	Narcissistic, Paranoid, Limit and Antisocial.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	128	answer	2	Histrionic, Limit, Schizoid and Paranoid.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	128	answer	3	Limit, Narcissistic, Schizoid and Paranoid.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	129	question	-	Which of these elements can put at risk the cognitive therapy of OCD ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	129	answer	0	Question dysfunctional beliefs instead of the content of obsessions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	129	answer	1	That the therapist becomes a source of reinsurance.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	129	answer	2	That the cognitive questioning be applied.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	129	answer	3	Avoid the primacy of authority arguments on the part of the therapist.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	130	question	-	When a traumatic event occurs, the greatest risk of chronification of symptoms occurs in cases in which:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	130	answer	0	Sleep disturbance occurs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	130	answer	1	People show affective dullness responses (emotional anesthesia).
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	130	answer	2	A greater hyperactivation is observed in the first moments.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	130	answer	3	They do not have self-help groups.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	131	question	-	In the treatment of Generalized Anxiety Disorder:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	131	answer	0	There are no differences between the results of Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy and benzodazepines.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	131	answer	1	In the treatment with benzodacepines there is a lower risk of relapse.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	131	answer	2	The combination of CognitiveConductual Therapy and benzodazepines brings considerable benefits to the results.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	131	answer	3	Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy is superior to the use of benzodazepines.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	132	question	-	In the field of treatments for phobic disorders, which is the intervention that has the most empirical support ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	132	answer	0	The techniques of exposure to phobic stimuli.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	132	answer	1	Psychoeducation regarding the unconscious causes of phobias.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	132	answer	2	The combined treatments (Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy + benzodazepines).
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	132	answer	3	The recognition of dysfunctional thoughts that keep phobias.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	133	question	-	In the metacognitive model of the psychological treatment of Wells Generalized Anxiety Disorder, the type 2 concern refers to:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	133	answer	0	The social concern.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	133	answer	1	The concern about the cognitive processes and events themselves.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	133	answer	2	The concern for physical sensations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	133	answer	3	The worry about traumatic events.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	134	question	-	In the cognitive therapy of OCD, with what type of obsessions is it more important to question the excessive importance given to thoughts and the fusion thought-action moral type and probabilistic type ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	134	answer	0	With the obsessions of pollution.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	134	answer	1	With reactive obsessions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	134	answer	2	With autogenous obsessions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	134	answer	3	With the obsessions of doubt.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	135	question	-	Interoceptive Exposure therapy is one of the components of psychological treatments of:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	135	answer	0	The Dysthymia
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	135	answer	1	Adaptive Disorders
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	135	answer	2	Obsessive-compulsive disorder
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	135	answer	3	The Panic and Agoraphobia Disorder.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	136	question	-	Regarding the Panic control program of the Barlow group, which of the following statements is CORRECT ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	136	answer	0	The Prevention with Response Prevention should only be applied if there is a Comorbid Obsessive Disorder.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	136	answer	1	The main element is the combination of psychological techniques such as Cognitive Restructuring together with pharmacological treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	136	answer	2	The cognitive work of identifying and challenging misinterpretations is the main component of this program.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	136	answer	3	The fact of systematically exposing the patient to interoceptive sensations similar to those experienced in their panic attacks is of central importance in this program.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	137	question	-	Currently, the most effective treatments for OCD are:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	137	answer	0	Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy and benzodazepines.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	137	answer	1	Exposure with response prevention and atypical neuroleptics.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	137	answer	2	New generation psychological therapies and noradrenergic antidepressants.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	137	answer	3	Exposure with response prevention, cognitive therapies and inhibitors of serotonin reuptake.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	138	question	-	In Posttraumatic Stress Disorder:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	138	answer	0	Both prolonged exposure and cognitive restructuring are equally effective.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	138	answer	1	Only cognitive restructuring is effective.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	138	answer	2	Jacobson's relaxation shows greater efficacy than cognitive restructuring.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	138	answer	3	Only brief exposure is effective due to the difficulty of processing the trauma.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	139	question	-	One of the problems associated with exposure treatment with OCD response prevention is that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	139	answer	0	Around 25% of patients do not adhere to treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	139	answer	1	It is less effective for obsessions with overt compulsions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	139	answer	2	The combination with pharmacological treatment worsens the result.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	139	answer	3	Relapse rates are greater than 50%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	140	question	-	The cognitive treatments of Social Phobia have among its main objectives:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	140	answer	0	The decrease in depressive rumination, since it is the main cause of social anxiety.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	140	answer	1	Eliminate negative expectations of loss of control over one's behavior.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	140	answer	2	The increase in motivation for change, especially affected in these patients.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	140	answer	3	Improve self-observation and self-records.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	141	question	-	Which of these statements referring to the extinction procedure is INCORRECT ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	141	answer	0	The extinction is faster the more evident is the contingency relation between the response we want to eliminate and its consequence.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	141	answer	1	The extinction is faster the less intense the reinforcements to which the response we want to eliminate is associated.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	141	answer	2	The extinction is slower the less effort it costs to emit the answer we want to eliminate.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	141	answer	3	Extinction is faster when the response to be eliminated has been subjected to an intermittent reinforcement program.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	142	question	-	What are the distinctive characteristics of "Contextual Therapies":
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	142	answer	0	The relevance that these therapies confer to the context, to the verbal behavior and to the functions of the behaviors rather than to their form.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	142	answer	1	The centrality granted by these therapies to the emotional context as the main causal factor of the problem behaviors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	142	answer	2	The consideration of variables so far not taken into account as motivations, interests, learning history and customer values, among other contextual variables.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	142	answer	3	The explicit rejection that these therapies manifest before the cognitive factors, which are considered as mere epiphenomena, independent of the context.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	143	question	-	In which of the following statements does the principle of Premack best be expressed ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	143	answer	0	In order to personalize and better generalize the learning to natural contexts it is very pertinent to use the activity as a reinforcer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	143	answer	1	It has to do with the principle of parsimony in the sense that it is better to use a primary reinforcement, such as the activity itself, than to resort to more complex ones.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	143	answer	2	It is a principle that establishes the component that precedes (Premack) to the maximum effectiveness of a reinforcer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	143	answer	3	Of the activities that an individual performs, the most likely can be used as the least likely reinforcer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	144	question	-	Which of the following statements is the CORRECT one regarding the response cost and the extinction as operative procedures for the reduction and / or elimination of a behavior? :
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	144	answer	0	The cost of response is a type of extinction that involves a way of eliminating the behavior by withdrawing a certain positive stimulation for the person.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	144	answer	1	Extinction is a type of special response cost in which the behavior is completely eliminated.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	144	answer	2	The cost of response involves the withdrawal of an appetitive stimulus, while extinction involves the withdrawal of stimuli that maintain a certain response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	144	answer	3	Extinction produces the complete disappearance of the response while the response cost always maintains the response at low rates.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	145	question	-	From the psychodynamic models, the corrective emotional experience (Alexander and French), is characterized by:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	145	answer	0	Re-experience situations from the past, avoiding the transfer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	145	answer	1	Relive a traumatic event again in all its intensity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	145	answer	2	Re-experience traumatic situations or deficit links and correct them through the transfer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	145	answer	3	A rational learning of the lived event, without emotional connection.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	146	question	-	Which of the following questions is an example of a "circular question" in Systemic Family Therapy ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	146	answer	0	How are you?
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	146	answer	1	Who cares more for their depression?
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	146	answer	2	When will you take charge of your life and look for a job?
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	146	answer	3	What is your name?
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	147	question	-	The Systematic Selection of Treatments (Beutler and Harwood, 2000) suggests that for a treatment to be more beneficial, the relationship between different variables of the patient and certain characteristics of the treatment must be taken into account. Which of the following characteristics of the treatment is related to the treatment? Patient resistance ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	147	answer	0	Directivity
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	147	answer	1	Duration.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	147	answer	2	Intensity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	147	answer	3	Format.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	148	question	-	According to Bordin, the agreement in objectives, the agreement in tasks and the positive emotional bond are the three components of:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	148	answer	0	The transference.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	148	answer	1	The therapeutic alliance
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	148	answer	2	The therapeutic relationship
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	148	answer	3	The therapeutic process
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	149	question	-	According to Lambert (1986, 1992), what is the percentage of patient change explained by the common factors / therapeutic relationship ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	149	answer	0	About 5%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	149	answer	1	About 15%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	149	answer	2	About 30%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	149	answer	3	About 70%.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	150	question	-	The introduction of a fading technique in a chip economy program would entail:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	150	answer	0	Decrease the time between the execution of the behavior and the delivery of the cards.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	150	answer	1	Decrease the number of chips needed to earn reinforcers.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	150	answer	2	Increase the time between execution of the behavior and delivery of the cards.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	150	answer	3	Deliver the cards at random immediately after the execution of the target behaviors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	151	question	-	What kind of cognitive error consists in attributing responsibility for external errors or events to oneself even though there is no basis for it ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	151	answer	0	Self-reference
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	151	answer	1	Personalization.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	151	answer	2	Absolutist thinking.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	151	answer	3	Self-attribution
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	152	question	-	According to Carl Rogers, what are the three components of the therapist that facilitate the therapeutic change of the patient ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	152	answer	0	Empathy, totality and commitment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	152	answer	1	Reflexivity, alliance and self-knowledge.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	152	answer	2	Empathy, authenticity and unconditional positive acceptance.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	152	answer	3	Reflexivity, acceptance and transfer.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	153	question	-	Which disease requires the daily contribution of insulin because the pancreatic beta cells do not secrete it or do it insufficiently, and it usually appears in childhood-adolescence ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	153	answer	0	Cystic fibrosis.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	153	answer	1	Type I diabetes
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	153	answer	2	Type II diabetes.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	153	answer	3	Pancreatitis
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	154	question	-	From the systemic perspective, the symptoms are considered:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	154	answer	0	An expression of systemic familial dysfunction.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	154	answer	1	An expression of family history.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	154	answer	2	An intrapsychic alteration.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	154	answer	3	An expression of the patient's internal conflict.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	155	question	-	What psychotherapeutic models consider that the symptomatic manifestation is the expression of an intrapsychic conflict of the individual ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	155	answer	0	Systemic models
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	155	answer	1	Psychodynamic models.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	155	answer	2	Behavioral models
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	155	answer	3	Integrative models
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	156	question	-	In modeling and with regard to retention processes, it can be stated that:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	156	answer	0	Cognitive practice (mentally repeating the sequence of learned behavior) is not effective.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	156	answer	1	Complex behaviors benefit more from repetition than simple behaviors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	156	answer	2	Cognitive repetition does not improve the perception of self-efficacy of the subject.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	156	answer	3	Cognitive repetition fatigates the subject and diminishes his persistence to carry out the task successfully.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	157	question	-	The basic characteristic of the alteration of thought called "perseveration" is:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	157	answer	0	The repetition in echo of the words or phrases of the interlocutor.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	157	answer	1	The repetition or persistent fixation of ideas or words.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	157	answer	2	A speech pattern in which the conclusions reached are not logically followed from the premises.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	157	answer	3	Accelerated slowing of the course of thought.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	158	question	-	Regarding the generalization of social skills learned in the treatment of schizophrenia, which statement is CORRECT ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	158	answer	0	The graduation of the stimuli must be fast.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	158	answer	1	You must work with the same interlocutors.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	158	answer	2	Do not overdo the trained behaviors to avoid overlearning.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	158	answer	3	The possible consequences of the emission of behaviors in the environment must be assessed.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	159	question	-	Decrease the high Expressed Emotion (Leff and Vaughn, 1989) is the goal of different family intervention programs in schizophrenia. Which of the following dimensions does NOT correspond to this construct of "Expressed Family Emotion" ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	159	answer	0	Hot.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	159	answer	1	Overemplication.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	159	answer	2	Ambivalence.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	159	answer	3	Hostility.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	160	question	-	Why is the Community Assertive Treatment (TAC) defined for people with severe mental disorder ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	160	answer	0	The patient is supported but not the family members or caregivers.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	160	answer	1	It is a model that puts the emphasis on medication.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	160	answer	2	It offers an individualized treatment, centered on the patient and his natural environment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	160	answer	3	It is complemented with other health services, since the team that develops the TAC does not cover 24 hours a day.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	161	question	-	In the cognitive rehabilitation of schizophrenia, which of the following statements is CORRECT ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	161	answer	0	It must begin with tasks that demand a high demand for attentional capacity.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	161	answer	1	The person should be trained in tasks that require a single type of response.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	161	answer	2	Programs that fit the general and abstract needs of the person should be used.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	161	answer	3	Metacognitive training should be performed.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	162	question	-	Focusing techniques to reduce the frequency and discomfort associated with auditory hallucinations include:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	162	answer	0	Divert the patient's attention from the form and physical characteristics of hallucinations, so as not to focus on these aspects.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	162	answer	1	Pay attention to the content of hallucinations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	162	answer	2	Avoid the beliefs and thoughts of the person regarding hallucinations.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	162	answer	3	Circumscribe the work exclusively to the framework of the clinical session, avoiding tasks between sessions.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	163	question	-	Of the following elements, which are characteristic of a typical social skills training session for the treatment of schizophrenia ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	163	answer	0	Identification of the problem, exposure in imagination, modeling and homework.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	163	answer	1	Identification of the problem, relaxation techniques, modeling and homework.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	163	answer	2	Identification of the problem, cognitive restructuring, modeling and homework.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	163	answer	3	Identification of the problem, behavior tests, modeling and homework.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	164	question	-	Cognitive-behavioral treatments for positive symptoms (hallucinations and delusions) are not very effective:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	164	answer	0	In acute phases.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	164	answer	1	In prodromal phase.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	164	answer	2	With patients taking psychodrugs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	164	answer	3	With patients in early intervention programs.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	165	question	-	Among the factors that have been shown to be associated with adherence to therapeutic treatments are NOT included:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	165	answer	0	The type of symptoms that characterize the disease suffered.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	165	answer	1	The complexity of the treatment of the pathology.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	165	answer	2	The empathic attitude on the part of the professional.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	165	answer	3	The sociodemographic variables of the patient.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	166	question	-	In the treatment of Anorexia Nervosa, what is the predictor of poor results that has shown the greatest consensus through the studies ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	166	answer	0	Its comorbidity with bulimia nervosa.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	166	answer	1	The late onset of anorexia nervosa.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	166	answer	2	The longest duration of the disease before going to treatment.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	166	answer	3	The low family support.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	167	question	-	What treatment is recommended for the unspecified eating disorder ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	167	answer	0	Guided self-help program.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	167	answer	1	Cognitive-behavioral therapy.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	167	answer	2	Interpersonal therapy
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	167	answer	3	The right treatment for the eating disorder that most closely resembles the eating disorder you are suffering from.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	168	question	-	In the cognitive-behavioral treatment for Fairburn bulimia nervosa, what is the main objective of the third phase ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	168	answer	0	The prevention of relapses.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	168	answer	1	The cognitive restructuring.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	168	answer	2	The modification of the environmental circumstances that perpetuate the disorder.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	168	answer	3	The establishment of self-registers for the maintenance of change.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	169	question	-	What is the main objective that is intended with the technique of exposure to keys (Cue Exposure Theory, CET) in the treatment of drug addiction ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	169	answer	0	That the person with problems of drug addiction knows to identify the situations of risk and thus to prevent the relapse.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	169	answer	1	It involves using signals to indicate when the skills acquired during the treatment period should be activated.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	169	answer	2	Train so that the person with problems of drug addiction can identify what is the main cause of their addictive disorder.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	169	answer	3	The aim is to achieve through exposure and extinction procedures that the person with problems of drug addiction reduces their reactivity to the keys or signals that are associated with the consequences of consumption.
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	170	question	-	One of the usual procedures in the treatment of gambling addiction is to motivate the player to be included in the list of self-excluded in bingos, casinos and online gambling, so that they can not access the premises or play online. What psychological procedure is based on self-exclusion ?:
Cuaderno_2016_1_P	170	answer	0	Stimulus control.
