Cuaderno_2017_1_E	41	answer	1	Pfeiffer test.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	41	answer	2	Barthel Index.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	41	answer	3	Mini-cognitive exam.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	42	question	-	Which of the following nursing care related to cardioversion is INCORRECT ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	42	answer	0	Prior to the procedure, the persistence of the arrhythmia to be treated will be confirmed by means of a recording of the electrocardiogram (ECG) with 12 leads, or with a rhythm strip.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	42	answer	1	Monitor the patient with the defibrillator monitor, selecting the electrocardiographic derivation that shows the R wave of greater amplitude (higher voltage), which allows to correctly detect the defibrillator in a SINC (synchronized) manner.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	42	answer	2	Ensure that the oxygen delivery to the patient is not interrupted during the shock.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	42	answer	3	After cardioversion, in the case of skin burns, silver sulfadiazine will be applied to them.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	43	question	-	Esther attends to perform the relevant occupational health examination in her company. When evaluating the electrocardiogram of her, we observed that each P wave is followed by a QRS complex, but with a prolonged PR interval of constant form (> 0.20 seconds). Given the evidence on the electrocardiogram, we can suspect that Esther has:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	43	answer	0	First degree atrioventricular block.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	43	answer	1	Second-degree atrioventricular block type Mobitz I.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	43	answer	2	Mobitz II second degree atrioventricular block.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	43	answer	3	Third-degree atrioventricular block.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	44	question	-	48-year-old male, married and with 2 children, businessman with high position, smoker until 5 years ago. In October 2017, he suffered an episode of loss of consciousness with cardiorespiratory arrest in his work. Your coworkers initiate basic CPR maneuvers while waiting for the Emergency Service. Upon arrival, 7 minutes later, the patient is unconscious, without pulse and while continuing with compressions and ventilations, is monitored by observing on the electrocardiogram (ECG) a ventricular fibrillation. Indicate which of the following measures would be correct to perform in this situation, first:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	44	answer	0	Continue with CPR for 2 minutes, with a rhythm of 30 compressions and 2 ventilations, and reevaluate the situation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	44	answer	1	Continue CPR while channeling a venous line and administer 300 mg of amiodarone.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	44	answer	2	Apply a discharge of 200 J Biphasic and immediately begin with compressions, with cycles of 30 compressions and 2 ventilations.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	44	answer	3	Apply a 360 J Monophasic shock and re-evaluate the rhythm while administering 1 mg of adrenaline.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	45	question	-	During ventricular contraction of the heart:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	45	answer	0	The tricuspid and mitral valves are open and the semilunar valves are closed.
