Cuaderno_2017_1_E	91	question	-	In a patient with intracranial hypertension and left ventricular drainage, what is the general measure, from the postural point of view, that would take to prevent and control an increase in intracranial pressure ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	91	answer	0	Keep the patient in the Trendelemburg position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	91	answer	1	Place the patient in the right lateral decubitus position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	91	answer	2	Place the patient with the head of the bed between 15 and 30 degrees above the horizontal.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	91	answer	3	Place the patient in the left lateral decubitus position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	92	question	-	Which of the following alterations can cause a driving deafness ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	92	answer	0	Tympanic perforation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	92	answer	1	Acoustic neuroma
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	92	answer	2	Ototoxic drugs.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	92	answer	3	Overexposure to noise.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	93	question	-	What is the proper order of administration of eye drops and artificial tears ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	93	answer	0	It is indistinct. Artificial tears can be applied before eye drops and vice versa.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	93	answer	1	Due to the level of viscosity, artificial tears will be administered before the eye drops.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	93	answer	2	Due to the level of viscosity, artificial tears will be administered after eye drops.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	93	answer	3	Artificial tears and eye drops should not be administered in a close manner over time.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	94	question	-	Faced with an eye accident in which chemical products are poured directly into the eye, which substances have more penetration power and potentially lead to more serious injuries ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	94	answer	0	Acid substances, with a very low pH.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	94	answer	1	The substances of alkaline character, with a very high pH.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	94	answer	2	Substances with neutral pH.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	94	answer	3	The power of penetration is not related to the acid, neutral or alkaline character of the substance that causes the accident.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	95	question	-	In patients with insomnia linked to restlessness and disorientation secondary to cognitive deficit, what should be the appropriate attitude in relation to the sleep pattern ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	95	answer	0	It is necessary to impose a specific sleep pattern, in any case.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	95	answer	1	If the patient sleeps during the day, but also during the night, it is not necessary to impose a specific sleep pattern.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	95	answer	2	It is not necessary to achieve a specific sleep pattern in patients with cognitive deficit. Over time, it will self-regulate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	95	answer	3	It is mandatory to respect your sleep moments, regardless of whether they occur during the day.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	96	question	-	Which of the following skin lesions occur with loss of sensitivity and anesthesia ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	96	answer	0	First degree epidermal burn.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	96	answer	1	Second degree superficial dermal burn.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	96	answer	2	Ulcer by pressure of degree II.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	96	answer	3	Subdermal burn of the third degree.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	97	question	-	In the care of a patient with pressure ulcers, which of the following methods of debridement is likely to injure the areas surrounding the ulcer if it is not used properly or circumscribed to the lesion ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	97	answer	0	Mechanical method, by irrigation of the wound.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	97	answer	1	Autolytic method, with wet healing on the lesion.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	97	answer	2	Enzymatic / chemical method.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	97	answer	3	Osmotic method.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	98	question	-	Which of the following is NOT an intravenous anesthetic ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	98	answer	0	Propofol
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	98	answer	1	Ketamine
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	98	answer	2	Halotano.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	98	answer	3	Etomidate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	99	question	-	The most common spaces to perform the epidural block will be:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	99	answer	0	Between T12-L1 and L1-L2.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	99	answer	1	Between L2-L3 and L3-L4.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	99	answer	2	Between T11-T12 and T12-L1.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	99	answer	3	Between L1-L2 and L2 L3.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	100	question	-	Due to the classification system of the American Society of Anesthesiologist (ASA) to estimate the anesthetic risk, a subject with poorly controlled Diabetes Mellitus type 1 will be classified as:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	100	answer	0	ASA I.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	100	answer	1	ASA II.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	100	answer	2	ASA III.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	100	answer	3	ASA IV.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	101	question	-	Indicate the INCORRECT statement in relation to the electric scalpel plate:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	101	answer	0	This should be placed in an area devoid of hair and scar tissue.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	101	answer	1	It must be firmly fixed to the skin, without allowing air space between the plate and the skin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	101	answer	2	The skin where it is placed must be perfectly dry.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	101	answer	3	It should be placed preferably in areas with bony prominences.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	102	question	-	Ismael, after suffering a hip fracture, is subjected to a hip hemiarthroplasty. Which of the following postural norms will be indicated to teach Ismael during his hospital stay:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	102	answer	0	In the bed you should stay with your legs as close together as possible and without rotating your feet externally.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	102	answer	1	When Ismael is going to get out of bed he will do it on the side of the operated extremity in order to avoid internal rotation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	102	answer	2	If Ishmael sits in an armchair, the height of the chair should allow the hip to be lower than the knees.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	102	answer	3	When it is necessary to lateralize Ismael for hygiene or change of bedding this will be placed on the operated side.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	103	question	-	Based on the "Clinical Practice Guideline on Perioperative Care in Major Abdominal Surgery" published by the Ministry of Health, Social Services and Equality, which of the following recommendations is considered INCORRECT based on the recommendations of the (USPSTF) US Preventive Services Task Force ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	103	answer	0	It is recommended to implement a perioperative care plan that encourages the early and progressive mobilization of the patient, with the removal of the bed on the same day of surgery, and the start of ambulation within the first 24 postoperative hours.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	103	answer	1	In patients who have undergone surgery for colorectal surgery, small bowel surgery or gynecological abdominal surgery, it is recommended to start the oral intake of liquids and solids as soon as possible, according to the tolerance of the patient, preferably within the first 24 hours after the intervention. surgical
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	103	answer	2	In non-diabetic patients who are going to be operated on for major elective abdominal surgery, the administration of 200 to 400 ml of a carbohydrate drink containing at least 50 g of glucose is recommended, up to 2 hours before surgery.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	103	answer	3	The use of sedative and / or anxiolytic premedication of intermediate or long action in patients undergoing major abdominal surgery is recommended.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	104	question	-	Indicate the INCORRECT statement in relation to malignant hyperthermia:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	104	answer	0	It is an autosomal recessive inherited disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	104	answer	1	Symptomatologically, it is characterized, in the short term, by the increase in the end-to-end carbon dioxide that does not respond to ventilation and the presence of tachypnea and tachycardia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	104	answer	2	The drug of choice in the treatment of malignant hyperthermia will be succinylcholine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	104	answer	3	If the disorder is not controlled, it will lead to myoglobinuria, thus observing the dark colored urine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	105	question	-	Evaristo has undergone mitral valve repair surgery. After three days in the Intensive Care Unit, she continues with mechanical ventilation in ventilatory pressure support mode (PS). We observed that the patient has a respiratory rate of 8 breaths per minute, evidencing a tidal volume of 245 ml. When extracting an arterial gasometry, a pH of 7.28, a PCO2 of 63 mm Hg and a HCO3 of 28 mEq / L are observed. Which of the following acid-base imbalances will our patient present ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	105	answer	0	Respiratory acidosis
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	105	answer	1	Respiratory alkalosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	105	answer	2	Metabolic acidosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	105	answer	3	Metabolic alkalosis
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	106	question	-	A woman undergoing breast reconstructive surgery 3 days ago, she continues to present severe vomiting and considerable diarrhea, and she tells us that she is "very weak", getting dizzy when she gets out of bed very quickly. On physical examination we observed an irregular pulse, for which an electrocardiogram was performed showing a flattened P wave, depression of the ST segment and the existence of a U wave. Given the exposed findings, we can suspect that the patient has:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	106	answer	0	Hypokalemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	106	answer	1	Hyponatremia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	106	answer	2	Hypercalcemia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	106	answer	3	Hyperphosphatemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	107	question	-	Indicate the correct statement in relation to the drainages:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	107	answer	0	Penrose drainage is an active drainage.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	107	answer	1	The use of the Kehr tube is common in bile duct surgeries.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	107	answer	2	The Jackson Pratt drainage only allows blood to be evacuated, unable to evacuate air.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	107	answer	3	The water seal in the thoracic drainage (Pleur-evac ®) facilitates the entry of outside air into the system during expiration.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	108	question	-	To maintain blood pressure there are two determinants:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	108	answer	0	Cardiac output (CO) and systemic vascular resistance (SVR).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	108	answer	1	Heart rate (HR) and body temperature (Tª).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	108	answer	2	Blood pressure (BP) and heart rate (HR).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	108	answer	3	The preload and the afterload.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	109	question	-	Cardiac output (GC) meets the following formula:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	109	answer	0	GC = FC (heart rate) x VE (left ventricular ejection volume).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	109	answer	1	GC = FC (heart rate) x VE (right ventricular ejection volume).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	109	answer	2	GC = TA (blood pressure) x VE (ejection volume of the left atrium).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	109	answer	3	GC = TA (blood pressure) x VE (ejection volume of the right atrium).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	110	question	-	The term Central Venous Pressure refers to:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	110	answer	0	The load or volume that distends the left ventricle before contraction or systole.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	110	answer	1	It is the blood pressure measured at the junction of the vena cava with the right atrium.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	110	answer	2	The load or volume that distends the left atrium before relaxation or diastole.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	110	answer	3	The load or volume that distends the right atrium before relaxation or diastole.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	111	question	-	The main cause of Mitral Stenosis is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	111	answer	0	Congenital disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	111	answer	1	Rheumatic disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	111	answer	2	Coronary heart disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	111	answer	3	Infectious disease
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	112	question	-	The triad of Virchow is constituted by:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	112	answer	0	Arterial stasis, Hypercoagulability, Lesions of the venous wall.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	112	answer	1	Venous stasis, Hypercoagulability, Lesions of the venous wall.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	112	answer	2	Hypertension, Hypocoagulability, injuries of the arterial wall.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	112	answer	3	Hypotension, Hypocoagulability, injuries of the arterial wall.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	113	question	-	Cardioversion is indicated in:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	113	answer	0	Treatment of acute myocardial infarction.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	113	answer	1	Treatment of complete AuricularVentricular Block.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	113	answer	2	Prophylactic treatment of some arrhythmias that can trigger Cardiorespiratory arrest (CRP) or that appear after it.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	113	answer	3	Treatment of Ventricular Fibrillation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	114	question	-	The surgical position in which the patient is placed with the thighs in abduction, the knees and hips flexed, and the feet are suspended with stirrups or legs that are fixed to the table of denominates:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	114	answer	0	Lithotomy position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	114	answer	1	Inverted Trendelemburg position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	114	answer	2	Kraske position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	114	answer	3	Sitting position.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	115	question	-	A local anesthetic is indicated in the treatment of ventricular arrhythmias, such as those resulting from an acute myocardial infarction, digital toxicity, cardiac surgery or cardiac catheterization. Is about:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	115	answer	0	Bupivacaine
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	115	answer	1	Lidocaine
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	115	answer	2	Mepivacaine
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	115	answer	3	Procaine
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	116	question	-	To avoid a neuromuscular block, administration of the aminoglycoside antibiotic gentamicin should be done:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	116	answer	0	In fast bolus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	116	answer	1	In intravenous infusion for a period of 30-60 minutes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	116	answer	2	In intravenous infusion between 5 and 10 minutes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	116	answer	3	In slow intravenous injection administered between 1 and 5 minutes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	117	question	-	In the prevention and treatment of postoperative nausea and vomiting in children and adults, an antagonist of type 3 serotonin receptors (5-HT3) is indicated. Is about:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	117	answer	0	Ondansetron.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	117	answer	1	Methylprednisolone
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	117	answer	2	Metoclopramide.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	117	answer	3	Domperidone
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	118	question	-	We have a patient in our care who has just arrived from a tumor resection surgery at the level of the temporal cerebral cortex. Which of the following cares should I NOT do ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	118	answer	0	Assess and record the level of consciousness using the Glasgow comma scale.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	118	answer	1	Observe and record the pupillary state and photomotor reflex.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	118	answer	2	Maintain proper ventilation and avoid hypoxemia, as this increases cerebral edema.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	118	answer	3	Perform routine aspirations to avoid accumulation of secretions, since they can later produce pneumonia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	119	question	-	The patient in bed 227 has just arrived from the operating room where a skeletal femur traction has been placed. Which of the following nursing care would NOT be adequate to perform in the immediate postoperative period ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	119	answer	0	Perform neurovascular evaluations frequently.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	119	answer	1	Evaluate the condition of the skin, in addition to the specific care of the nails or needles used in traction.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	119	answer	2	Assess the possibility of the appearance of pseudoarthrosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	119	answer	3	Assess the pain of the patient, and it may be necessary to administer analgesics more frequently.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	120	question	-	A newly operated cataract patient arrives at our resuscitation, in what position should the patient be placed to reduce intraocular pressure ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	120	answer	0	In semi-Fowler position on the healthy side.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	120	answer	1	In semi-Fowler position on the affected side.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	120	answer	2	Prone position with the head resting on the affected side.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	120	answer	3	Supine decubitus with the headboard at 0º.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	121	question	-	Of the different lesions on the skin, the pustule is characterized by:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	121	answer	0	Solid mass, prominent, palpable with a circumscribed edge.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	121	answer	1	Semisolid mass in the subcutaneous tissue or the dermis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	121	answer	2	Linear crack in the skin that extends beyond the epidermis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	121	answer	3	Vesicle or blister filled with purulent fluid.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	122	question	-	A patient who has had recurrent otitis externa comes to our nursing office. Which of the following preventive measures would you NOT recommend ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	122	answer	0	Protect the external auditory canal when you shower, wash your head or swim in the pool.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	122	answer	1	If you are diagnosed with otitis externa, avoid water sports for 7-10 days to allow the canal to heal.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	122	answer	2	Avoid scratching the external auditory canal with the nail.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	122	answer	3	The patient should clean the external auditory canal with cotton-tipped applicators (sticks).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	123	question	-	They have assigned him a quota of population in a Health Center, with a very old population. What prevalence of people with heart failure are likely to be found in people older than 70 ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	123	answer	0	Between 1 and 2l%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	123	answer	1	5%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	123	answer	2	7%
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	123	answer	3	Above 10%
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	124	question	-	In a home visit to a patient with heart failure, type 2 diabetes and dyslipidemia, when reviewing the patient's first aid kit, you find a series of drugs that the patient habitually consumes. Which of them poses a risk for the worsening of heart failure ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	124	answer	0	Metformin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	124	answer	1	Dexketoprofen
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	124	answer	2	Furosemide.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	124	answer	3	Carvedilol.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	125	question	-	Which of the following vaccines should be indicated in people with heart failure ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	125	answer	0	Hepatitis C.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	125	answer	1	Hepatitis B.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	125	answer	2	Pneumococcus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	125	answer	3	Chickenpox.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	126	question	-	Indicate which of the following statements is true in relation to the Social Determinants of Health:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	126	answer	0	The distribution of health problems in any population is usually random.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	126	answer	1	The fact that the disease and its biological and behavioral causes follow certain social patterns shows us that the individual determinants are influenced by more structural social determinants.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	126	answer	2	Social determinants in health are understood as unjust and avoidable differences in health among groups of populations defined socially, economically, demographically or geographically.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	126	answer	3	Empowerment consists of measures of redistribution of power favoring those who have more.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	127	question	-	According to the conceptual framework of the determinants of social inequalities in health, based on Solar and Irwin and Navarro, we can affirm that:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	127	answer	0	When the social class decreases, health improves, both expressed in perceived health and in an excess of mortality or morbidity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	127	answer	1	Inequalities only affect a small segment of the poorest population.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	127	answer	2	Inequalities are reproduced throughout the life cycle, the social class of the family where one is born, the level of studies acquired or occupation, generating unequal resources and opportunities throughout life.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	127	answer	3	The differences in health between men and women essentially respond to biological differences.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	128	question	-	Regarding the Hepatitis A vaccine, which of the following statements is NOT true:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	128	answer	0	The Hepatitis A vaccine will be indicated only to people older than 65 years.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	128	answer	1	The Hepatitis A vaccine is an inactivated virus vaccine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	128	answer	2	The Hepatitis A vaccine is administered in 2 doses, separating the 2nd dose between 6 to 12 months of the first.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	128	answer	3	The complete and correct vaccination of Hepatitis A confers protection of 9599%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	129	question	-	In which of these means will we NOT find Legionella ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	129	answer	0	Respirators and nebulizers.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	129	answer	1	SPA baths, thermal waters or showers.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	129	answer	2	Saltwater.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	129	answer	3	Cooling towers
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	130	question	-	Regarding HIV / AIDS, it is FALSE that:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	130	answer	0	In addition to vertical and horizontal transmission routes (blood or blood products and serosanguineous or genital fluids), some cases of transmission by arthropod vectors have now been documented.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	130	answer	1	In injecting drug users who share syringes, it is transmitted from microtransfusions of infected blood, when injected with contaminated equipment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	130	answer	2	Asymptomatic pregnant women, as well as those with elevated CD4 + lymphocyte counts, have a lower risk of HIV transmission.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	130	answer	3	The highest risk sexual practice is the genital-anal relationship between males, and the risk is significantly higher for the anal recipient than for the insertor.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	131	question	-	In relation to the tuberculin test (Mantoux) or Purified Protected Derivative (PPD) it is true that:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	131	answer	0	The reading (at 48-72 h.) Consists of measuring the diameter of the erythema.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	131	answer	1	It consists of a subcutaneous injection in the ventral forearm face of PPD (purified protein derivative).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	131	answer	2	In adults, a positive reaction (≥ 5 mm) usually indicates previous contact with the tubercle bacillus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	131	answer	3	In children, a positive reaction (≥ 1 mm) usually indicates tuberculous disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	132	question	-	Which of the following options is NOT a recommendation of physical activity for the adult population ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	132	answer	0	The long sedentary periods should be reduced.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	132	answer	1	Minimum aerobic activity of 150 minutes per week of moderate physical activity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	132	answer	2	It must be done in blocks of a minimum duration of 30 minutes, to have effects on health.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	132	answer	3	To obtain greater benefits, aerobic activity can be increased to 300 minutes of moderate or 150 minutes of vigorous to the week, or an equivalent combination of both.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	133	question	-	Which of the following risk factors for drug addiction is of a microsocial type ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	133	answer	0	Group pressure.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	133	answer	1	Sex.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	133	answer	2	Personality.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	133	answer	3	Availability of substances.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	134	question	-	According to the World Health Organization and according to scientific evidence, the threshold to consider alcohol risk consumption is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	134	answer	0	Less than 20 g / day in men and less than 12 g / day in women.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	134	answer	1	Regular consumption of 12 g / day in women and 20 g / day in men.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	134	answer	2	Regular consumption of 20-40 g / day in women and 40-60 g / day in men.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	134	answer	3	Regular consumption of 24 g / day in both men and women.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	135	question	-	Messages about healthy eating should be based on epidemiological evidence. Identify which of the following messages about healthy eating is FALSE:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	135	answer	0	Reduce total fat intake, especially saturated and trans fat.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	135	answer	1	Limit egg consumption, due to its high cholesterol content.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	135	answer	2	Promote the consumption of proteins of vegetable origin, instead of those of animal origin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	135	answer	3	Encourage the consumption of whole grain cereals, instead of refined grains.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	136	question	-	Risk reduction (or harm reduction) strategies aim to not eliminate the use of drugs, but to admit that their use is inevitable and, therefore, to try to reduce the harm. Indicate which of the following statements is NOT correct:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	136	answer	0	They are primary prevention measures and health promotion.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	136	answer	1	They include programs for the exchange of sterile syringes, safe sex, maintenance with opiates (methadone), etc.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	136	answer	2	Its drawback is that they give some legitimacy to the use of drugs, which can have adverse effects, especially on vulnerable groups.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	136	answer	3	The evaluation of the effectiveness of the interventions is carried out on rare occasions and without adequate methodological rigor.
