Cuaderno_2017_1_E	185	question	-	In the reviews of the child's health after 2 years, what findings should we consider of risk in relation to childhood obesity ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	185	answer	0	Increase in BMI less than or equal to 2 units / year.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	185	answer	1	Adipose bounce before age 5
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	185	answer	2	The body mass index greater than or equal to the 85th percentile is an indicator of obesity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	185	answer	3	The body mass index greater than or equal to the 90th percentile is an indicator of obesity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	186	question	-	Before a woman who expresses in consultation her desire for pregnancy, the nurse plans to inform and give advice on lifestyles. Point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	186	answer	0	In women who plan their pregnancy and who are not immunized against rubella, vaccination before pregnancy with MMR vaccine is suggested and precautions should be taken to avoid pregnancy during the 28 days following vaccination.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	186	answer	1	It is suggested to administer a daily routine supplementation with a multivitamin preparation to avoid neural tube defects.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	186	answer	2	It is suggested to routinely administer a daily iodine supplementation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	186	answer	3	In women who plan their pregnancy and who are not immunized against hepatitis B, it is contraindicated until after delivery.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	187	question	-	Manuel is a person with advanced COPD, who requires home care. At the last visit he verbally manifested fatigue, weakness and we observed clear signs of dyspnea on exertion. Given the diagnosis of "Intolerance to Activity", what NIC intervention would we consider ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	187	answer	0	Intolerance of the activity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	187	answer	1	Self-care: activities of daily life.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	187	answer	2	Knowledge: prescribed activity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	187	answer	3	Energy management
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	188	question	-	Point out the correct answer. When applying silver dressings in the treatment of wounds, what is the main function of these among the following answers ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	188	answer	0	Reduce the microbial load in acute or chronic infected wounds.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	188	answer	1	Prevent the antimicrobial barrier in acute or chronic infected wounds.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	188	answer	2	Eliminate the smell of chronic wounds.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	188	answer	3	Eliminate exudate from chronic wounds.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	189	question	-	Manuela, is an elderly diabetic attended at home with criteria of high complexity. Her daughters do not live with her and take care of her according to her availability in a rotating way. The nurse identifies a diagnosis of "Committed family confrontation". What result criteria would we consider NOC ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	189	answer	0	Support the caregiver.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	189	answer	1	Help with self-care: transfer.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	189	answer	2	Performance of the main caregiver: direct care.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	189	answer	3	Encourage family involvement.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	190	question	-	Studies carried out in our field, highlight the high prevalence of malnutrition and the risk of malnutrition in dependent persons assisted at home. Indicate the parameter that is NOT assessed with the Mini Nutritional Assessment:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	190	answer	0	Loss of appetite
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	190	answer	1	Recent weight loss.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	190	answer	2	Consideration of the patient on his health compared to people his age.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	190	answer	3	Presence of osteoporosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	191	question	-	In Primary Care What is the recommended test for initial screening to determine the situation of fragility / functional limitation in older people ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	191	answer	0	Short Physical Performance Battery (SPPB).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	191	answer	1	Audit C.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	191	answer	2	Lawton-Brody Index.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	191	answer	3	Morisky-Green test.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	192	question	-	In relation to the community case management nurse, she points out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	192	answer	0	Case management has been incorporated as a service modality for people with highly complex health problems.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	192	answer	1	It is the nurse responsible for the execution of the Care Plan.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	192	answer	2	Identify and mobilize services or resources to support care.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	192	answer	3	It favors home care.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	193	question	-	In relation to the prevention activities that nurses must carry out in children's health programs, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	193	answer	0	In children under 2 years, brushing should be done by the parents, with a toothpaste with 1,000 ppm of fluoride and the amount similar to a "scraping or stain" on the toothbrush.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	193	answer	1	In the health check-ups of the first year of life, the use of walkers should be advised.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	193	answer	2	The psychomotor development of the child should be assessed through the Denver test or Denver Developmental Screening Test-II (DDST-II).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	193	answer	3	Make dietary recommendations systematically in the health checks of all children from 2 to 18 years.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	194	question	-	The Common Services Portfolio of the current National Health System includes services for women. Which of the following activities is NOT contemplated ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	194	answer	0	Puerperal visit in the first month of postpartum to assess the state of health of the woman and the newborn.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	194	answer	1	Prevention, detection and attention to the problems of women in the climacteric.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	194	answer	2	Monitoring of risk pregnancy in a coordinated way with specialized attention.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	194	answer	3	Detection of risk groups and early diagnosis of gynecological cancer.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	195	question	-	In the family assessment in crisis situations, the nurse can identify the characteristics of functional or dysfunctional families. Which of the following tests can be useful ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	195	answer	0	MOS questionnaire.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	195	answer	1	Duke-UNC questionnaire.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	195	answer	2	Apgar Familiar.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	195	answer	3	Family Genogram
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	196	question	-	You are in the Primary Care office where you are going to vaccinate a person. Note in the package insert that an adjuvant is found among the components of the vaccine. What does this component refer to ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	196	answer	0	An adjuvant is a substance that increases the immunogenicity of the vaccine antigen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	196	answer	1	An adjuvant, despite its effect, will decrease the stability of the vaccine antigen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	196	answer	2	An adjuvant should not be introduced into vaccines for special populations, such as the elderly or immunosuppressed.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	196	answer	3	An adjuvant does not allow reducing the amount of vaccine antigen included in the vaccine or the number of doses of vaccines administered.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	197	question	-	Receive a notice to attend a traffic accident. It is the only health staff until the arrival of advanced life support. Upon arrival, a patient is found who has been removed from the car and who presents amputation at the level of the distal femur with intense arterial hemorrhage. The patient is unconscious. What would be the order of action ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	197	answer	0	Insert venous via to administer fluids, perform evaluation of the airway, breathing and circulation and resuscitation maneuvers if necessary.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	197	answer	1	Place tourniquet above the wound, perform airway assessment, breathing, circulation and perform cardiopulmonary resuscitation maneuvers if applicable.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	197	answer	2	Evaluate the airway, breathing, circulation, perform resuscitation maneuvers if necessary and elevate the limb to reduce bleeding.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	197	answer	3	Check the airway, breathing, circulation, perform resuscitation maneuvers if necessary and then apply a tourniquet over the wound.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	198	question	-	Mrs. M.F.B goes to your Primary Health Care clinic in the center where you work with a report from the hematologist of the reference hospital in which a thrombocytopenia is indicated as a diagnosis. You review the drugs you are taking. Which of them can contribute to thrombocytopenia ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	198	answer	0	Ibuprofen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	198	answer	1	Metformin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	198	answer	2	Omeprazole
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	198	answer	3	Bromazepam.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	199	question	-	Which of the following answers is a defining characteristic of the nursing diagnosis "ineffective management of family health" ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	199	answer	0	Reject the change in health status.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	199	answer	1	Failure to take action to reduce risk factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	199	answer	2	Express desire to improve the immunization / vaccination status.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	199	answer	3	Express desire to improve the choices of daily life to achieve the objectives.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	200	question	-	She goes to the Primary Care consultation María, 8 years old, accompanied by her father because of leg injuries. The father comments that yesterday they were in an old family house in the countryside to review the structure of it and stayed to sleep, although the mattresses were old. Multiple and grouped erythematous papules arranged in a zigzag pattern are observed in the girl. It does not present hemorrhagic sufferers. What would be the first suspected cause of these injuries ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	200	answer	0	Bedbug stings
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	200	answer	1	Horse-fly stings
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	200	answer	2	Tracked stings.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	200	answer	3	Lice bites
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	201	question	-	Point out the correct answer. Manuel, 58, has recently started treatment with acenocoumarol. Go to your consultation for assessment and health education. You will inform about:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	201	answer	0	The interaction with medications such as acetylsalicylic acid is negligible.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	201	answer	1	The interaction of broadleaf vegetables because this treatment acts to enhance the action of vitamin K.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	201	answer	2	The interaction of broadleaf vegetables because this treatment works by inhibiting the action of vitamin K.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	201	answer	3	The interaction with certain intercurrent processes is not significant due to the wide therapeutic margin of this treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	202	question	-	Are you as a companion of a relative in a consultation, in his presence a person collapses? What is the sequence of steps to follow in the performance, according to the latest recommendations of the European Resuscitation Council 2015 ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	202	answer	0	Early recognition and asking for help, early cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) by health professionals, Automatic External Defibrillation (AED), early advanced life support.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	202	answer	1	Early recognition and asking for help, early CPR by witnesses, basic life support.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	202	answer	2	Early recognition and waiting for help, early CPR by health professionals, DEA, early advanced life support and standardized post-resuscitation care.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	202	answer	3	Early recognition and asking for help, early CPR per witness, early defibrillation, early advanced life support and standardized post-resuscitation care.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	203	question	-	Which parameter does NOT indicate a good start and initiation of breastfeeding ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	203	answer	0	The baby's chin touches the chest and the nose is free.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	203	answer	1	There is less areola visible below the chin than above the nipple.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	203	answer	2	Sucking sounds are heard.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	203	answer	3	Absence of pain in the mother.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	204	question	-	She goes to the primary care clinic Teresa, 35 years of age to administer the anti-hepatitis A vaccine. After its administration, the patient complains of generalized itching and difficulty breathing. Given the suspicion of an anaphylactic reaction to a component of the vaccine, what immediate action would be the LEAST adequate ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	204	answer	0	Assess airway patency.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	204	answer	1	Administration of intravenous adrenaline.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	204	answer	2	100% oxygen administration.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	204	answer	3	Administration of inhaled or nebulized salbutamol.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	205	question	-	Augustine goes to the consultation of the health center. You, as your Primary Care nurse, detect the presence of bradycardia. Which of the following factors could be linked ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	205	answer	0	Body temperature of 38ºC.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	205	answer	1	Presence of hemorrhage.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	205	answer	2	Digitalis taking.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	205	answer	3	Step from decubitus position to standing.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	206	question	-	Jesus, a 72-year-old man presents a wound after a fall a few days ago. The bed is dry, and there is a hard, blackened plaque that makes healing difficult. Within the types of debridements available, choose the correct answer in relation to autolytic debridement:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	206	answer	0	The cells responsible for autolytic debridement are macrophages and phagocytes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	206	answer	1	It occurs naturally in all wounds, but can be inhibited by the use of amorphous hydrogels.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	206	answer	2	One of the advantages is that it presents a shorter action over time.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	206	answer	3	It is a type of traumatic debridement and not very selective.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	207	question	-	He goes to the emergency service José Antonio, 12, diagnosed with diabetes. He presents sweating and tremor and a capillary blood glucose of 43 mg / dl. To what physiological mechanism are these signs caused by hypoglycemia ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	207	answer	0	Stimulation of the sympathetic nervous system.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	207	answer	1	Stimulation of the parasympathetic nervous system.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	207	answer	2	Inhibition of the autonomic nervous system.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	207	answer	3	Alteration of the central nervous system.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	208	question	-	Which of the following muscles participates in the raising of the rib cage during inspiration ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	208	answer	0	External intercostals.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	208	answer	1	Internal intercostals
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	208	answer	2	Diaphragm.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	208	answer	3	Straight of the abdomen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	209	question	-	When a manager trusts in the high involvement and training of each one of the people that make up the group, encourages him to discuss and share decision-making with them, the leadership style is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	209	answer	0	Autocratic.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	209	answer	1	Bureaucratic.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	209	answer	2	Permissive.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	209	answer	3	Democratic.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	210	question	-	As a Nursing professional in a Health Center, you receive an urgent notice to go to a home with the information of loss of consciousness of a 53-year-old man. Upon arrival at the site he finds the person on the floor of a yard under construction and the woman reports that she has been working all morning despite the heat that she is doing. The patient shows an abnormal flexion of the extremities, to the call it emits incomprehensible sounds and only opens the eyes before the pain. Indicate your score on the Glasgow scale:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	210	answer	0	3 + 2 + 1 = 6.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	210	answer	1	4 + 1 + 1 = 6.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	210	answer	2	3 + 3 + 1 = 7.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	210	answer	3	3 + 2 + 2 = 7.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	211	question	-	Lucía is a 42-year-old woman who comes to the consultation of her Primary Care nurse after being discharged from the hospital due to appendectomy. Presents a wound in the abdomen considered contaminated clean. Depending on the degree and likelihood of contamination, a wound is a clean contaminated type when:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	211	answer	0	It has dead tissue.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	211	answer	1	They are surgical wounds that have affected the respiratory, alimentary, genital or urinary tract and do not show signs of infection.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	211	answer	2	They are surgical wounds in which the sterile field has been seriously violated.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	211	answer	3	They show signs of inflammation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	212	question	-	During the focused assessment of the breathing pattern of Mr. Juan Antonio, 68, he finds the following characteristics: frequency and depth of irregular breathing, with periods of apnea combined with periods of breathing that increase in depth and frequency and then decrease gradually until again pause for apnea. Point out how you would record this respiratory pattern in the medical record:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	212	answer	0	Cheyne-Stokes breathing.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	212	answer	1	Breathing Biot.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	212	answer	2	Eupneic breathing.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	212	answer	3	Breath of Kussmaul.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	213	question	-	Elena has had a permanent colostomy 10 days ago for sigma cancer. She goes to consult with her Primary Care nurse today and says that she has not yet been able to change her device because she does not want to "see what she has there", it is her daughter who carries out the hygiene of the area. What nursing diagnosis based on the NANDA Taxonomy would you write in the Clinical History in this case ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	213	answer	0	Body image disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	213	answer	1	Personal oversight
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	213	answer	2	Acute confusion
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	213	answer	3	Unstable emotional control.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	214	question	-	According to the strategy of health promotion and prevention in the National Health System, which of the following recommendations on physical activity in the adult population is NOT correct ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	214	answer	0	Perform a minimum of 150 minutes per week of moderate physical activity or a minimum of 75 minutes per week of vigorous activity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	214	answer	1	Strength exercises (muscle enhancement) of large muscle groups should be performed at least two days a week.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	214	answer	2	Reduce prolonged sedentary periods, taking active breaks every three or four hours with short stretching sessions or taking a short walk.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	214	answer	3	In order to maintain the range of joint mobility, it is recommended to perform series of flexibility exercises twice a week.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	215	question	-	Among the recommendations of different international organizations on healthy eating are all the following, except one. Identify it:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	215	answer	0	Increase the daily intake of fruits, vegetables and vegetables to reach, at least 400 g / day.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	215	answer	1	Moderate the consumption of simple sugars such as sweets, sweets and soft drinks.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	215	answer	2	Increase the consumption of legumes, whole grains and nuts.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	215	answer	3	Consume at least 30% of the caloric intake from saturated fatty acids.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	216	question	-	The Strategy for the Promotion of Health and Prevention of the National Health System proposes to detect and intervene on frailty in people over 70 years of age. What test do you propose to use to perform fragility screening in Primary Care ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	216	answer	0	Short Physical Performance Battery (SPPB) execution test.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	216	answer	1	Downton scale.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	216	answer	2	Tinetti scale.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	216	answer	3	Goldberg Health Questionnaire.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	217	question	-	Is it necessary to administer diphtheria-tetanus booster vaccine in a healthy 25-year-old patient who has been properly vaccinated in childhood, has been cut with glass from a bottle and has a clean wound ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	217	answer	0	Yes, a booster dose of diphtheria-tetanus should be administered after more than 10 years have elapsed since the last dose.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	217	answer	1	Yes, a booster dose of diphtheria-tetanus and a dose of antitetanus gammaglobulin should have been administered more than 10 years after the last dose.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	217	answer	2	No, it is protected and it would not be necessary to give a booster dose.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	217	answer	3	Yes, whenever an incised wound occurs, a dose of tetanus vaccine should be administered, regardless of the patient's immunization status.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	218	question	-	Regarding the administration of vaccines, indicate the wrong answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	218	answer	0	To administer vaccines intramuscularly, the needle should pierce the skin at a 90º angle.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	218	answer	1	When a vaccine and a gamma globulin should be administered, they should be injected into different extremities.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	218	answer	2	The tuberculosis vaccine (BCG) is administered intradermally.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	218	answer	3	The rotavirus vaccine is administered by the deep subcutaneous route.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	219	question	-	In relation to the screening and intervention on alcohol risk consumption, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	219	answer	0	To perform the risk consumption screening in Primary Care, the use of the AUDIT-C test is proposed.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	219	answer	1	In men, a consumption higher than 40 g / day is considered risky (4 Unit of Standard Drink UBE) or 280 g / week (28 UBE).
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	219	answer	2	In women, a consumption higher than 24 g / day (2-2.5 UBE) or 170 g / week (17 UBE) is considered risky.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	219	answer	3	Among the recommendations for reducing consumption in the non-dependent risk drinker is the convenience of drinking distilled beverages instead of fermented beverages.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	220	question	-	In relation to the measures of prevention of Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs), point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	220	answer	0	To prevent the transmission of human papilloma virus, the Interterritorial Council of the National Health System recommends the vaccination of girls at 12 years of age.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	220	answer	1	The latex condom and the diaphragm are considered very effective methods for the prevention of STIs.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	220	answer	2	Spermicides are not considered an adequate method to prevent STIs.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	220	answer	3	People with a diagnosed STI should receive advice about the period in which they and their partners should avoid having sex.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	221	question	-	Soledad, a 73-year-old woman who is visited at her daughter's house, with whom she usually lives. In a new assessment of the Activity / Exercise pattern, Soledad tells her that before she reached the Health Center, which is half a kilometer away, but since the last time her vision has worsened, the streets are under construction and she finds herself with worse physical condition. Her daughter reports that Soledad is afraid of falling and that she now walks worse and has difficulty climbing stairs and ramps, but that she still drives well inside the house. Indicate the diagnostic label to which the case corresponds:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	221	answer	0	Intolerance to activity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	221	answer	1	Deterioration of the ability to translate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	221	answer	2	Deterioration of standing.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	221	answer	3	Impairment of ambulation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	222	question	-	Juana of 89 years, conscious and oriented, has been institutionalized in the hospital for three months. The reason for admission was a fracture of the left humerus, but after its intervention, it was complicated by a respiratory infection process that kept it intact and with minimal possibility of displacement. Social interaction and daily activity have been reduced considerably. Manifest boredom and motivation to increase activity and social contacts, however, the environment does not allow to engage in a daily activity similar to your habit at home. Indicate the diagnostic label according to the case:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	222	answer	0	Sedentary lifestyle
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	222	answer	1	Deficit of recreational activities.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	222	answer	2	Risk of disuse syndrome.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	222	answer	3	Fear.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	223	question	-	Walking down the street to make a home visit is a man of about 40 who suffers a heat stroke. Point out the correct option with regard to heat stroke:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	223	answer	0	The heat stroke is manifested by a rise in body temperature above 41 ° C, hot skin, diaphoresis, redness, miotic and non-reactive pupils and change of adjustment at the level of the hypothalamus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	223	answer	1	The heat stroke is manifested by a rise in body temperature above 39 ° C, an increase in heart rate, a drop in blood pressure, hot skin, diaphoresis, redness and a change in the level of the hypothalamus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	223	answer	2	Heat stroke is manifested by a rise in body temperature above 40 ° C, a decrease in heart rate and blood pressure, hot, dry, pale skin and depression of hypothalamus function.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	223	answer	3	Heat stroke is manifested by a rise in body temperature above 41ºC, an increase in heart rate, a drop in blood pressure, hot, dry, red skin, and depression of hypothalamus function.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	224	question	-	The positive Trousseau sign where the carpal spasm occurs is characteristic of an electrolyte disturbance and can be easily identified in the Primary Care consultation with the help of a cuff to take the tension. Indicate the type of alteration of the electrolyte balance in question:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	224	answer	0	Hypocalcemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	224	answer	1	Hypomagnesemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	224	answer	2	Hyperkalemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	224	answer	3	Hypernatremia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	225	question	-	He goes to the home of Milagros, a 61-year-old woman on dialysis for kidney failure who has manifested diarrhea and paresthesias in the extremities in the last few hours. During the assessment, you find a substantial decrease in the usual heart rate along with an irregular pulse. Indicate the type of electrolyte imbalance to suspect before said evaluation:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	225	answer	0	Hypokalemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	225	answer	1	Hypomagnesemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	225	answer	2	Hypermagnesemia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	225	answer	3	Hyperkalemia
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	226	question	-	A follow-up assessment of Ramona is performed for the diagnosis of excess fluid volume by means of the scale of four points of assessment of the edema. Point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	226	answer	0	The fovea up to two millimeters is recorded as 0.
Cuaderno_2017_1_E	226	answer	1	The fovea from 2 to 7 millimeters is rated as 2+.
