Cuaderno_2017_1_M	68	answer	3	It is recommended to replace the aneurysmal aorta when, in a period of 1 year, an increase in the diameter of the aneurysm of more than 1 cm is observed.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	69	question	-	In a situation of heart failure, the heart presents different adaptive mechanisms. Which of the following is NOT correct?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	69	answer	0	Inhibition of the arginine-vasopressin system, which generates vasoconstriction and hydrosaline retention.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	69	answer	1	Development of myocardial hypertrophy, to normalize the overload of the ventricular wall.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	69	answer	2	Activation of the sympathetic nervous system, which increases ventricular contractility.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	69	answer	3	Alterations in the production of energy in the myocardium and modifications in the extracellular matrix of the myocardiocytes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	70	question	-	Male of 84 years of age, with chronic heart failure in functional grade II secondary to ischemic heart disease with severe non-revascularizable systolic dysfunction, chronic kidney disease stage 3 (glomerular filtration 45-50 mL / min) and permanent atrial fibrillation with heart rate> 80 beats per minute. Which of the following drugs does NOT provide benefit to the patient based on the evidence currently available?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	70	answer	0	Ivabradina.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	70	answer	1	Inhibitors of angiotensin converting enzyme.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	70	answer	2	Anti-aldosteronic.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	70	answer	3	Beta-blockers.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	71	question	-	A 45-year-old man, with a history of febrile symptoms and chest pain, goes to the hospital with dyspnea and tachypnea. On physical examination, the blood pressure figures are low, the jugular venous pressure is elevated with a prominent descending sinus x and the pulse is paradoxical. What diagnosis would you suspect?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	71	answer	0	Dilated cardiomyopathy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	71	answer	1	Pericardial effusion with cardiac tamponade.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	71	answer	2	Constrictive pericarditis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	71	answer	3	Ischemic heart disease
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	72	question	-	The presence in the right cardiac catheterization of an average pressure of the pulmonary artery> of 25 mm Hg and a pulmonary pressure (or capillary)> of 15 mm Hg, is defining:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	72	answer	0	Idiopathic pulmonary arterial hypertension.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	72	answer	1	Pulmonary arterial hypertension associated with connective tissue disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	72	answer	2	Pulmonary hypertension secondary to left heart disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	72	answer	3	Chronic thromboembolic pulmonary hypertension.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	73	question	-	The most frequent location of deep vein thrombosis is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	73	answer	0	Venous plexuses of the soleus muscles.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	73	answer	1	Femoral sector in the thigh.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	73	answer	2	Iliac sector
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	73	answer	3	Vena cava inferior.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	74	question	-	Regarding the resection surgery of pancreatic head adenocarcinoma, indicate which technique is most used:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	74	answer	0	The cephalic duodenopancreatectomy with regional lymphadenectomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	74	answer	1	The pancreaticojejunostomy, which consists in the derivation of the pancreatic duct to the intestine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	74	answer	2	Corporo-caudal pancreatectomy by laparoscopy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	74	answer	3	Enucleation of the tumor without the need for lymphadenectomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	75	question	-	A 78-year-old woman with dementia and institutionalized is brought by her caregivers for severe abdominal pain with deterioration of the general state and abdominal distension. Analytical with leukocytosis, elevated hematocrit, renal failure and metabolic acidosis. The ECG shows atrial fibrillation. Abdominal tomography detects edematous small bowel loops, with intestinal and portal pneumatosis. The most likely diagnosis is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	75	answer	0	Perforation of gastric or duodenal ulcus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	75	answer	1	Biliary ileus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	75	answer	2	Obstructive sigmoid neoplasia with perforation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	75	answer	3	Mesenteric ischemia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	76	question	-	An 80-year-old woman attended the emergency department with abdominal pain that began in the epigastrium and subsequently irradiated to the left iliac fossa. It is accompanied by fever of 37.5ºC. An abdominal CT is performed, objectifying inflammation in the walls of the sigma and mesenteric abscess of 2 cm. The treatment of choice is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	76	answer	0	Admission in plant with absolute diet and broad spectrum antibiotic treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	76	answer	1	Discharge colostomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	76	answer	2	Drainage by laparoscopic surgery.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	76	answer	3	Urgent surgery with sigmoidectomy and colorectal anastomosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	77	question	-	A 52-year-old man was referred to the digestive service for symptoms of hematochezia, tenesmus and reduced diameter of the stool. A series of tests are performed, diagnosing a sigma adenocarcinoma without distant metastasis. The patient is surgically treated and referred to the medical oncology office to assess complementary chemotherapy treatment. Which of the following factors is of poor prognosis after surgical resection and should be taken into account when planning chemotherapy treatment?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	77	answer	0	The presence of anemia at diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	77	answer	1	The existence of a family history of colorectal cancer.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	77	answer	2	The size of the primary lesion and histological differentiation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	77	answer	3	The perforation or adhesion of the tumor to adjacent organs.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	78	question	-	In ulcerative colitis, what factor does NOT increase the risk of colorectal neoplasia?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	78	answer	0	The time of evolution.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	78	answer	1	The extensive affectation of the disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	78	answer	2	The coexistence of primary biliary cirrhosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	78	answer	3	Family history of colorectal cancer.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	79	question	-	A 56-year-old man, smoker and drinker, presented dysphagia mainly to solids, regurgitation and retrosternal pain. Endoscopy was performed, finding a stenosing 3 cm tumor in the distal esophagus. The biopsy is reported as an adenocarcinoma. Thoracic CT shows thickening of 2 cm in the thoracic esophagus without distant metastases. In the transesophageal ultrasound, a tumor is observed that invades the muscle, without observing mediastinal lymph nodes. What is the treatment of choice?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	79	answer	0	Neoadjuvant chemoradiotherapy and later esophagectomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	79	answer	1	Radiotherapy as definitive treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	79	answer	2	Placement of stent-type prosthesis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	79	answer	3	Esophagectomy and gastric plasty with cervical anastomosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	80	question	-	A 39-year-old woman diagnosed with type 1 diabetes mellitus more than 20 years ago. For several months he has reported nausea, with some vomiting and abdominal distension. He has lost 6 Kg of weight. Gastroscopy: normal esophagus, stomach with alimentary remains and rest of the exploration until second duodenal portion without alterations. What evidence do you think is most useful for your diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	80	answer	0	Ultrasound of the abdomen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	80	answer	1	Esophageal manometry
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	80	answer	2	CT of the abdomen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	80	answer	3	Isotopic study of gastric emptying.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	81	question	-	A 35-year-old man with no pathological history of interest who went to the emergency room for presenting a picture of instability after an episode of black stools such as tar. In the emergency room, arterial hypotension was observed and recovered with conventional fluid therapy. Hemoglobin on admission 8 g / dL, hematocrit 25%. In the following days it continues with melénic episodes and descent of the hematocrit that need the transfusion of 3 packed red blood cells. Colonoscopy and upper digestive endoscopy were performed, finding no cause of his hemorrhagic symptoms. After one week of hospital admission and the transfusion of 4 units of red blood cell concentrates, she continues with manes. The next step to follow is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	81	answer	0	Immediate surgical intervention.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	81	answer	1	Endoscopic capsule
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	81	answer	2	Surgical enteroscopy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	81	answer	3	Continue with conservative treatment and request arteriography.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	82	question	-	A 30-year-old woman, 33 weeks pregnant, who consulted for pruritus of a week of evolution. Liver tests show a slight increase in transaminase values ​​(AST 77 IU / L and ALT 84 IU / L), as well as alkaline phosphatase (155 IU / L) and gamma-glutamyl-transpeptidase (125 IU / L), with a Total bilirubin figure of 2.3 mg / dL. The hemogram and the coagulation study are normal, the abdominal ultrasound shows no hepatic or biliary abnormalities and the hepatitis virus serology, as well as the autoantibodies are negative. Which of the following attitudes is correct?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	82	answer	0	Perform a liver biopsy to establish the diagnosis of liver disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	82	answer	1	Treat the patient with ursodeoxycholic acid, since it is probably a benign intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	82	answer	2	Interrupting pregnancy since the most likely diagnosis is acute fatty liver of pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	82	answer	3	Perform an MRI to rule out primary sclerosing cholangitis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	83	question	-	A 67-year-old man with alcoholic cirrhosis followed up by the hepatology service is diagnosed with a hepatocellular carcinoma of 3 cm in diameter located in the left lobe, segment 3. Subjected to a study to assess the treatment to be followed, it is shown that the patient does not have Portal hypertension has a normal hepatic function, a MELD score of 7 and a Child-Pugh grade A. The alpha-fetoprotein is less than 50 ng / mL and no distant metastasis has been observed. What is the most indicated treatment in this patient?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	83	answer	0	Apply percutaneous ethanol injection.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	83	answer	1	Liver resection.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	83	answer	2	Liver transplant
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	83	answer	3	Transarterial chemoembolization.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	84	question	-	A 24-year-old man with chronic iron deficiency anemia of unknown origin, with ileocolonoscopy and esophagogastroduodenoscopy without lesions. An endoscopic capsule study was performed observing isolated ulcers at the level of the distal jejunum. In which of the following diseases are these injuries?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	84	answer	0	Whipple's disease
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	84	answer	1	Cystic pneumatosis intestinal.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	84	answer	2	Refractory celiac sprue.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	84	answer	3	Eosinophilic enteritis
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	85	question	-	In irritable bowel syndrome, it is true that:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	85	answer	0	Routine laboratory studies (analysis) show specific abnormalities of this syndrome.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	85	answer	1	Among the symptoms that make us think of an irritable bowel are: nighttime abdominal pain, progressive pain and weight loss.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	85	answer	2	It courses with diarrhea or constipation; if both are manifested, this entity is ruled out.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	85	answer	3	In patients with irritable bowel syndrome with predominance of diarrhea, the diagnostic study should include: stool culture, celiac disease screening, colonoscopy with biopsies.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	86	question	-	Which statement about pancreatic cancer is correct?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	86	answer	0	The risk factors involved in this neoplasia include smoking, obesity and acute pancreatitis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	86	answer	1	The most suitable diagnostic imaging test is helical CT without contrast and double phase.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	86	answer	2	It is necessary to confirm preoperatory anatomopathological diagnosis before performing surgical treatment with a curative purpose.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	86	answer	3	The genetic alteration detected most frequently is the deletion of the p16 gene.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	87	question	-	What is the treatment of choice for a 38-year-old man diagnosed with Cushing's disease in relation to a pituitary macroadenoma 22 mm in diameter?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	87	answer	0	Initially try medical treatment and, if it is not effective, resort to surgery.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	87	answer	1	Adrenalectomy
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	87	answer	2	Selective surgical resection of the adenoma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	87	answer	3	Radiation therapy to try to decrease the tumor size.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	88	question	-	A 55-year-old woman, type 2 diabetic and obese, on treatment with metformin, with 8% Hb A1c, tells a story of recurrent urinary tract infections. Which of the following therapeutic options to associate with metformin considers the LESS adequate?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	88	answer	0	DPP4 inhibitors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	88	answer	1	GLP1 analogs.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	88	answer	2	Basal insulin
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	88	answer	3	SGLT2 inhibitors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	89	question	-	Which of the following drugs has been shown to be effective in reducing fibrosis in a patient with non-alcoholic steatohepatitis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	89	answer	0	Pioglitazone.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	89	answer	1	Pentoxifylline
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	89	answer	2	Ursodeoxycholic acid.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	89	answer	3	Fenofibrate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	90	question	-	A 27-year-old woman consulted for presenting secondary amenorrhea of ​​one year of evolution. It does not refer to yatrogenic antecedents. Analytically, the estradiol concentration is lower than normal and the prolactin value is 12 ng / mL. Indicate which of the explorations cited below would request as a first step to try to identify the origin of the disorder:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	90	answer	0	Magnetic resonance hypothalamus pituitary.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	90	answer	1	Karyotype
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	90	answer	2	Basal FSH.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	90	answer	3	Stimulation with chorionic gonadotropin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	91	question	-	A 34-year-old woman admitted for a polyuria and polydipsia study. In the first 24 hours of admission, a diuresis of 8.2 liters was observed and an analytical sample was obtained showing a glycemia of 96 mg / dL, natremia of 148 mEq / L and plasma osmolality of 309 mOsm / kg with urinary osmolality of 89 mOsm / kg. What diagnostic test should be done next?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	91	answer	0	Infusion test of hypertonic saline for serial determination of antidiuretic hormone.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	91	answer	1	Dehydration test (Miller test).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	91	answer	2	Administration of desmopressin with serial control of osmolality in urine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	91	answer	3	Determination of antidiuretic hormone in plasma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	92	question	-	A 24-year-old student of mathematics, who comes to the clinic to confirm the diagnostic suspicion after a consultation in Google. Since childhood he has episodes of intense pain, lancinating, in hands and feet, lasting between minutes and days. He relates them to physical exercise, stress or fever, and was diagnosed with "growing pains". Later he notes that he does not have sweating after playing sports. He has also observed punctate skin lesions, of a dark red color, in "the swimsuit zone", considered non-specific. Get the diagnosis after collecting three keys (painful neuropathy, hypohidrosis and angiokeratomas). What do you think is the diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	92	answer	0	Fabry disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	92	answer	1	Pompe disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	92	answer	2	Hereditary amyloidotic polyneuropathy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	92	answer	3	Gaucher disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	93	question	-	A 73-year-old patient presented complete neurological dysphagia in the swallowing test, secondary to a cadioembolic stroke in the territory of the left middle cerebral artery. You will need long-term nutritional support. Of the following treatment modalities, which one do you consider most appropriate for this case?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	93	answer	0	Enteral nutrition by nasogastric tube.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	93	answer	1	Enteral nutrition by nasoduodenal tube.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	93	answer	2	Enteral nutrition by gastrostomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	93	answer	3	Enteral nutrition by jejunostomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	94	question	-	A 45-year-old woman presented to the emergency department with confusional symptoms accompanied by dysphonia. On examination, the patient had a palpable mass in the neck and in the blood analysis plasma levels of 15 mg / dL (normal up to 10.2 mg / dL). Given these findings, which of the following diagnoses should be suspected?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	94	answer	0	Parathyroid carcinoma
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	94	answer	1	Medullary thyroid carcinoma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	94	answer	2	MEN type I.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	94	answer	3	Adenoma of parathyroid.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	95	question	-	64 year old woman Menopause at 54 years old. Two pregnancies and eutocic births. He does not take any medication. He goes to the emergency department referring vaginal bleeding of two days with discomfort in hypogastrium. The clinical examination performed by the gynecologist does not object to injuries in the external genitalia, vagina or cervix. The vaginal touch is not conclusive. Which of the following behaviors seems the most appropriate as the first diagnostic approach?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	95	answer	0	Transvaginal ultrasound and endometrial thickness measurement. Depending on it, take an endometrial biopsy or not.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	95	answer	1	Endometrial biopsy by aspiration in consultation. With it I can obtain the diagnosis very reliably and it is economical.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	95	answer	2	Hysteroscopy with sedation and directed biopsy if any lesion is seen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	95	answer	3	I would perform a microlevel, since it is the test that would give me the definitive diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	96	question	-	A 24-year-old woman complained of low abdominal pain of two weeks evolution that has worsened with the last sexual intercourse. He refers to having a recent partner with whom he only occasionally uses a condom. The examination presents regular general condition. Tº of 38.6ºC, leucocytes 16,000 / uL (85% neutrophils); PCR 30 mg / L. The speculum examination evidences abundant abnormal vaginal discharge and painful cervical mobilization. Indicate the FALSE answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	96	answer	0	We would start antibiotic treatment as soon as we suspect the diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	96	answer	1	We would indicate as a complementary preferential test a hysterosalpingography for tubal evaluation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	96	answer	2	The delay in diagnosis and treatment increases the appearance of sequelae.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	96	answer	3	The presence of abscess would be a criterion for hospitalization.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	97	question	-	A 21-year-old woman presented with a hormonal study with FSH 0.29 mUI / mL (normal in the follicular phase = 3.50-12.50 mUI / mL) and LH <0.1 mUI / mL (normal follicular phase 2.40-12.60 mUI / mL). We must perform a differential diagnosis between the following clinical situations EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	97	answer	0	Administration of combined oral contraceptives.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	97	answer	1	Premature ovarian failure.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	97	answer	2	Eating behavior disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	97	answer	3	Craniopharyngioma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	98	question	-	Regarding urinary incontinence, point out the FALSE answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	98	answer	0	In urinary stress incontinence, a precipitating factor is physical exercise.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	98	answer	1	In urgency incontinence, the urinary frequency is normal.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	98	answer	2	The most reliable test to establish an accurate diagnosis of the type of incontinence is the urodynamic study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	98	answer	3	In the treatment of emergency urinary incontinence, anticholinergic drugs are used.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	99	question	-	A 34-year-old woman consulted for recurrent co-surgery. It provides a cytology with a high-grade intraepithelial lesion (H-SIL). Subsequently, colposcopy and biopsy are performed on a mosaic area and the histology tells us of a focus of invasive squamous carcinoma of 2 mm in length. Which therapeutic option is the most appropriate for this patient?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	99	answer	0	Conization
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	99	answer	1	Total hysterectomy without adnexectomy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	99	answer	2	Pelvic radiotherapy with curative intention.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	99	answer	3	Repeat a larger biopsy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	100	question	-	What anatomopathological characteristics present, in most cases, tumors included in the molecular subtype of breast cancer called "basal-like"?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	100	answer	0	High positivity for hormone receptors, negativity for HER2 and low expression of Ki67.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	100	answer	1	High positivity for hormone receptors, negativity for HER2 and high expression of Ki67.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	100	answer	2	Absence of hormone receptor expression and negativity for HER2.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	100	answer	3	Absence of hormone receptor expression and presence of HER2 positive (overexpressed or amplified).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	101	question	-	A 64-year-old woman with no relevant comorbidities was operated on for a right breast cancer through an enlarged lumpectomy and selective sentinel node biopsy, with the following pathological result: poorly differentiated infiltrative ductal carcinoma (grade 3), size 2.2 cm ( pT2), positive estrogen and progesterone receptors, Ki67 25%, HER2 negative. It presents macroscopic involvement of the sentinel lymph node, although there is no involvement of the rest of isolated axillary lymph nodes (pN1). What adjuvant systemic treatment do you consider most appropriate for this patient?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	101	answer	0	Adjuvant hormone therapy that includes aromatase inhibitors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	101	answer	1	Adjuvant chemotherapy, preferably with anthracyclines and taxanes, followed by hormone therapy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	101	answer	2	Adjuvant chemotherapy in association with the monoclonal antibody trastuzumab, followed by hormone therapy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	101	answer	3	Adjuvant chemotherapy, preferably with anthracyclines and taxanes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	102	question	-	Which of the following is NOT a movement in the head delivery mechanism?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	102	answer	0	Retroflection
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	102	answer	1	Flexion.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	102	answer	2	Detachment
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	102	answer	3	Intrapelvic rotation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	103	question	-	A 36-year-old woman who attended the clinic for having suffered three spontaneous abortions in the first trimester. He has not had any pregnancy to term. Among the studies that you will request in the first place, the following is NOT included:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	103	answer	0	Hysterosalpingography.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	103	answer	1	Karyotype in peripheral blood of both members of the couple.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	103	answer	2	Determination of antiphospholipid antibodies.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	103	answer	3	Vaginal ultrasound.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	104	question	-	Which of the following is the sequence of measures CORRECT to a postpartum hemorrhage?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	104	answer	0	Uterine massage, bladder catheter placement, volume replacement, administration of uterotonics and revision of the birth canal.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	104	answer	1	Uterine massage, bladder catheter placement, volemia replacement, administration of uterotonics and transvaginal ultrasound.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	104	answer	2	Uterine massage, bladder catheter placement, volume replacement, administration of uterotonics and uterine tamponade.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	104	answer	3	Uterine massage, bladder catheter placement, volume replacement, administration of uterotonics and ligation of uterine arteries.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	105	question	-	40-year-old woman who consults for anemia. In the analytical highlights Hb 10.5 g / dL, iron deficiency, macrocytosis and hypergastrinemia. He has a history of lupus arthropathy and Graves Basedow's disease. It is being treated with prednisone 15 mg / d, colchicine 0.5 mg every 12 h and methimazole 10 mg / d. What do you consider the most likely cause of anemia?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	105	answer	0	Hematic losses in relation to steroid treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	105	answer	1	Medullary hypoplasia 2º to colchicine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	105	answer	2	Hemolysis secondary to taking methimazole.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	105	answer	3	Type A gastritis
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	106	question	-	A 32-year-old woman consulted because she wanted to get pregnant and reported a history of a lung embolism episode 7 years earlier while taking oral contraceptives. Treatment was performed with acenocoumarol for 6 months. The thrombophilia study was negative. Prophylaxis of venous thrombosis is advised in case you become pregnant. Point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	106	answer	0	Prophylactic treatment with low molecular weight heparin should be advised during pregnancy and up to 6 weeks postpartum.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	106	answer	1	Prophylactic treatment with aspirin should be advised throughout the pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	106	answer	2	Prophylaxis with acenocoumarol should be advised throughout the pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	106	answer	3	Since the thrombophilia study was negative, only prophylaxis of venous thrombosis with compression stockings for lower limbs is required.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	107	question	-	Regarding anticoagulant treatment, indicate the FALSE response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	107	answer	0	Dabigatran - Direct thrombin inhibitor.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	107	answer	1	Plasugrel - Aggregation inhibitor and platelet activation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	107	answer	2	Edoxaban - Direct factor Xa inhibitor.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	107	answer	3	Idarucizumab - Inhibitor of plasminogen activation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	108	question	-	A 64-year-old woman with a history of bilateral carpal tunnel. In the last months it presents a picture of asthenia and progressive dyspnea, until making small efforts. In the analytical one stands out a pro-BNP of 2,500 pg / mL, as well as the existence of a monoclonal component (positive immunofixation for lambda chains) in serum of 0.4 g / dL. The levels of kappa and lambda free light chains are 1.2 and 67.8 mg / dL, respectively. A sternal puncture is performed, observing a medullary plasmacytosis of 6%. Absence of lytic lesions in CT of the entire skeleton. What is the diagnosis of suspicion and the initial diagnostic test for confirmation?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	108	answer	0	Waldenström macroglobulinemia - Molecular analysis of the MYD88 gene.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	108	answer	1	Symptomatic multiple myeloma - PET / CT.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	108	answer	2	Amyloidosis AL - Aspirate / abdominal fat biopsy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	108	answer	3	POEMS syndrome - Determination of VEGF.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	109	question	-	A 17-year-old woman who presents very abundant rules from the first menstruation. Refer frequent epistaxis. Hematimetry: Hb 10.5 g / dL, VCM 77 fL, leukocytes 7,200 / uL with normal formula, platelets 182,000 / uL. Prothrombin time 12 "(12"), aPTT 34 "(30"), fibrinogen 340 mg / dL. Platelet aggregation with ADP, collagen and epinephrine: absence of response. Aglutina with ristocetina. In cytometry, absence of Gp IIb-IIIa is observed. Which is the diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	109	answer	0	Thrombosis of Glanzmann.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	109	answer	1	Von Willebrand disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	109	answer	2	Primary immune thrombocytopenia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	109	answer	3	Bernard-Soulier syndrome.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	110	question	-	A 23-year-old girl is referred by her obstetrician for the study of thrombocytopenia. Her platelets in the first prenatal evaluation a month ago were 42,000 / uL. She is 16 weeks pregnant and does not report hemorrhagic manifestations. Physical examination is normal. Hemogram: leukocytes 8,500 / uL, Hb 12 g / dL, platelets 51,000 / uL. The revision of the blood smear reveals platelets in accumulations. What is the diagnostic suspicion?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	110	answer	0	Primary immune thrombocytopenia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	110	answer	1	Thrombocytopenia of pregnancy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	110	answer	2	Seudotrombocitopenia by EDTA.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	110	answer	3	Thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	111	question	-	With regard to the hematopoietic progenitor transplant, point out the FALSE statement:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	111	answer	0	In patients who lack an identical or unrelated HLA-identical donor, umbilical cord blood can be used as an alternative source.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	111	answer	1	In patients lacking a familiar or unrelated HLA-identical donor, progenitor cells from a haploidentical donor can be used.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	111	answer	2	In autologous transplantation the cells are cryopreserved and must be thawed prior to administration.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	111	answer	3	The graft effect against leukemia is greater in autologous than in allogeneic transplantation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	112	question	-	A 34-year-old man who consulted in the emergency department for dysuria and burning in the urethral meatus, with the presence of a thick and thick discharge that exits through the meatus for 3 days. Which of the following answers is FALSE?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	112	answer	0	A sample of the urethral exudate must be obtained to make the etiological diagnosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	112	answer	1	Empirical treatment will be performed with intramuscular ceftriaxone and azithromycin orally in single doses, pending microbiological results.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	112	answer	2	Antibiogram should be performed in cases in which N. gonorrhoeae is isolated.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	112	answer	3	At 2-3 weeks after the administration of the treatment, new urethral samples must be obtained to confirm the microbiological cure.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	113	question	-	A 65-year-old woman underwent haematopoietic precursor transplant 30 days ago and severe neutropenia. It begins with cough and expectoration hemoptica in addition to fever and dyspnea of ​​moderate efforts that does not improve despite five days of treatment with amoxicillin-clavulanate (875/125 mg / 8 h) and levofloxacin (500 mg / 12 h). Thoracic radiographs show multiple poorly defined pulmonary nodules, some of them cavitated. Among the following, what is the most likely suspected diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	113	answer	0	Septic embolisms.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	113	answer	1	Invasive pulmonary aspergillosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	113	answer	2	Staphylococcus aureus pneumonia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	113	answer	3	Systemic candidiasis
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	114	question	-	A 38-year-old man visited the emergency room due to fever above 39ºC and a deterioration in his level of consciousness after having made a trip to Equatorial Guinea without antimalarial prophylaxis. In the analytical highlights: creatinine of 3.4 mg / dL, AST 764 U / L, ALT 678 U / L. The laboratory reports the visualization in blood of a Plasmodium falciparum with a parasitemia level of 6%. What treatment would you establish at this time?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	114	answer	0	Mefloquine by mouth
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	114	answer	1	Intravenous artesunate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	114	answer	2	Doxycycline orally.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	114	answer	3	Quinine sulfate orally.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	115	question	-	An 85-year-old man with a peripheral venous catheter who, one week after being hospitalized due to a stroke, begins with shivering and fever. Blood cultures are performed and from microbiology it is reported that gram positive cocci are growing in clusters. Pending the antibiogram, what is the most appropriate antibiotic treatment?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	115	answer	0	Cefazolin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	115	answer	1	Cloxacillin
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	115	answer	2	Vancomycin
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	115	answer	3	Linezolid.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	116	question	-	Luis is a 25-year-old boy who suffered splenectomy after a bicycle accident 1 year ago. He has a dog that bit him 24 hours ago and a small wound on his right hand. Go to your health center (located 3 hours from the nearest hospital) for fever of 39 º C, pain in the wound and malaise. On examination PA 100/60 mm Hg, HR 110 beats per minute, slight inflammation in the wound without pus. Which of the following actions is more indicated at this time?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	116	answer	0	Send to the hospital to vaccinate for rabies and tetanus and keep under observation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	116	answer	1	Clean the wound and administer intramuscular nonspecific gammaglobulin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	116	answer	2	Give 400 mg of oral moxifloxacin and send to the hospital.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	116	answer	3	Give clindamycin 600 mg orally every 8 hours and observation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	117	question	-	A 38-year-old woman of veterinary profession, in charge of the surveillance of wild animals and helping with domestic livestock. It begins with a picture of high fever with chills, headache, myalgias and nonproductive cough that it interprets as a flu process. He comes because of chest pain. Chest radiography revealed bilateral pulmonary infiltrates in lower fields. A serological test is performed with elevation of antibody titers against antigens in phase II. Which of the following statements is true?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	117	answer	0	The form of transmission of this entity is by ticks.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	117	answer	1	Both doxycycline and hydroxychloroquine are effective in treating acute forms of this disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	117	answer	2	In its acute form it also presents, generally, elevation of antibodies against antigens in phase I.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	117	answer	3	Mortality in acute forms is almost non-existent.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	118	question	-	What is the current standard guideline in our setting for the treatment of pulmonary tuberculosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	118	answer	0	Isoniazide + rifampicin + pyrazinamide (6 months).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	118	answer	1	Isoniazide + rifampicin + pyrazinamide + ethambutol (2 months) followed by isoniazid + rifampicin (4 months).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	118	answer	2	Isoniazide + rifabutin + ethambutol (9 months).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	118	answer	3	Isoniazide + rifampicin + pyrazinamide (2 months) followed by isoniazid + rifampicin (4 months).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	119	question	-	A 45-year-old man consulted for productive cough, pleuritic pain on his right side and fever of 48 hours of evolution. A basal O2 saturation of 88% and rales on the right base were observed. The chest X-ray shows a right basal consolidation. Have a history of HIV infection well controlled with antiretrovirals (CD4 cells 550 cells / uL and undetectable HIV viral load). Which of the empirical antimicrobial treatments listed below seems more appropriate?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	119	answer	0	Ceftriaxone 2 g and azithromycin 500 mg every 24 hours.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	119	answer	1	Ceftriaxone 2 g, azithromycin 500 mg every 24 hours and trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole 5 mg / kg / 8 h (based on doses of trimethoprim).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	119	answer	2	Methyl-prednisolone 40 mg / day, ceftriaxone 2 g IV / 24 h and trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole 5 mg / kg / 8 h (based on dose of trimethoprim).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	119	answer	3	Meropenem 1 g / 8 h and vancomycin 1 g / 12 h.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	120	question	-	With regard to infection with the hepatitis C virus (HCV), point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	120	answer	0	In the world, the most frequent route of transmission of HCV is vertical.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	120	answer	1	If HCV is acquired in adulthood, it becomes chronic in 5-10% of cases.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	120	answer	2	The majority of patients with chronic HCV infection have positive HCV antibodies.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	120	answer	3	Acute HCV infection occurs with frank jaundice in more than 80% of cases.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	121	question	-	A 65-year-old woman who visited her dentist for pain in the right mandibular body and ulcerated lesion in the oral mucosa with exposure of bone over a rubbing area due to her dental prosthesis, which had lasted three months. Her background includes a vertebral fracture due to osteoporosis 5 years ago, smoker of a pack of cigarettes a day, type 2 diabetes for 15 years, polymyalgia rheumatica in oral steroid treatment (5 mg of prednisone daily for 5 years) and neoplasia of Right breast treated 5 years ago with surgery and local radiotherapy. The patient has been treated with denosumab for 5 years. What is the most likely clinical diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	121	answer	0	Mandibular bone lesion secondary to radiotherapy (osteoradionecrosis).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	121	answer	1	Mandibular vascular bone necrosis secondary to diabetic vasculopathy, smoking and osteoporosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	121	answer	2	Epidermoid verrucosa-ulcerated carcinoma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	121	answer	3	Mandibular osteonecrosis secondary to treatment with denosumab.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	122	question	-	In which of the following lesions of the jaws does the treatment require a partial or marginal resection, since simple enucleation or curettage of it is not enough to eradicate it?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	122	answer	0	Adenomatoid odontogenic tumor.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	122	answer	1	Odontogenic myxoma
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	122	answer	2	Osteoblastoma
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	122	answer	3	Eosinophilic granuloma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	123	question	-	What result would acupuncture offer with a 500 Hz tuning fork, in an idiopathic right ear deafness?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	123	answer	0	Rinne positive (+) of the right ear and Weber to the left ear.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	123	answer	1	Rinne negative (-) of the right ear and Weber towards the left ear.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	123	answer	2	Rinne positive (+) of the left ear and Weber to the right ear.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	123	answer	3	Rinne negative (-) of the left ear and Weber to the right ear.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	124	question	-	A 47-year-old man, with a history of a right parotid pleomorphic adenoma, treated with surgery (extrafacial parotidectomy) 6 months ago, who came to our clinic because he presented pain during the mastication with sweating and reddening of the skin of the preauricular region. What treatment would be the one of choice?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	124	answer	0	Total parotidectomy enlarged when suspicion of tumor recurrence.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	124	answer	1	Pregabalin
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	124	answer	2	Injection of intradermal botulinum toxin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	124	answer	3	Broad spectrum antibiotic therapy
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	125	question	-	Considering that the pathophysiology of benign paroxysmal positional vertigo is cupulolithiasis, what treatment would it indicate in a patient in whom the symptoms persist after two weeks?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	125	answer	0	Vestibular neuroleptic or antidopaminergic sedatives.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	125	answer	1	Corticosteroids
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	125	answer	2	Replacement maneuver of particles.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	125	answer	3	Neurectomy of the singular nerve.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	126	question	-	We will suspect acute renal failure of pre-renal origin in the presence of:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	126	answer	0	Hypotension, elevation of serum urea and creatinine levels, urine osmolarity less than 500 mOsm / kg, and fractional sodium excretion greater than 1%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	126	answer	1	Digestive intolerance, elevation of serum urea and creatinine levels, urine osmolarity greater than 500 mOsm / kg and fractional sodium excretion less than 1%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	126	answer	2	Previous intravenous administration of iodinated contrast, elevation of serum urea and creatinine levels, urine osmolarity less than 500 mOsm / kg and fractional sodium excretion greater than 1%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	126	answer	3	Previous administration of an aminoglycoside antibiotic, elevation of serum urea and creatinine levels and isostenuria.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	127	question	-	The most characteristic association of metabolic alterations that we can find in the presence of chronic renal failure in advanced stages is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	127	answer	0	Hyperkalemia, hypophosphoremia, hypercalcemia and metabolic acidosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	127	answer	1	Hypokalemia, hypophosphoremia, hypocalcemia and metabolic acidosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	127	answer	2	Hyperkalemia, hyperphosphatemia, hypocalcemia and metabolic acidosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	127	answer	3	Hyperkalemia, hyperphosphatemia, hypocalcemia and metabolic alkalosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	128	question	-	A 28-year-old man presented to the emergency department of the hospital due to gross hematuria. Which of the following alterations in urinalysis would support the diagnosis of glomerulonephritis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	128	answer	0	Dysmorphic red blood cells and / or blood cylinders.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	128	answer	1	Proteinuria of 1 g / day, with a negative result on a dipstick and with microalbuminuria greater than 300 mg / 24 hours.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	128	answer	2	Coexistence of hematuria with pyuria without bacteriuria.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	128	answer	3	Clots in the urine with the naked eye.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	129	question	-	Man of 25 years with no known background of interest. It takes 2 months with foamy and loaded urine, without other symptoms. Physical exploration without findings. Elemental urine: pH 5; glucose -; hemoglobin ++; proteins ++; leukocyte esterase -; proteinuria 1.5 g / 24 hours; Urinary Na 60 mEq / L; Urinary K 30 mEq / L; Urinary Cl 100 mEq / L. Blood biochemistry: creatinine 1.6 mg / dL; urea 80 mg / dL; Na 140 mEq / L; K 3.8 mEq / L. Immunological study: negative antiDNA; ANCA negative; antiMBG negative; negative rheumatoid factor; C3 20 mg / dL (normal 60-120); C4 10 mg / dL (normal 20-40). Renal biopsy is performed. Which of these diagnoses do you think is most likely to be found in the biopsy?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	129	answer	0	Membranous glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	129	answer	1	Glomerulonephritis of minimal changes.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	129	answer	2	IgA mesangial glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	129	answer	3	Membranoproliferative glomerulonephritis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	130	question	-	Which of the following is the most common form of presentation of lithium nephropathy?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	130	answer	0	Glomerulosclerosis
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	130	answer	1	Nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	130	answer	2	Chronic tubulo-interstitial nephropathy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	130	answer	3	Acute interstitial nephritis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	131	question	-	A 55-year-old man who underwent a kidney transplant 24 hours ago. It begins with hematuria and subsequently with a sudden cessation of diuresis. What imaging test is indicated to clarify the diagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	131	answer	0	Isotopic renogram.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	131	answer	1	Ultrasound-Doppler
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	131	answer	2	Intravenous urography.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	131	answer	3	Magnetic resonance.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	132	question	-	A 55-year-old diabetic man with good glycemic control who came for erectile dysfunction of 3 years of evolution, of slow onset. In the treatment of erectile dysfunction, etiological causes should be initially treated, lifestyles should be modified that favor erectile dysfunction and identify the needs and expectations of the patient and his partner. What should be the complementary treatment to consider?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	132	answer	0	Phosphodiesterase inhibitors 5.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	132	answer	1	Vacuum devices.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	132	answer	2	Alprostadil topical.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	132	answer	3	Intracavernous injections
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	133	question	-	A 63-year-old man with no family history of prostatic carcinoma consulted for mild obstructive voiding symptoms. It provides a determination of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) less than 1 ng / mL. In rectal examination, a hardened and fixed area of ​​half a centimeter is seen in a prostatic lobe. In this case, the correct attitude is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	133	answer	0	Repeat the determination of PSA in three months.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	133	answer	1	Indicate a transrectal prostate biopsy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	133	answer	2	Treat with an alpha blocking to improve the obstructive symptomatology and repeat the PSA annually.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	133	answer	3	Schedule a retropubic prostatic resection.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	134	question	-	Two-year-old girl diagnosed with grade II unilateral vesicoureteral reflux (reflux to the ureter, pelvis and calyces without dilation of the urinary tract and normal papillary morphology). What is the most appropriate treatment at the beginning of this pathology?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	134	answer	0	Endoscopic injection of dextranomer in the intramural ureteral tract.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	134	answer	1	Ureteral reimplantation by open route.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	134	answer	2	Laparoscopic ureteral reimplantation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	134	answer	3	Conservative treatment by observation and antibiotic / antiseptic prophylaxis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	135	question	-	A 35-year-old man visited the emergency room for a 48-hour history of fever of 39ºC, shivering, poor general condition, frequency, dysuria, bladder tenesmus and perianal pain. In the analytical sample, it showed creatinine values ​​of 0.9 mg / dL, procalcitonin of 1.5 ng / mL, leukocytes of 20,000 / uL and PSA of 45 ng / mL. What is the attitude to follow in this patient?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	135	answer	0	Serotherapy, antipyretics, urine culture, antibiotherapy and thoracoabdominal CT.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	135	answer	1	Serotherapy, antipyretics and antibiotic therapy prior to prostate biopsy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	135	answer	2	Sueroterapia, antitérmicos and antibioterapia during three weeks and to repeat levels of PSA in three months.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	135	answer	3	Sueroterapia, antitérmicos and antibioterapia. Request levels of prostatic acid phosphatase.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	136	question	-	A woman goes to the emergency room three days after being subjected to extracorporeal shock wave lithotripsy on a calculation of 2.1 cm maximum diameter located in the left kidney. He presented poor general condition, pain in the left renal fossa, nausea and fever of 39.2ºC. Simple Rx is performed in which several small calculi are seen in the area of ​​the left distal ureter. The radiologist informs us that on ultrasound he observes the existence of left pyelocalicial grade II dilatation. The next step should be:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	136	answer	0	Urinary ureteroscopy given the existence of obstructive uropathy of lithiasic cause.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	136	answer	1	Income with intravenous hydration, as well as antibiotic treatment, given the suspicion of urinary infection.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	136	answer	2	Urgent urinary diversion (ureteral catheterization or percutaneous nephrostomy) given the suspicion of complicated obstructive uropathy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	136	answer	3	New session of extracorporeal shock wave lithotripsy, previous symptomatic treatment of the patient with anti-inflammatory, antibiotic treatment and intravenous hydration.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	137	question	-	A 29-year-old woman with persistent moderate asthma well controlled with fluticasone / salmeterol every 12 hours and terbutaline on demand discovers that she is 5 weeks pregnant. Which attitude is the most correct?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	137	answer	0	Substitute fluticasone / salmeterol for budesonide / formoterol.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	137	answer	1	Suspend fluticasone / salmeterol and keep only salbutamol on demand.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	137	answer	2	Suspend fluticasone / salmeterol and try maintenance only with montelukast.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	137	answer	3	Remove fluticasone / salmeterol and try maintenance only with budesonide at medium doses.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	138	question	-	A 23-year-old woman is brought to the emergency room by the emergency service after a car accident with the result of 2 deaths and she is the only survivor. Upon arrival at our center, the patient is under orotracheal intubation and hemodynamically stable. The physical examination reveals multiple blunt injuries throughout the body, bleeding on the sheet on the scalp, and slight generalized bilateral hypophonosis. Normal cardiac auscultation. Abdomen: soft and depressible without signs of peritonism. Rest of physical exploration by normal appliances. It was decided to perform cranio-cervico-thoracic-abdominal-pelvic CT. What radiological finding would NOT be compatible with a ruptured aorta?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	138	answer	0	Left pleural effusion.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	138	answer	1	Mediastinal emphysema
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	138	answer	2	Pericardial effusion
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	138	answer	3	Mediastinal broadening.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	139	question	-	Within the definition of acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	139	answer	0	It is due to an alteration of the pulmonary capillary membrane.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	139	answer	1	Radiologically, bilateral opacities not explained by pleural effusion, atelectasis or pulmonary nodules are observed.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	139	answer	2	It is necessary that there is an occlusion pressure of the pulmonary artery (POAP)> 18 mmHg.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	139	answer	3	The quotient Pa02 / FiO2 must be less than or equal to 200 mmHg.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	140	question	-	The study of the multifunctional severity of COPD is performed with the BODEX and BODE indices, which have some common criteria. Which of the following criteria is exclusively part of one of the two indexes?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	140	answer	0	Dyspnea assessment (MRC).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	140	answer	1	Distance traveled (meters).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	140	answer	2	Body mass index (BMI).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	140	answer	3	Forced vital capacity (FVC).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	141	question	-	He receives a 65-year-old man, former smoker with an accumulated consumption of 50 packs / year and diagnosed with emphysema-like COPD. He cites cough with little expectoration and dyspnea of ​​moderate efforts. Request respiratory functional tests. Of the following results, which one is LESS likely?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	141	answer	0	FEV1 (expiratory flow in the first second) less than 80%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	141	answer	1	DLCO (diffusion capacity) normal.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	141	answer	2	FEV1 / FVC ratio less than 70%.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	141	answer	3	TLC (total lung capacity) increased.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	142	question	-	A 47-year-old man, with a history of depressive syndrome, is seen in the emergency room after having found him in his unconscious home. In arterial blood gases, it stands out: pH 6.94; HCO3 5 mEq / L; PaCO2 17 mmHg. The anion gap or anion gap is 35 (normal value 12 ± 2). The glycemia and creatinine were normal and the ketone bodies negative. The calculated osmolarity revealed a value of 295 mOsm / kg, compared to an osmolarity measured directly of 325 mOsm / kg. Point out the correct statement:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	142	answer	0	The patient presents a mixed acidosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	142	answer	1	The possibility of methanol poisoning should be ruled out.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	142	answer	2	It is a metabolic acidosis due to loss of bicarbonate. We must rule out diarrhea or kidney losses.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	142	answer	3	Given the decrease in bicarbonate, its immediate replacement is essential in order to achieve, in the first hour, its normal plasma values.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	143	question	-	A 51-year-old woman reports dyspnea from moderate efforts of several months of evolution. He does not have a history of interest and the elementary analysis (blood count and basic biochemistry) is normal. In the respiratory functional tests, a FEV1 / FVC ratio greater than 0.7 and a FVC and a TLC of 85% and 83% were observed in relation to their theoretical values, respectively. The DLCO is 40%. Given these data, I would think about:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	143	answer	0	Disorder of the thoracic or neuromuscular cage.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	143	answer	1	Emphysema.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	143	answer	2	Vascular lung disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	143	answer	3	Asthma.
