Cuaderno_2017_1_M	164	question	-	An 80-year-old man with rheumatoid arthritis for 10 years and high blood pressure. He has been treated with paracetamol, tramadol and indapamide for years and in the last 3 months also with prednisone 7.5 mg daily and etanercept, with good results. She consulted because for 2 weeks she has invalidating pain of the left hip without fever. The analyzes show 14,000 leukocytes / uL, hemoglobin 10 g / dL, PCR 50 mg / L, creatinine 1.2 mg / dL. Pelvic radiography is normal. Indicate the CORRECT attitude:
