Cuaderno_2017_1_M	177	question	-	Triage is a method of classifying patients who, following a color scale, allows us to establish priorities when assisting a patient. Its use is extended in the hospital emergency but it is also used in out-of-hospital medicine in situations of disasters or accidents with multiple victims. Imagine that you are in a mobile ICU as the first intervening resource in one of these situations. What would you do to identify the milder or green patients?
