Cuaderno_2017_1_M	184	question	-	A 65-year-old woman with no personal history of interest, operated on for sigmoid adenocarcinoma that infiltrates the serosa (T4) with involvement of 2 lymph nodes of 35 isolates (N1). In the extension study, no distant metastasis (M0) is evident. What is the next step to make?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	184	answer	0	Determine mutation of KRAS and NRAS to be able to administer an anti-EFGR in case of not being mutated.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	184	answer	1	Associate treatment with chemotherapy bevacizumab if mutated.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	184	answer	2	Administer a combination of chemotherapy with fluorouracil and oxaliplatin.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	184	answer	3	Perform treatment with radiotherapy by having lymph node involvement.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	185	question	-	In relation to the presence of mutations in EFGR in patients with non-small cell lung cancer, which of the following statements is FALSE?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	185	answer	0	They are especially frequent in Caucasian patients and exceptional in Asian population.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	185	answer	1	They are located mainly in exons 19 and 21 of the gene.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	185	answer	2	They are more frequent in adenocarcinomas, in non-smokers and in females.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	185	answer	3	In patients with advanced stages, the use of tyrosine kinase inhibitors (gefitinib or erlotinib) has been shown to be superior to chemotherapy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	186	question	-	All of the following drugs have been shown to be effective in the treatment of hormone-resistant prostate cancer, EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	186	answer	0	Docetaxel
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	186	answer	1	Abiraterone
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	186	answer	2	Enzalutamide
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	186	answer	3	Nivolumab.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	187	question	-	In relation to the agony, point out the INCORRECT response:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	187	answer	0	The ideal drug for sedation is midazolam.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	187	answer	1	Morphine is contraindicated in the treatment of dyspnea because it produces respiratory depression.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	187	answer	2	The standard treatment for premortem rales is the administration of anticholinergics.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	187	answer	3	In the agitation the treatment is haloperidol.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	188	question	-	A 45-year-old woman diagnosed with stage IV breast cancer with multiple bone metastases, undergoing hormonal treatment and intravenous bisphosphonates. He comes to his office referring to intense basal bone pain (EVA = 7), in several locations, without associated neurological symptoms and pain exacerbations (EVA = 9) several times a day that force him to remain at rest. On treatment with ibuprofen (600 mg every 8 hours) and tramadol (150 mg daily). What treatment would you consider more appropriate in this patient to improve pain control?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	188	answer	0	Suspend ibuprofen and tramadol and start a major opioid such as morphine or oxycodone.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	188	answer	1	Stop tramadol, maintain ibuprofen and start a major opioid such as morphine or oxycodone.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	188	answer	2	Suspend ibuprofen and tramadol and start a major opioid such as morphine or oxycodone, and at the same time treatment for breakthrough pain with sublingual fentanyl.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	188	answer	3	Suspend tramadol, maintain ibuprofen and initiate a major opioid such as morphine or oxycodone, and at the same time treatment for breakthrough pain with sublingual fentanyl.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	189	question	-	He goes to the home of an oncological patient who lately does not have pain well controlled. In the physical examination it seems that there is no evidence of tumor progression, it does not reveal any data of interest of the previously known. In the anamnesis the main caregiver states that the patient has pain at 8 hours after receiving the basal dose of morphine every 12 hours. This clinical situation is called:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	189	answer	0	Tolerance.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	189	answer	1	Hyperalgesia
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	189	answer	2	Dependence.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	189	answer	3	Inefficiency.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	190	question	-	Woman with advanced neurodegenerative disease. He arrives at the emergency room of the hospital with a respiratory infection, which has triggered acute global respiratory failure. The patient has registered an advance directive. In those previous instructions, she says "she does not want to be subjected to mechanical ventilation." He also stated that he appointed his friend Pedro as his representative. The doctor who assesses the patient in the emergency department and has read the advance directive asks Pedro for his doubts about it, since the picture is acute and potentially reversible after treatment that includes mechanical ventilation, and it seems that the document is written thinking about a chronic situation, not the current one. You consider it TRUE that:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	190	answer	0	The representative can change the patient's advance directive, in their best interest.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	190	answer	1	The doctor, being an emergency situation, is not obliged to follow the advance directive or consult with the representative.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	190	answer	2	The representative can not change the advance directive. Its purpose is to guarantee respect for the patient's values ​​and compliance with the instruction.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	190	answer	3	The immediate family members present can make a substitution decision in their best interest, and the opinion of the representative does not matter.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	191	question	-	Overdiagnosis is the phenomenon that occurs when people are diagnosed with diseases that would never cause them symptoms or shorten their lives, but instead the alarm generated by the finding may cause undesirable consequences. Which of the following actions is considered to cause overdiagnosis?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	191	answer	0	The screening of colon cancer directed to the population segment of 50-69 years through the fecal occult blood test.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	191	answer	1	Screening for prostate cancer in healthy men using the PSA test.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	191	answer	2	Start a diagnostic study for people who come to the clinic for presenting persistent microhematuria.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	191	answer	3	Start a diagnostic study for people who come to the clinic for chronic cough.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	192	question	-	Why is it necessary to obtain informed consent of diagnostic and therapeutic procedures?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	192	answer	0	It is a legal requirement that exempts the doctor from any liability.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	192	answer	1	It involves a shared decision making after informing the patient of the procedure.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	192	answer	2	It gives the doctor freedom to perform new procedures.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	192	answer	3	It allows to determine if the patient is capable of making decisions.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	193	question	-	Indicate the variable on which, fundamentally, the decision on surgical margins in the treatment of a cutaneous melanoma case will depend:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	193	answer	0	Larger diameter of the lesion, in millimeters.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	193	answer	1	Maximum thickness of the lesion, in millimeters (Breslow index).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	193	answer	2	Presence of ulceration in the lesion.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	193	answer	3	Mitosis per square millimeter (mitotic index).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	194	question	-	A 74-year-old man came to his office for presenting constitutional syndrome with a loss of 5 kilos in the last month, along with asthenia. He reports that in the last three weeks, in addition, he has observed the appearance of red lesions on legs that sometimes drain an oily material, also associated with abdominal and rib pain, as well as pain and flushing of the ankles and knees. You decide to perform a biopsy and note that "phantom cells" appear in the subcutaneous tissue. The clinical manifestations of the patient and this finding of the skin biopsy will lead him to perform one of the following tests to make the definitive diagnosis:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	194	answer	0	Gastrointestinal endoscopy: gastric adenocarcinoma.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	194	answer	1	Abdominal CT scan: pancreatic cancer.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	194	answer	2	Thoracic CT: lymph node sarcoidosis (Löfgren's syndrome).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	194	answer	3	Cultivation of cutaneous nodules: cutaneous tuberculosis (lupus vulgaris).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	195	question	-	If there is a direct trauma to the orbital region, point out the correct answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	195	answer	0	Trapping of the optic nerve is common, clinically causing diplopia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	195	answer	1	There may be a burst of the orbital floor with clinical diplopia and enophthalmos.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	195	answer	2	Frequently, a Le Fort-I type maxillofacial fracture occurs.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	195	answer	3	There is a very high risk of eyeball burst.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	196	question	-	67-year-old man, diabetic and asthmatic, with primary open-angle glaucoma in both eyes. He has an eye pressure of 34 mmHg in his right eye and 31 mmHg in his left eye. Which of the following pharmacological groups is the most indicated as the first choice as a hypotensive treatment?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	196	answer	0	Inhibitors of carbonic anhydrase.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	196	answer	1	Beta-blockers.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	196	answer	2	Alpha-2 agonists.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	196	answer	3	Derivatives of prostaglandins.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	197	question	-	A 26-year-old woman with schizophrenia who goes to the mental health clinic after a recent hospitalization for a psychotic decompensation. After being admitted 22 days is discharged the week prior to the current review. The family reports that they find her very uneasy and with great psychomotor restlessness. On examination, it is evident that she can not remain seated and is continuously circling the consultation without a specific purpose. The positive psychotic symptoms that led to their admission are not observed, since they adjusted their treatment with 15 mg of haloperidol daily in the hospital. The diagnosis of the situation presented by the patient is:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	197	answer	0	Generalized anxiety disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	197	answer	1	Anxiety secondary to psychotic decompensation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	197	answer	2	Acatisia
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	197	answer	3	Attention deficit disorder and hyperactivity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	198	question	-	For the treatment of acute mania, the following antipsychotics are approved by the FDA, EXCEPT:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	198	answer	0	Olanzapine.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	198	answer	1	Clozapine
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	198	answer	2	Aripiprazole
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	198	answer	3	Ziprasidone.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	199	question	-	Woman of 55 years, married and with two children of 25 and 20 years of age. Go to the mental health clinic for problems in the family environment. The patient reports being ill, sad and worried about "the troubles that my husband gives me". He has seen him embraced by another woman and affirms that "he is against her and that he deceives her because he cares too much for his children". Both the husband and the children deny that information given by the patient. With no outstanding psychiatric medical history, he presents a psychopathological exploration of lucidity with a good level of awareness and orientation in the 3 spheres. Presents discreet hypothymia of months of evolution. Alteration of the content of thought in the form of delusional ideas of a celotypical nature and of damage with self-referential phenomena. There is no alteration of the sensoperceptive sphere. It does not present autolytic ideation. It maintains an adequate cognitive rhythm and preserves the biological rhythms of sleep and appetite. What is the diagnosis that best fits the clinical picture presented by the patient?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	199	answer	0	Paranoid schizophrenia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	199	answer	1	Major depressive disorder with psychotic characteristics.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	199	answer	2	Paranoid personality disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	199	answer	3	Delirious disorder
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	200	question	-	What is the diagnostic orientation to a 35-year-old man with no medical history who comes to the clinic explaining insurmountable fears to enter crowded places after experiencing a month ago, when entering a shopping center, an acute episode of anxiety with somatic symptoms ( tachycardia, sweats, dyspnea ..)?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	200	answer	0	Anticipatory stress disorder
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	200	answer	1	Avoidance drive phobia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	200	answer	2	Obsessive disorder
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	200	answer	3	Anguish disorder with agoraphobia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	201	question	-	A 22-year-old medical student, with a family history in the same sense of her discomfort, consults for fear, from childhood, to observing scenes that contain blood or physical damage, which causes fainting with loss of consciousness and falling soil, with full recovery in a few minutes. What are the correct diagnostic orientation and therapeutic attitude?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	201	answer	0	He suffers from a conversion disorder and requires analytic psychotherapy.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	201	answer	1	He suffers from agoraphobia and requires treatment with monoamine oxidase inhibitors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	201	answer	2	He suffers from a simple phobia and requires cognitive-behavioral treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	201	answer	3	He suffers from a specific phobia and does not require treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	202	question	-	Some parents come to consultation worried about the situation of their son who is going to repeat 4th of Compulsory Primary Education (EPO). At school they complain about their behavior, but they have not made any intervention. The parents feel guilty because they have delayed the request for help because of the sister's health problems. Two years ago, she was diagnosed with leukemia and focused on her treatment, which has evolved positively. They state that their son has problems with classmates because of his character, he is very restless and distracted, he does not accept losing and he is upset when he does not win. She always had the problems, but they increase at the beginning of EPO, and the teacher has always told them that she was lazy but that she was capable, taking away her importance. How would you orient this case?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	202	answer	0	He would diagnose attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) and treat him with methylphenidate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	202	answer	1	I would analyze the family dynamics to work on the problems derived from the illness in the sister and what this had meant in the behavior of the child.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	202	answer	2	Intervened with the school to provide information on possible school bullying.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	202	answer	3	I would have an interview with the child and request school information.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	203	question	-	Monica is a twenty-year-old girl who is taken to the emergency room by her parents because they do not know what to do with her. For about three years she has been obsessed with her silhouette and seems to judge everything based on the physical aspect, underestimating other personal qualities that she has and that everyone recognizes. Since about five months ago he also has episodes that make him feel very bad and that he describes as uncontrollable, consisting in the intake of enormous quantities of food in a very short time. This has been happening to her more and more frequently, occurring between two and three times a week for the last 3 months. Account for example that last night ate four packets of cookies in an hour and a half after what, as usual usually do, unable to withstand the feeling of guilt has caused vomiting, thus ejecting most of what was ingested. In this patient it would be much more IMPROBABLE to find one of the following characteristics, point it out:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	203	answer	0	Metabolic acidosis with hyperchloremia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	203	answer	1	Fasting behaviors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	203	answer	2	History of impulsive behaviors such as alcohol consumption or self-harm behaviors of low lethality.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	203	answer	3	Elevated serum amylase levels.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	204	question	-	Point out the correct answer about clinical trials with medicines in children:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	204	answer	0	They are legally possible and ethically acceptable, but the researcher must respect the explicit desire of the child to refuse to participate in the trial, provided that the latter is able to form an opinion.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	204	answer	1	They are legally possible and ethically acceptable and only require the authorization of the parents or legal guardians.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	204	answer	2	They are legally possible and ethically acceptable, as long as the child is 12 years of age or older.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	204	answer	3	They are legally possible but they are not ethical, since children do not have the capacity to consent to research.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	205	question	-	One clinical trial showed no significant difference between the new drug thromboporix and placebo in the incidence of myocardial infarction (7% versus 5%, p = 0.68) in the total study population, but it did show that thromboporix reduced the risk of infarction in one of the 20 subgroups analyzed, specifically in those older than 55 years (3% versus 8%, p = 0.048). Point out the TRUE:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	205	answer	0	The significant result in the subgroup reasonably rules out a type I error.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	205	answer	1	It can be useful to propose new hypotheses, which should be checked in new tests designed for this purpose.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	205	answer	2	The type II error can be the cause of statistical significance in said subgroup.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	205	answer	3	The result obtained in the subgroup is an example of the so-called Brawnwald paradox.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	206	question	-	In relation to phase III clinical trials conducted in oncology, point out the true answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	206	answer	0	The response rate is usually used as the main variable, since it is considered clinically relevant under any circumstance.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	206	answer	1	In frequent tumors, such as colon cancer, phase III clinical trials are usually uncontrolled clinical trials.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	206	answer	2	When the existence of important prognostic factors of the type of cancer under study is known, it is advisable to stratify the randomization to ensure an equitable distribution of these factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	206	answer	3	Very strict inclusion criteria that exclude certain types of patients (for example elderly patients) should be used, as this will make the results more general.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	207	question	-	In 2000, Swedish researchers conducted a study to see if cannabis use increased the risk of schizophrenia. To this end, they identified 50,087 men who were part of the compulsory military recruitment between 1969 and 1970. As part of the recruitment process, they were interviewed where, in a non-anonymous way, they indicated the use of cannabis. This group was followed from 1970 to 1996 through the hospital records to find out how many of them had a diagnosis of schizophrenia registered during that period. For the analysis, they divided the subjects into two groups: those who indicated that they had used cannabis 2 or more times and those who used cannabis less than 2 times and calculated the frequency of schizophrenia in each of them. What kind of epidemiological study is it about?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	207	answer	0	Cohort study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	207	answer	1	Cases and controls study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	207	answer	2	Retrospective cross section study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	207	answer	3	Non-randomized clinical trial.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	208	question	-	In an epidemiological cohort study, what do we mean by exposed patients?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	208	answer	0	Patients who have the risk factor of the disease or health problem we want to study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	208	answer	1	Patients who agree to participate in the study after giving their informed consent.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	208	answer	2	Subjects who do not develop the disease or health problem under study during follow-up.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	208	answer	3	Patients who have the disease or health problem we want to study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	209	question	-	The dermatology department of a hospital has registered all the cases diagnosed of toxic epidermal necrolysis in the center during the last twenty years. It is found that 20% of these patients had been exposed to carbamazepine in the 6 weeks prior to diagnosis, while 10% had been exposed to phenytoin. Which of the following corresponds to the design of this study?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	209	answer	0	An ecological study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	209	answer	1	A case-control study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	209	answer	2	A prevalence study.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	209	answer	3	A descriptive study
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	210	question	-	The survival of patients infected with the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is being evaluated depending on the time of acquisition of the infection. Which of the following tests is the most appropriate for the proposed objective?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	210	answer	0	Student's t test.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	210	answer	1	Calculation of the linear regression.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	210	answer	2	Kaplan-Meier Estimator.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	210	answer	3	Calculation of the logistic regression.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	211	question	-	With which of the following measures can we reduce the amplitude of a confidence interval?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	211	answer	0	Increasing the sample size or decreasing the degree of confidence.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	211	answer	1	Decreasing the sample size or decreasing the degree of confidence.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	211	answer	2	Increasing the sample size or decreasing the statistical power.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	211	answer	3	Increasing the sample size or increasing the degree of confidence.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	212	question	-	Regarding the sensitivity analyzes in pharmacoeconomic evaluations, indicate the FALSE answer:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	212	answer	0	It is an analysis of uncertainty.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	212	answer	1	They can be multivariate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	212	answer	2	Endpoint sensitivity analysis is univariate.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	212	answer	3	Monte Carlo simulation is a type of probabilistic sensitivity analysis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	213	question	-	Health-related quality of life (HRQoL) is evaluated by:
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	213	answer	0	Standardized questionnaires with proven metric properties.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	213	answer	1	Simple chest x-ray and global blood and urine analysis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	213	answer	2	Minimum basic data set (CMBD).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	213	answer	3	Screening tests of high sensitivity and specificity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	214	question	-	What are the characteristics of the Spanish health system?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	214	answer	0	Public financing, universal coverage, comprehensive healthcare, equity based on accessibility and territorial decentralization.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	214	answer	1	Public financing, universal coverage, comprehensive healthcare, efficiency and territorial centralization.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	214	answer	2	Mixed financing (public and private), mixed management (public and private) and territorial centralization.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	214	answer	3	Financing for social security contributions, mixed management (public and private) and territorial decentralization.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	215	question	-	Cochrane, an independent organization whose purpose is to provide the best available evidence, usually bases its recommendations on systematic reviews. What do you think this methodology is about?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	215	answer	0	From a study with random distribution of participants between the intervention group and the control group.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	215	answer	1	Of a statistical technique that allows to combine the findings of several independent studies with each other.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	215	answer	2	From a structured search based on a well-defined question and an explicit protocol.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	215	answer	3	From a scientific consensus technique valid for independent collaboration groups.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	216	question	-	What is the recommended anatomical site for administration of a vaccine intramuscularly in infants less than 12 months of age?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	216	answer	0	Anterior rectus of the abdomen.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	216	answer	1	Deltoid.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	216	answer	2	External anterolateral aspect of the thigh (vastus lateralis muscle).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	216	answer	3	Dorso-gluteal region (upper external quadrant of the gluteus maximus).
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	217	question	-	Which of the following vaccines is recommended for administration at 12 months with a booster dose at 3-4 years?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	217	answer	0	Hepatitis B.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	217	answer	1	Viral triple.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	217	answer	2	Chickenpox.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	217	answer	3	Vaccine against pneumococcus.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	218	question	-	Which of the following characteristics is LESS important in a population screening (or early detection) program?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	218	answer	0	That the diagnostic test for early detection is very specific.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	218	answer	1	That the early identification of the disorder allows to apply interventions that improve its prognosis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	218	answer	2	That the early detection process is economically profitable.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	218	answer	3	That the program be applied to a common disorder with a large burden of morbidity.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	219	question	-	A 35-year-old Bolivian woman, 3 months pregnant, who has been living in Spain for 10 years with her partner, who is Spanish and has never traveled to Latin America. The woman has two other children with her partner, born in Spain and a brother who lives in Bolivia and another in Spain. During pregnancy, he was diagnosed with Trypanosoma cruzi infection. Which of the following actions to perform on the disease is INCORRECT?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	219	answer	0	Recommend that your children have T. cruzi serology because of the risk of transplacental transmission.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	219	answer	1	Inform the patient of the risk of T. cruzi transmission and of the attitude that will be taken during pregnancy, delivery and postpartum.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	219	answer	2	Recommend that your husband get the serology of T. cruzi because of the risk of transmitting the disease through sexual contact.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	219	answer	3	Recommend that your brothers get serology of T. cruzi for the risk of vector transmission.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	220	question	-	Which of the following characteristics is attributable to the case-control studies?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	220	answer	0	They allow to know the risk associated with exposure to several factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	220	answer	1	It includes a group exposed to one factor and another group not exposed.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	220	answer	2	They are very efficient when the prevalence of exposure to the factor is very low.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	220	answer	3	They are randomized studies.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	221	question	-	When the protocol of a research project is elaborated, which of the following aspects should be undertaken in the first place?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	221	answer	0	Define the objectives.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	221	answer	1	Justify the problem.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	221	answer	2	Establish the reference population.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	221	answer	3	Define the hypothesis.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	222	question	-	A 35-year-old man went to the emergency department with intense perianal pain and fever of 38ºC, which lasted two days. On examination, he presented a painful mass in the left ischio-rectal fossa. What is the most appropriate attitude?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	222	answer	0	Broad spectrum antibiotics and control evolution.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	222	answer	1	Perform echoendoscopy and ultrasound-guided FNA.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	222	answer	2	Drainage under regional anesthesia.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	222	answer	3	Perform a CT scan and thus assess the approach to correct treatment.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	223	question	-	In secondary prevention, after an acute myocardial infarction, which of the following measures has NOT shown a beneficial effect?
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	223	answer	0	Physical exercise.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	223	answer	1	Calcium antagonists.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	223	answer	2	Acetylsalicylic acid.
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	223	answer	3	Beta-blockers
Cuaderno_2017_1_M	224	question	-	In the design of clinical trials, randomization allows to reduce the risk of the following causes of bias, EXCEPT one:
