Cuaderno_2017_1_P	31	question	-	What characterizes the Münchausen syndrome ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	31	answer	0	Tendency to urinary infections that the patient will try to explain due to a lack of natural regulation of their body temperature.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	31	answer	1	The use by patients of a florid and very technical terminology in the description of their physical symptoms when they are sick.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	31	answer	2	The pretense of a nonexistent disease, the wandering behavior from hospital to hospital and the pathological tendency to lie.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	31	answer	3	Continuous body check behaviors (such as checking the body for suspicious lumps, taking a fever continuously, purging several times a week, and following a strict diet) for fear of having cancer.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	32	question	-	The presence of symptoms or deficits that affect the voluntary or sensory motor functioning, which suggests the existence of a medical, neurological or other disease, for which no clinical evidence is found to corroborate it, is one of the characteristics of the:
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	32	answer	0	Undifferentiated somatoform disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	32	answer	1	Somatization disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	32	answer	2	Conversion disorder
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	32	answer	3	Pain disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	33	question	-	What is the difference between factitious and simulation disorders ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	33	answer	0	That the patient with factitious disorder obtains an internal gain of the symptoms, while in the simulation one the gain is external.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	33	answer	1	The difference lies in the diseases and disorders caused by the persistent symptoms: physical disorders in factitious disorder and various mental disorders in the simulation.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	33	answer	2	That the simulation provides the patient with more psychological benefits, proper to the role of the patient.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	33	answer	3	That in factitious disorder the person is aware of the simulation of his illness, while in the simulation disorder the person really believes that he has a specific disease.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	34	question	-	In what type of dissociative disorder does the patient feel distanced as if he were an external observer of his body or mental processes ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	34	answer	0	The dissociative escape
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	34	answer	1	The conversion disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	34	answer	2	The depersonalization disorder.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	34	answer	3	Hysterical psychosis
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	35	question	-	What is the essential characteristic of dissociative disorders ?:
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	35	answer	0	A disturbance in the integration of the functions of consciousness, memory, identity and perception.
