Cuaderno_2017_1_P	100	answer	2	It is easy to get consensus with the dialogue.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	100	answer	3	There is coherence between what a person says and what they think.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	101	question	-	The so-called "actor-observer effect" consists of:
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	101	answer	0	Attribute our behaviors to external factors and the behaviors of others to internal factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	101	answer	1	Attribute our behaviors to internal factors and the behaviors of others to external factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	101	answer	2	Attributing both our behaviors and the behaviors of others to internal factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	101	answer	3	Attribute both our behaviors and the behaviors of others to external factors.
Cuaderno_2017_1_P	102	question	-	The so-called "illusory correlation" produces:
